ch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084612 - fixed localized string issues with monitor errors r=yjamora\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336163\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/tasks.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_tasks_actors.js"], "git_node": "bca64cd126086d2ebc3ce407b41af7c939a869cb", "git_parents": ["02225661150a761be04227ef9d311d4bc6fc506b"], "node": "9b1c1f3b24ee295a01b5a20e3b4a8fe60aaa85eb", "parents": ["aea5270f771cbb6b8def2d939beaf4029ccc278c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@ritter.vg\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1700396: Bump updatebot to get some QOL fixes r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335338\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/updatebot/updatebot-version.sh"], "git_node": "7d1cb29f2c4847d877f9448c2feb7577d6f30bee", "git_parents": ["bca64cd126086d2ebc3ce407b41af7c939a869cb"], "node": "d9749ef854b21fe751545e74c3106bd2b03aea0e", "parents": ["9b1c1f3b24ee295a01b5a20e3b4a8fe60aaa85eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrej Glavic \u003caglavic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083864 - Remove the AWSY tp5 test. r=perftest-reviewers,mozperftest-reviewers,mccr8,kshampur\n\nThe tp5 task never runs on any branch and is no longer maintained.\nRemoving it also removes the tp5n pageset download that every AWSY task\ndid in the populate-webroot step, even though only tp5 used it. tp6\npasses the web root to mitmproxy, which creates the directory itself.\n\nmach awsy-test now defaults to the tp6 or base prefs, matching CI,\ninstead of the tp5 prefs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335299\n", "files": ["docs/performance/memory/awsy.md", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/perfdocs/framework_gatherers.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/test_perfdocs_framework_gatherers.py", "taskcluster/kinds/test/awsy.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/test-sets.yml", "testing/awsy/awsy/__init__.py", "testing/awsy/awsy/test_memory_usage.py", "testing/awsy/awsy/webservers.py", "testing/awsy/conf/prefs.json", "testing/awsy/conf/testvars.json", "testing/awsy/mach_commands.py", "testing/awsy/perfdocs/config.yaml", "testing/awsy/perfdocs/index.md", "testing/awsy/tp5n-pageset.manifest", "testing/mozharness/configs/awsy/linux_config.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/awsy/macosx_config.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/awsy/taskcluster_windows_config.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/awsy_script.py", "testing/perfdocs/generated/awsy.md"], "git_node": "53b621c35f69e056d9e4018b419648a60e68fbeb", "git_parents": ["7d1cb29f2c4847d877f9448c2feb7577d6f30bee"], "node": "3ebbc4afa48f9eefd87eff4002c5b751c3f299ab", "parents": ["d9749ef854b21fe751545e74c3106bd2b03aea0e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069152 - Add a copy action to the text selection menu. r=fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley,hjones,bolsson,settings-reviewers,omarg\n\nFor background on the Highlight to Search project, here is [[ https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lpprhnIKYbXSNnVE-OSmVcE1Vpm9_vBBIKIOjW8_0lE/edit?tab=t.os3nbc21wjhe | the current spec ]].\n\nTo manually experiment with this feature, here is [[ https://searchux.netlify.app/highlight-to-search/ | the UX prototype ]].\n\nTo test manually, set `browser.highlightToSearch.featureGate` to true, select some text on a page, click the Copy\nicon in the selection menu that appears, and confirm the text is on the clipboard.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332275\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/main-popupset.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js", "browser/components/genai/tests/xpcshell/test_show_chat_entrypoint.js", "browser/components/preferences/config/tabs-browsing.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/tests/browser_tabs_browsing_highlightToSearch.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/genai.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css"], "git_node": "c67c2fc426ede6ba4b7b8d7084de7479c294ad91", "git_parents": ["53b621c35f69e056d9e4018b419648a60e68fbeb"], "node": "9ae24e0dff720727d6f2e529d0c1226cd474db21", "parents": ["3ebbc4afa48f9eefd87eff4002c5b751c3f299ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nathan Barrett \u003cnbarrett@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082634 - Set max width of newtab to match moz-search r=omc-reviewers,ini,emcminn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335206\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/content-src/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/_Base.scss"], "git_node": "21945b7b813bef054665c77e43b83a6611724ad3", "git_parents": ["c67c2fc426ede6ba4b7b8d7084de7479c294ad91"], "node": "65f50496913fac0b3232f30045cef9e46882f34c", "parents": ["9ae24e0dff720727d6f2e529d0c1226cd474db21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nathan Barrett \u003cnbarrett@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083527 - Add spacing between stories and newtab message. r=ini\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335402\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/_Base.scss"], "git_node": "3ef2fd3f91c9665ddd139e7137b24c7460fca95f", "git_parents": ["21945b7b813bef054665c77e43b83a6611724ad3"], "node": "e9724a22676f9cd439453a64f4aca04c2459c906", "parents": ["65f50496913fac0b3232f30045cef9e46882f34c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nathan Barrett \u003cnbarrett@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083528 - Increase card stack border radius r=emcminn,omc-reviewers,fterdal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335403\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css"], "git_node": "4ce0c1da6993bf7783041331d66efc8da91d1b78", "git_parents": ["3ef2fd3f91c9665ddd139e7137b24c7460fca95f"], "node": "145a1ee746d73d4931bb80ae5f531c4c6e888b24", "parents": ["e9724a22676f9cd439453a64f4aca04c2459c906"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Tang \u003cdanielzgtg.opensource@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035730 - Increase localhost/llama.cpp maxLength to 32768 r=Mardak\n\nThe previous max, 8192, made summarization near-useless because we only\nneed it for *long* articles.\n\nTested working with llama.cpp 5aeac37a35b44fde4bdffaec9159f2fcb253b622 .\n32768 seems stable, while 45000 causes connection resets.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335078\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "47acbd5d2c159f10d0828a2f1a77449ac982a60a", "git_parents": ["4ce0c1da6993bf7783041331d66efc8da91d1b78"], "node": "ba7d5f87af1aba11eb4219ec011140a4e02985d8", "parents": ["145a1ee746d73d4931bb80ae5f531c4c6e888b24"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084244 - Fix for vertical pinned tabs height in compact mode r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,niklas,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335763\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "9fe69146e2c6dc41947e0df5c458ca6e6e3cb115", "git_parents": ["47acbd5d2c159f10d0828a2f1a77449ac982a60a"], "node": "5d7b38164d75a0bdb65c39f2a62e3c4d65846653", "parents": ["ba7d5f87af1aba11eb4219ec011140a4e02985d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrej Glavic \u003caglavic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083658 - Set MOZ_REMOTE_ALLOW_SYSTEM_ACCESS for browsertime so local runs work with the bundled geckodriver. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nLocal runs fall back to the geckodriver bundled with browsertime, which\ndoesn't set the variable Firefox now requires for system access.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335996\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/raptor/browsertime/base.py"], "git_node": "9f59330bb03c05f59c7bfe451b618e8845c816cd", "git_parents": ["9fe69146e2c6dc41947e0df5c458ca6e6e3cb115"], "node": "857c6e4d539e753ba3d805d339d32fed06cbb731", "parents": ["5d7b38164d75a0bdb65c39f2a62e3c4d65846653"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mirko Kerezovic \u003cmirko@kerezovic.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068078 - Prefix website select CSS custom properties. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,Mardak,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334065\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-confirmation/ai-website-confirmation.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-select/ai-website-select.css"], "git_node": "1f798a6b12d44f86435af1ae1f99be58cd645de8", "git_parents": ["9f59330bb03c05f59c7bfe451b618e8845c816cd"], "node": "d6c086fefdc5555499990cce4571fc0dd36d83a7", "parents": ["857c6e4d539e753ba3d805d339d32fed06cbb731"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Coll76 \u003ccollins.kubu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081880 - Make make_intl_data.py require a subcommand. r=mgaudet DONTBUILD\n\nRunning make_intl_data.py without a subcommand crashed with an\nAttributeError because argparse subparsers are optional by default in\nPython 3. Marking the subparsers as required makes argparse print the\nusage text and exit with an error when the subcommand is missing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334505\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/intl/make_intl_data.py"], "git_node": "06e367bda3b9c5475929e27627c1e5d3b75444dc", "git_parents": ["1f798a6b12d44f86435af1ae1f99be58cd645de8"], "node": "4ab6253a1391b5f0562b0c544ab2ff3a6772d905", "parents": ["d6c086fefdc5555499990cce4571fc0dd36d83a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marco Castelluccio \u003cmcastelluccio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083676 - Assert that the helper app dialog cleared its progress listener before creating the transfer. r=Gijs\n\nThe check was inverted, so it warned for every download, where the listener is\nexpected to be null. Only the helper app dialog sets the listener, and it\nclears it before the transfer is created, so a listener that is still set is a\nbug.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335246\n", "files": ["uriloader/exthandler/nsExternalHelperAppService.cpp"], "git_node": "6299c4ff89a291b603988c732fb51e0fdc0776cf", "git_parents": ["06e367bda3b9c5475929e27627c1e5d3b75444dc"], "node": "fe76dd8da9d8ac08f4f882dbc90bf353ab3eb698", "parents": ["4ab6253a1391b5f0562b0c544ab2ff3a6772d905"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris Monteiro \u003cchrismmonteiro1+github@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079962 - Show local server hints when a connection to localhost is refused. r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson,Gijs\n\nA refused loopback connection almost always means nothing is listening on\nthat port, so the generic busy-site, network and firewall hints don't apply.\nTimeouts, resets and other hosts keep the existing hints.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332217\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/aboutNetError.mjs", "toolkit/content/aboutNetErrorHelpers.mjs", "toolkit/content/errors/net-errors.mjs", "toolkit/content/net-error-card.mjs", "toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_error_registry.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/neterror/netError.ftl"], "git_node": "361f049312d74c337b27f303ffd0ee00ae55addb", "git_parents": ["6299c4ff89a291b603988c732fb51e0fdc0776cf"], "node": "6d41ecec59dc277f8643add40e7706c174a1aa02", "parents": ["fe76dd8da9d8ac08f4f882dbc90bf353ab3eb698"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matt Cleinman \u003c9295855+mcleinman@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083787 - Update image for empty state r=ip-protection-reviewers,rking\n\nr=#ip-protection-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336036\n", "files": ["browser/components/ipprotection/assets/vpn-website-rules-settings-empty-state.svg", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/vpn-site-rules-list.css", "browser/components/ipprotection/content/vpn-site-rules-list.mjs"], "git_node": "d6c01eb9af3ed9cf265a6fc196c6f438a0ec4f3d", "git_parents": ["361f049312d74c337b27f303ffd0ee00ae55addb"], "node": "0922f9537ed44dd99ab1afcb5386e4e12c8a19fd", "parents": ["6d41ecec59dc277f8643add40e7706c174a1aa02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084856: reject an in-flight WebTransportSendStream close() when abort() races it r=saschanaz\n\nGive the send stream a close algorithm that holds the FIN until a microtask,\nand add the [[PendingOperation]] steps to the controller's abort signal.  An\nabort() in the same turn as close() now closes the pipe with the error status,\nso the parent sends RESET_STREAM instead of the FIN, and the close promise is\nrejected with the abort reason.\n\n[[PendingOperation]] here only spans the microtask before the FIN reaches\nthe pipe, so only an abort() in the same turn as close() is caught; bug\n2073981 covers the full window.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336098\n", "files": ["dom/webtransport/api/WebTransportSendStream.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/streams-close.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "9b46dc5b9fbd9693f222b13a45dfe997984178d6", "git_parents": ["d6c01eb9af3ed9cf265a6fc196c6f438a0ec4f3d"], "node": "c6f3c76d130ac9668d73c13df9d741eb29e4fac1", "parents": ["0922f9537ed44dd99ab1afcb5386e4e12c8a19fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081886: Rename ai-website-chips to smartwindow-chips r=flozia,urlbar-reviewers,adw\n\n**Context**\nWe're renaming `ai-website-chips` to `smartwindow-chips` as this component is no longer used just as a website chip across smart window. We are expanding how we use our chips, adding it to new features such as the monitor and smart pages.\nOur goal is to have a clear naming and also add a third type of chip for source citations - we currently have context and inline, and would like to add source as a third.\n\n**This patch**\nThis patch is related to the renaming of the component, and others in the same stack will handle the CSS and Lit component changes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334757\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-item/agent-monitor-item.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/chat-assistant-citations/chat-assistant-citations.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/chat-assistant-citations/chat-assistant-citations.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-message/ai-chat-message.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-highlights/aitab-highlights.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-table/aitab-table.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-text-block/aitab-text-block.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-chip/smartwindow-chip.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-chip/smartwindow-chip.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-chip/smartwindow-chip.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-prompts/smartwindow-prompts.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/website-chip-container/website-chip-container.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/website-chip-container/website-chip-container.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/aiChatContent.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_content_message_event.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_message.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_blocks.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_table.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_chat.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_item.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_grouped_chips.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_monitor_button_panel.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_monitor_create.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_context_chips.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_inline_mentions.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_telemetry.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_website_chip.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_chat_assistant_citations.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/test_website_chip.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/test_website_chip_page.html", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInputUtils.mjs"], "git_node": "d37bb41e1dd3b4f27bde2404dc5835a0b75e0170", "git_parents": ["9b46dc5b9fbd9693f222b13a45dfe997984178d6"], "node": "25b050c2fefd325a960fd234588bb55f66014cbd", "parents": ["c6f3c76d130ac9668d73c13df9d741eb29e4fac1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge Mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/corruption_detection/frame_instrumentation_generator.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/corruption_detection/frame_instrumentation_generator_header_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/common_audio/signal_processing/auto_correlation.c", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/temporal_layer_rate_tracker.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/temporal_layer_rate_tracker.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/utility/temporal_layer_rate_tracker_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "89b0dae371b2cea270bcafbcf8c9a2c98121800a", "git_parents": ["d37bb41e1dd3b4f27bde2404dc5835a0b75e0170", "e33ac8a9b64e3946a203af8df5b2aa1bb4711d5c"], "node": "090dd7ae4c1af34f637b519599e1b8dac14d1f8d", "parents": ["25b050c2fefd325a960fd234588bb55f66014cbd", "da9645630220310b11df117bd930777f6aebf5bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2035730 - Increase localhost/llama.cpp maxLength to 32768 r=Mardak\" for causing bc tests failures at components/genai\n\nThis reverts commit 47acbd5d2c159f10d0828a2f1a77449ac982a60a.\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "3e83070a2272c693bb048f01a9cc9d2e46c398a5", "git_parents": ["89b0dae371b2cea270bcafbcf8c9a2c98121800a"], "node": "cd4bd8d9667264b57fbd29a1dce4970721f31abd", "parents": ["090dd7ae4c1af34f637b519599e1b8dac14d1f8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2081886: Rename ai-website-chips to smartwindow-chips r=flozia,urlbar-reviewers,adw\" for causing bc and TV tests failures at aiwindow_grouped_chips.js\n\nThis reverts commit d37bb41e1dd3b4f27bde2404dc5835a0b75e0170.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-item/agent-monitor-item.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/chat-assistant-citations/chat-assistant-citations.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/chat-assistant-citations/chat-assistant-citations.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-message/ai-chat-message.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-highlights/aitab-highlights.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-table/aitab-table.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-text-block/aitab-text-block.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-chip/smartwindow-chip.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-chip/smartwindow-chip.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-chip/smartwindow-chip.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-prompts/smartwindow-prompts.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/website-chip-container/website-chip-container.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/website-chip-container/website-chip-container.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/aiChatContent.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_content_message_event.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_message.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_blocks.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aitab_table.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_chat.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_item.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_grouped_chips.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_monitor_button_panel.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_monitor_create.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_context_chips.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_inline_mentions.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_telemetry.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_website_chip.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_chat_assistant_citations.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/test_website_chip.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/test_website_chip_page.html", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInputUtils.mjs"], "git_node": "3df317e34b8b4da0a63be3997656b2baa4a264ff", "git_parents": ["3e83070a2272c693bb048f01a9cc9d2e46c398a5"], "node": "ca22ff0003df6eeed0a68adc34b50d7d395a1f26", "parents": ["cd4bd8d9667264b57fbd29a1dce4970721f31abd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Wyatt Verchere \u003cwverchere@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084826 - Vendoring application-services eba864f. r=bdk,jonesetc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336094\n", "files": ["third_party/application-services/components/ads-client/src/ads.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/fxa-client/src/internal/mod.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/fxa-client/src/internal/state_manager.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/fxa-client/src/state_machine/mod.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/fxa-client/src/state_machine/transitions.rs", "third_party/application-services/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "71cd9e6f21d9603f0594f9eb6f84ef7adc5ae0b4", "git_parents": ["3df317e34b8b4da0a63be3997656b2baa4a264ff"], "node": "cf7b3e9d6dabd3d78e4c12707ee7d819064a239a", "parents": ["ca22ff0003df6eeed0a68adc34b50d7d395a1f26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069164 - Add a three-dot menu to control which selection menu actions are shown. r=fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley,hjones,bolsson,settings-reviewers,omarg\n\nFor background on the Highlight to Search project, here is [[ https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lpprhnIKYbXSNnVE-OSmVcE1Vpm9_vBBIKIOjW8_0lE/edit?tab=t.os3nbc21wjhe | the current spec ]].\n\nTo manually experiment with this feature, here is [[ https://searchux.netlify.app/highlight-to-search/ | the UX prototype ]].\n\nTo test manually, set `browser.highlightToSearch.featureGate` to true,\nselect some text on a page, click the three-dot icon in the selection\nmenu that appears, and confirm each toggle shows or hides its action in\nthe bar.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332770\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/main-popupset.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js", "browser/components/preferences/config/LegacyPaneMappings.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/config/tabs-browsing.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/tests/browser_tabs_browsing_highlightToSearch.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/genai.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css"], "git_node": "4c3c3c60dad593c87dbf6a637c08e606986688ef", "git_parents": ["71cd9e6f21d9603f0594f9eb6f84ef7adc5ae0b4"], "node": "a74f7467556b170106a32bd1a6ca6da9c129711b", "parents": ["cf7b3e9d6dabd3d78e4c12707ee7d819064a239a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Leritte \u003cjleritte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084382 - Keep the background from showing through the fire button's hover animation while its colors cross-fade. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,akulyk\n\nThe flare faded out while the settled flame faded in on top of it, so halfway through the settle about a quarter of the hover background showed through, turning the flame grayish in dark mode. The purple flame and the flare had the same issue during the grow. Each layer now stays opaque until the one fading in above it covers it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335818\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/toolbarbutton-icons.css"], "git_node": "613a00268881dd15ee55b0ee29a9930738801eb3", "git_parents": ["4c3c3c60dad593c87dbf6a637c08e606986688ef"], "node": "2ae43dc7b28ed82d4a95366a86c2856cd05cdeb4", "parents": ["a74f7467556b170106a32bd1a6ca6da9c129711b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084661 - Upgrade taskgraph to 24.5.1. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335998\n", "files": ["taskcluster/requirements.in", "taskcluster/requirements.txt"], "git_node": "6c8ff53f94de1c557749bd525d5e1417a87a2d75", "git_parents": ["613a00268881dd15ee55b0ee29a9930738801eb3"], "node": "7d278fdac4760ca2765b5486f9cc6f5f7d0d317a", "parents": ["2ae43dc7b28ed82d4a95366a86c2856cd05cdeb4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Danielle Graham \u003cdgraham@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049172 - Use design tokens for the blocked site page colours to improve link and button contrast. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,akulyk\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334714\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/blockedSite.css"], "git_node": "90158ac0721764bb2583cf83b84fd2b0ba6c810c", "git_parents": ["6c8ff53f94de1c557749bd525d5e1417a87a2d75"], "node": "fd7590d89b303c1bd742aae2543cad43b9558630", "parents": ["7d278fdac4760ca2765b5486f9cc6f5f7d0d317a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Danielle Graham \u003cdgraham@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082915 - remove non nova test references in fxview tests. r=fxview-reviewers,sfoster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335386\n", "files": ["browser/components/firefoxview/tests/browser/browser_history_firefoxview.js", "browser/components/firefoxview/tests/browser/browser_recentlyclosed_firefoxview.js", "browser/components/firefoxview/tests/browser/browser_syncedtabs_errors_firefoxview.js", "browser/components/firefoxview/tests/browser/browser_syncedtabs_firefoxview.js"], "git_node": "d97a00b6bba299b30ff2cc12f571e83ec54693db", "git_parents": ["90158ac0721764bb2583cf83b84fd2b0ba6c810c"], "node": "b7475a04ef555b2f8c2df843b0355621d2cd2a7a", "parents": ["fd7590d89b303c1bd742aae2543cad43b9558630"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Drew Willcoxon \u003cadw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072942 - Decrease the urlbar row gutter in compact uidensity mode. r=dao,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers\n\nAll this does is make the row gutter smaller in compact mode.\n\nThe spec [1] says rows should be 28px tall in compact mode, and I think it shows\nthe row gutter at 2px.\n\nOn Windows at 100% scale, the current visible row height in normal and compact\ndensities is already 28.5px. The visible height is determined by the font size\nand `--urlbarview-row-padding-block`, whose value is `--space-small`. Changing\nit to `--space-xsmall` drops the height to 23px, which seems too small and cuts\ncuts off the bottom of chiclets. So I think we're good on visible row height.\n\nThe current gutter is 2.7px. The gutter is determined by\n`--urlbarview-row-gutter`, whose value is `--space-xsmall`. Changing it to\n`--space-xxsmall` drops it to 1.4px. A little smaller than 2px but visually it\nmight as well be, it looks reasonable, and it noticeably decreases the height of\nthe panel.\n\n[1] https://www.figma.com/design/XT0eDYh4RtbMNWaYQi0efM/Chrome-Sidebar-UX-Specifications--Sprint-1-?m=auto&node-id=13742-77617&t=0nlbmpOK3tGUU1Tv-1\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336096\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css"], "git_node": "5e67116e9f3e814d0a911ffc6c992f68f3aa971b", "git_parents": ["d97a00b6bba299b30ff2cc12f571e83ec54693db"], "node": "eb58ba5f211d32d0a293c04ed6695ceb02f43e5c", "parents": ["b7475a04ef555b2f8c2df843b0355621d2cd2a7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078993 - Don't run scripts between updating two carets. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336063\n", "files": ["layout/base/AccessibleCaretManager.cpp"], "git_node": "955b3b5b7fc10eeac3adbe182b91d94efe79ff65", "git_parents": ["5e67116e9f3e814d0a911ffc6c992f68f3aa971b"], "node": "0edb0d782f5e3ff1b696e7f2a3564dcb2ee59017", "parents": ["eb58ba5f211d32d0a293c04ed6695ceb02f43e5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083874 - Horoscope: Add the Powered by Yahoo menu string r=fluent-reviewers,flod\n\nAdds the string for the Horoscopes menu link to Yahoo, its content provider. The next patch in the stack uses it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336072\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "19318334e85a44273b0ad47ad4ceb8a2c9b8cd52", "git_parents": ["955b3b5b7fc10eeac3adbe182b91d94efe79ff65"], "node": "786e076a3c4914db4238df5c7a48e36f8ef21341", "parents": ["0edb0d782f5e3ff1b696e7f2a3564dcb2ee59017"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1920886 - Keep the ProcessReader timeout tests' child running well past the timeout. r=mozbase-reviewers,whimboo\n\ntest_timeout and test_output_timeout gave their child 0.1s against a 0.05s timeout, so a reader thread that\nstarted or woke late found the child already finished and reported no timeout. The child now sleeps 10s and is\nkilled when the test ends.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336051\n", "files": ["testing/mozbase/mozprocess/tests/test_process_reader.py"], "git_node": "76d4dc92d9ca0d7fd9f1c0ec8d6c925bec22ac9f", "git_parents": ["19318334e85a44273b0ad47ad4ceb8a2c9b8cd52"], "node": "1336e52aae6cc4060e8f1ec678ed2120c65ee4b0", "parents": ["786e076a3c4914db4238df5c7a48e36f8ef21341"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1972602 - Remove legacy enrollment store and disable persistence in tests r=ralkhulaidi,nimbus-reviewers,emcminn,settings-reviewers,Gijs\n\nThe shared SQL database in the ProfilesDatastoreServices has been the\nsource of truth for Nimbus since bug 1972426. However, we've still had\nthe legacy ExperimentDataStore.json to support xpcshell tests that do\nnot enable the ProfilesDatastoreService (see bug 1967779).\n\nBy default we no longer persist experiments to disk when running in a\ntest environment (when `Cu.isInAutomation` is true at startup). This\nremoves the need for keeping the legacy experiment store. Persistence\nis, however, enabled in all toolkit/components/nimbus xpcshell tests to\nensure correctness.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D322754\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/experimental_features/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-quickactions/browser_commands.js", "testing/profiles/xpcshell/user.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/Enrollments.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/ExperimentManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/ExperimentStore.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/Migrations.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/PrefFlipsFeature.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/RemoteSettingsExperimentLoader.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/SharedDataMap.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/NimbusTestUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/browser/browser_SharedDataMap.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/browser/browser_about_config_pref_change.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/browser/browser_experimentapi_child.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/browser/browser_remotesettings_experiment_enroll.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/browser/head.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/head.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/shutdown/test_RSEL_updateRecipes_load_unenrolled_slugs.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/shutdown/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_ExperimentManager_lifecycle.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_ExperimentManager_prefs.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_ExperimentStore.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_FirefoxLabs.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_Migrations.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_RemoteSettingsExperimentLoader_updateRecipes.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_bug2054546.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_policy.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_prefFlips.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "fc4a910c10545412dc4291547f796454c409bf5b", "git_parents": ["76d4dc92d9ca0d7fd9f1c0ec8d6c925bec22ac9f"], "node": "a7a6c0a4a77bd852c0a95c448fa590dfd37bcc62", "parents": ["1336e52aae6cc4060e8f1ec678ed2120c65ee4b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054870 - Picture of the Day: don't flash the empty state when the widget is turned back on. r=reemhamz\n\nTurning Picture of the Day off used to send an empty picture to the page, so turning it back on briefly showed \u201cCheck back tomorrow\u201d while the image loaded. The feed now clears its cache without updating the page, as Weather does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335309\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/PictureOfTheDayFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_PictureOfTheDayFeed.js"], "git_node": "461043e5985a60dd2711251e465233eeba674752", "git_parents": ["fc4a910c10545412dc4291547f796454c409bf5b"], "node": "ba2d49df30c12be197a7f5e38fca8849ccd6bdcc", "parents": ["a7a6c0a4a77bd852c0a95c448fa590dfd37bcc62"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Cunnane \u003cscunnane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069165 - Record clicks on the Manage settings entry of the text selection menu. r=yjamora\n\nFor background on the Highlight to Search project, here is [[ https://docs.google.com/document/d/1lpprhnIKYbXSNnVE-OSmVcE1Vpm9_vBBIKIOjW8_0lE/edit?tab=t.os3nbc21wjhe | the current spec ]].\n\nTo manually experiment with this feature, here is [[ https://searchux.netlify.app/highlight-to-search/ | the UX prototype ]].\n\nAdds the `selection_menu.menu_click` event, with the clicked entry in its `item` extra, and records it when \"Manage settings\" is clicked in the three-dot menu.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335856\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/GenAI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/genai/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/genai/tests/browser/browser_chat_shortcuts.js"], "git_node": "3eccbbc13c5f6fd00847ebe52f5df6ccaa0367a2", "git_parents": ["461043e5985a60dd2711251e465233eeba674752"], "node": "b5403c579deaffd4458e70ec3f5988b6710cf204", "parents": ["ba2d49df30c12be197a7f5e38fca8849ccd6bdcc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Heitor Neiva \u003chneiva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072797 - Exclude beetmover-integration tasks from automatic try selection. r=taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau\n\nmach try auto impersonates autoland and the filters then let it thru even on Try.\nAdding `^beetmover-integration-` to `UNCOMMON_TRY_TASK_LABELS` excludes the tasks from try auto and ordinary fuzzy selections while still allowing explicit selection via `--full`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336038\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/target_tasks.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_target_tasks.py"], "git_node": "0d9a82ec5bbbc85bce8bdbbaf5d720b46efd4835", "git_parents": ["3eccbbc13c5f6fd00847ebe52f5df6ccaa0367a2"], "node": "4d68bbf9f0da2c9681e00f17d37e5810a3a70d46", "parents": ["b5403c579deaffd4458e70ec3f5988b6710cf204"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\naf -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nan -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nar -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nast -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\naz -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nbe -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nbg -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nbn -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nbo -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nbqi -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nbr -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nbrx -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nbs -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nca -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nca-valencia -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\ncak -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\nckb -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d888e\ncs -\u003e 2c980fabd54bd83fa76e5018cff052ca4c4d