efault", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2073135 - Clear all aspects of depth-stencil attachments when resolving WebGL2 framebuffer data. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\" for causing macOS gl failures in test_2_conformance__context__context-attributes-alpha-depth-stencil-antialias.html.\n\nThis reverts commit 6cdf09c22bf6be9c54e1e3ef5f49691afb88624e.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLFramebuffer.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLFramebuffer.h"], "git_node": "6bb811006a50c49d09691d9066cfebbc1b2b1dcc", "git_parents": ["da28b0f57a2babecf41e9ba512b03cb013a5b532"], "node": "f6051ce1ac15a48ce146fa85e9e0eac911e27554", "parents": ["79602c430291cf2d736194f741e105c827227189"], "tags": []}], "date": 1793206852, "git_changesets": ["da28b0f57a2babecf41e9ba512b03cb013a5b532", "6bb811006a50c49d09691d9066cfebbc1b2b1dcc"], "user": "sstanca@mozilla.com"}, "45670": {"changesets": [{"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085310 - Enabled `unifiedSearchButton.always` in nightly. r=jteow\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336354\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser_searchModeSwitcher_basic.js"], "git_node": "532638161e81e1fe049fc645f4747521ccea3098", "git_parents": ["0e693091efcc82e55df07772299ecfb68a6d1d06"], "node": "4e2c88f0ad32a485914c9d1864eca3d8109fc820", "parents": ["5a9a73d2912636a8715fa145b21048be654223f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082172 - Use appropriate userContext for contextual search r=urlbar-reviewers,mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336385\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/ActionsProviderContextualSearch.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d11a66924b178a8643fab82851918057e69b4605", "git_parents": ["532638161e81e1fe049fc645f4747521ccea3098"], "node": "9cde4963c2b74e1d0e50cfd2b197f65846b4cae1", "parents": ["4e2c88f0ad32a485914c9d1864eca3d8109fc820"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jaron Kramer \u003cinfo@jkramertech.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1961431 - Respect reduced motion for fullscreen API transitions. r=vhilla,edgar\n\nSkip fullscreen API fade transitions when LookAndFeel reports a preference for reduced motion. Check the setting on each request and preserve the configured transition durations.\n\nAdd a browser test using DOMFullscreenTestUtils that covers entering and leaving fullscreen with reduced motion disabled, enabled, and disabled again. Run on all desktop platforms and expect custom transitions on Windows.\n\nMake security-delay tests explicitly opt into animations when they require fullscreen fades. Add permission-prompt coverage with reduced motion enabled to verify the normal security delay still blocks clicks without a transition.\n\nExercise legacy fullscreen on macOS in the reduced-motion permission test and register observer and permission cleanup. Use ChromeUtils.now consistently with PopupNotifications for security-delay assertions and simulated expiration.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330168\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-fullscreen/browser_fullscreen_permissions_prompt.js", "browser/base/content/test/browser-popupNotifications/browser_popupNotification_security_delay.js", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowOuter.cpp", "dom/base/test/fullscreen/browser.toml", "dom/base/test/fullscreen/browser_fullscreen-reduced-motion.js"], "git_node": "2511cb15c44b122399e503a6b1e55e16bd18214d", "git_parents": ["d11a66924b178a8643fab82851918057e69b4605"], "node": "23919ac25150b25b29de8a48779deafe0c9bc142", "parents": ["9cde4963c2b74e1d0e50cfd2b197f65846b4cae1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079620 - Base the decision image on Debian 13. r=releng-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330474\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/docker-image/kind.yml"], "git_node": "0b5ad54d7da09325228da06263baecaeee3559b5", "git_parents": ["2511cb15c44b122399e503a6b1e55e16bd18214d"], "node": "a6b7fe7dea237e7d66beccb199ae494bbeb4d014", "parents": ["23919ac25150b25b29de8a48779deafe0c9bc142"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083404: Remove invalid special-case for negating hypot() expressions in calc(). r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nBefore this patch, we mishandled negation of 'hypot()' in a special-case that\npropagated the negation to the children.  This was ineffective and wrong; it\nstill produced a positive result, due to the squaring arithmetic that happens\nin a hypot() operation.\n\nThis patch makes hypot() share the same codpath that we use for many other math\nfunctions, implementing negation using wrap_self_in_negate().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337315\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/generics/calc.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/hypot-pow-sqrt-computed.html"], "git_node": "a362b3e9a326e51565e836aeb0c1b7befcbd02bf", "git_parents": ["0b5ad54d7da09325228da06263baecaeee3559b5"], "node": "e7324d6ddff63e230a8566fa4da748eb063e6afa", "parents": ["a6b7fe7dea237e7d66beccb199ae494bbeb4d014"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084178 - Don't block the main thread on Bounce Tracking Protection storage initialization. r=bvandersloot\n\nDatabase operations are queued on the same serial task queue as\ninitialization, so they already run after it. Waiting for it on the main\nthread made the first clear-data call or write after startup hang for as\nlong as the database took to open and load.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335638\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingProtection.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingProtectionStorage.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingProtectionStorage.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/nsIBounceTrackingProtection.idl", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/xpcshell/test_bouncetracking_storage_batch_write.js"], "git_node": "978e8e715fce2342537e652eebe994c1d4382982", "git_parents": ["a362b3e9a326e51565e836aeb0c1b7befcbd02bf"], "node": "5d57f753563c9226e1fded5de825826b27c59e9a", "parents": ["e7324d6ddff63e230a8566fa4da748eb063e6afa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084178 - Don't let loading the Bounce Tracking Protection database undo earlier writes and clears. r=bvandersloot\n\nThe on-disk state is applied to memory in a main thread task that can run\nafter writes and clears issued while the database was still loading. Skip\nloaded entries that those clears deleted. Merge the others using the usual\nprecedence rules and write the result back for sites written before the\nload, so the in-memory state matches the database.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335639\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingProtectionStorage.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingProtectionStorage.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/xpcshell/test_bouncetracking_storage_load.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "2412434d0e41affaaa57f9f3f52353c58ef4ca1f", "git_parents": ["978e8e715fce2342537e652eebe994c1d4382982"], "node": "232d1d51a57933b2d179f44f849801dde8f7302a", "parents": ["5d57f753563c9226e1fded5de825826b27c59e9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080325 - [devtools] Wait for #customizable-select in browser_rules_pseudo-element_01.js r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337458\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_pseudo-element_01.js"], "git_node": "56b4cca1503ab17334fa4bdfe00e7801d31f9c42", "git_parents": ["2412434d0e41affaaa57f9f3f52353c58ef4ca1f"], "node": "6a73a8549f7535ac5a1a700d3894834044110a92", "parents": ["232d1d51a57933b2d179f44f849801dde8f7302a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikki Sharpley \u003cnsharpley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083138 - Add the Nova motion easing tokens to the design system. r=kcochrane,jules,desktop-theme-reviewers,reusable-components-reviewers,sidebar-reviewers\n\n--motion-easing-emphasized and --motion-easing-standard are shared by the motion\nwork blocking on this bug, so they move out of sidebar.css and into the design\nsystem. The sidebar keeps its own duration tokens.\n\nThe new \"motion\" token category keeps them out of the uncategorized bucket, and\ngives the storybook table a preview that animates with the curve rather than\nthe generic swatch, which would emit an invalid \"motion:\" declaration.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336156\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_sidebar_animation.js", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/config/helpers/general/token-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/base/motion.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/storybook/tokens-table.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/storybook/tokens-table.stories.mjs"], "git_node": "8ef0137f9a4cc04540099bdb03889f6c1623c061", "git_parents": ["56b4cca1503ab17334fa4bdfe00e7801d31f9c42"], "node": "ad2bdd1e24e2ce0bf1e1d482c6179357e094d0cb", "parents": ["6a73a8549f7535ac5a1a700d3894834044110a92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Peter Lafreniere \u003cpeter@n8pjl.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083387 - Cache timezone offsets on ZonedDateTime objects. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,dminor\n\nOffset lookup in ICU makes up ~70% of the cost of date/time getters,\nand 10-50% of more complex operations. Caching the offsets eliminates\nICU overhead, at the cost of a small (2-8%) penalty for offset timezones.\n\nPack offset in the same slot as the calendar identifier to avoid\npromoting ZonedDateTime from AllocKind::OBJECT4.\n\nFor simplicity, this patch only uses the cache for the reciever\nwhen differencing, even when arg0 is a ZonedDateTime with a filled\ncache.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334912\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/temporal/Calendar.h", "js/src/builtin/temporal/Duration.cpp", "js/src/builtin/temporal/PlainDate.cpp", "js/src/builtin/temporal/PlainDateTime.cpp", "js/src/builtin/temporal/PlainTime.cpp", "js/src/builtin/temporal/TemporalTypes.h", "js/src/builtin/temporal/TimeZone.cpp", "js/src/builtin/temporal/TimeZone.h", "js/src/builtin/temporal/ToString.cpp", "js/src/builtin/temporal/ZonedDateTime.cpp", "js/src/builtin/temporal/ZonedDateTime.h"], "git_node": "588ca0be4f0c15ec197110e4bcae770f734c5bb4", "git_parents": ["8ef0137f9a4cc04540099bdb03889f6c1623c061"], "node": "99eec32b5a3137cc67f221b20967d8d99929a820", "parents": ["ad2bdd1e24e2ce0bf1e1d482c6179357e094d0cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henrik Skupin \u003cmail@hskupin.info\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070526 - [wdspec] Scale the action duration in duration.py by the timeout multiplier. r=webdriver-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nOn slow builds the first animation frame can arrive after the whole duration has elapsed, which results in only a single event being dispatched.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337567\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/perform_actions/duration.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/perform_actions/duration.py"], "git_node": "e32d28fbc6ee8325ae71229014d7ea478ab06cd6", "git_parents": ["588ca0be4f0c15ec197110e4bcae770f734c5bb4"], "node": "c34c67dce7377759f2a7cd9a1d480e62715341ab", "parents": ["99eec32b5a3137cc67f221b20967d8d99929a820"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1825674 - Fix offscreen-element-modified-before-coming-onscreen.html. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nThe transition wasn't being canceled because the flag was not being\nlooked up in the originating element.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337551\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/gecko/pseudo_element.rs", "servo/components/style/gecko/wrapper.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-view-transitions/offscreen-element-modified-before-coming-onscreen.html.ini"], "git_node": "6470fdebf7f16a1ba101694cdd3c8ea00ed93c5f", "git_parents": ["e32d28fbc6ee8325ae71229014d7ea478ab06cd6"], "node": "bd513229d3ab2c72ef678043693010f9a31399da", "parents": ["c34c67dce7377759f2a7cd9a1d480e62715341ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "pstanciu \u003cpstanciu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2084744: Update about:glean based on UX feedback r=TravisLong,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\" for causing bc failures @ browser_about_glean.js\n\nThis reverts commit 0e693091efcc82e55df07772299ecfb68a6d1d06.\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/aboutGlean.css", "toolkit/content/aboutGlean.html", "toolkit/content/aboutGlean.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/aboutGlean.ftl"], "git_node": "b14ce7584c2aae2d8b5a569ef9e570abca0d8fd7", "git_parents": ["6470fdebf7f16a1ba101694cdd3c8ea00ed93c5f"], "node": "f2e070b029cbd51f23e53c525dbc3c7d411c0d10", "parents": ["bd513229d3ab2c72ef678043693010f9a31399da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2073135 - Clear all aspects of depth-stencil attachments when resolving WebGL2 framebuffer data. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\" for causing macOS gl failures in test_2_conformance__context__context-attributes-alpha-depth-stencil-antialias.html.\n\nThis reverts commit 6cdf09c22bf6be9c54e1e3ef5f49691afb88624e.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLFramebuffer.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLFramebuffer.h"], "git_node": "2aaf1516463fafc94c1dbc80eb9e4ba7313f23b3", "git_parents": ["b14ce7584c2aae2d8b5a569ef9e570abca0d8fd7"], "node": "2f02bd66524de4f4a43de65beb15df7c2a492e31", "parents": ["f2e070b029cbd51f23e53c525dbc3c7d411c0d10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vlad Zahorodnii \u003cvlad.zahorodnii@kde.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086569 - Set proper app id with xx-pip-v1, r=gtk-reviewers,emilio\n\nThe `org.mozilla.` APP_NAME app id is usually not what we want.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337556\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp"], "git_node": "30b7996447f8a6212d7577aff0d38c9f021aba0f", "git_parents": ["2aaf1516463fafc94c1dbc80eb9e4ba7313f23b3"], "node": "551074a5e47b1b933ae9b521cc052bf4c4893d09", "parents": ["2f02bd66524de4f4a43de65beb15df7c2a492e31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061165 - Don't let a bfcache restore overwrite BTP's final host. r=manuel\n\nA bfcache restore never goes through OnStartNavigation, so it must not update the live record. Overwriting finalHost made the pending client bounce detection timer classify the page the user just left.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334238\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingState.cpp"], "git_node": "73f8d2e43d6f0f0b8298013dd01d785fcd297f24", "git_parents": ["30b7996447f8a6212d7577aff0d38c9f021aba0f"], "node": "634ccdc085ed43893c2118d8cf144a0d140d2bda", "parents": ["551074a5e47b1b933ae9b521cc052bf4c4893d09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061165 - Add a test case for a bfcache restore overwriting finalHost. r=manuel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316792\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser_bouncetracking_bfcache_finalhost.js"], "git_node": "abe226b3fc435019db4d24ca8843c006cad5b0ba", "git_parents": ["73f8d2e43d6f0f0b8298013dd01d785fcd297f24"], "node": "2f88e2074d7613f21bcdea3cee13fcefb5ffc0bf", "parents": ["634ccdc085ed43893c2118d8cf144a0d140d2bda"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082583 - Let a bfcache restore end BTP's extended navigation. r=dom-core-reviewers,manuel,smaug\n\nA bfcache restore creates no DocumentLoadListener, so BTP never saw it as a\nnavigation and kept the previous record open. If the restored page then\nnavigated without user activation, the page the user had gone Back from was\nclassified. Run the navigation steps from the parent's restore path instead,\nmatching a Back that is not served from the bfcache.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335170\n", "files": ["docshell/shistory/nsSHistory.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingState.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingState.h"], "git_node": "2cafdc65efbf83290bf37cf391352b4beb587af5", "git_parents": ["abe226b3fc435019db4d24ca8843c006cad5b0ba"], "node": "f8107a124f9d8b4467f3e483273906781376d5be", "parents": ["2f88e2074d7613f21bcdea3cee13fcefb5ffc0bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2082583 - Add tests for a bfcache restored page navigating without user activation. r=manuel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335171\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser_bouncetracking_bfcache_restore_redirect.js"], "git_node": "7ba4903c899aef6b13f56de70e385a04893a5435", "git_parents": ["2cafdc65efbf83290bf37cf391352b4beb587af5"], "node": "ed38e6af20cfff0962078c1b52de6a66fe2500ea", "parents": ["f8107a124f9d8b4467f3e483273906781376d5be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083368 - Set sharedUserMaxSdkVersion for the Fenix Beta and Release builds. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nWith it set to 32, new installs on Android 13 and later no longer join the shared user ID, while updated\ninstalls keep it. This resolves the Deprecated lint warning, so its suppression is removed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337381\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/beta/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/release/AndroidManifest.xml"], "git_node": "099964401b598081a701474e4cc020f9f974eb11", "git_parents": ["7ba4903c899aef6b13f56de70e385a04893a5435"], "node": "f96db04a3aa9e88585440acee60f86ec4d5f1836", "parents": ["ed38e6af20cfff0962078c1b52de6a66fe2500ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079555 - Migrate Dropdowns to use new Dropdown2 component r=android-reviewers,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333679\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/gleandebugtools/ui/GleanDebugToolsScreen.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/address/ui/edit/EditAddressScreen.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/creditcards/ui/CreditCardEditorScreen.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/doh/root/DohSettingsScreen.kt"], "git_node": "04a8864f4248f586e353ae7bca001b4e2e2cf36d", "git_parents": ["099964401b598081a701474e4cc020f9f974eb11"], "node": "4ef0bade5affc5c617652ec8b0dd498bab7323ad", "parents": ["f96db04a3aa9e88585440acee60f86ec4d5f1836"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079554 - Migrate the Translations Dropdown to use the new Dropdown2 component and update the Translations screen to match M3 spec r=android-reviewers,ohall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333680\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/translations/DownloadIndicator.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/translations/TranslationsDialogBottomSheet.kt"], "git_node": "7942d75eb7814e5521b06c4a3f20730e4e45cfdb", "git_parents": ["04a8864f4248f586e353ae7bca001b4e2e2cf36d"], "node": "bc7ac1ba819751eacb21dbb401281f447d0fb156", "parents": ["4ef0bade5affc5c617652ec8b0dd498bab7323ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079556 - Remove Dropdown and replace it with Dropdown2 r=android-reviewers,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333681\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/base/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/base/Dropdown.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/base/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/base/Dropdown2.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/base/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/base/menu/DropdownMenu.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/base/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/base/Dropdown2Test.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/base/src/test/java/mozilla/components/compose/base/DropdownTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/gleandebugtools/ui/GleanDebugToolsScreen.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/address/ui/edit/EditAddressScreen.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/creditcards/ui/CreditCardEditorScreen.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/doh/root/DohSettingsScreen.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/translations/TranslationsDialogBottomSheet.kt"], "git_node": "01f83e0326dd8e4d551e88effef6dcc43d220cc4", "git_parents": ["7942d75eb7814e5521b06c4a3f20730e4e45cfdb"], "node": "a9f8cba90a77ddb841784aeff560d2606aafe505", "parents": ["bc7ac1ba819751eacb21dbb401281f447d0fb156"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084193 - Remove formDefault color from AcornColors r=android-reviewers,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336016\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/base/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/base/theme/AcornColors.kt"], "git_node": "56b114470de7f77a744d3652d3db08b2306cb7cf", "git_parents": ["01f83e0326dd8e4d551e88effef6dcc43d220cc4"], "node": "0a4f40250df5aad9605c9f3fcc44e5fd9892c417", "parents": ["a9f8cba90a77ddb841784aeff560d2606aafe505"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083306 - Give the stack overflow trap at wasm baseline function entry a stackmap.  r=yury.\n\nThe Trap::StackOverflow created here didn't have a stackmap.  This patch\ncreates one, when compiling for debugging.  We can't use the same stackmap as\nalready exists for the interrupt trap because the two traps differ in\nresumability.\n\nThe debug-mode stackmap check (at end of baseline compilation) is updated\nso as to check that all Trap::StackOverflow's have a stackmap.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335989\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc-in-interrupt-at-entry.js", "js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmGC.h"], "git_node": "f6176fe3d657e397279524027a7717317e5be7df", "git_parents": ["56b114470de7f77a744d3652d3db08b2306cb7cf"], "node": "5311c7f39f9a2a7d08e3e7e7c1613153c94611fe", "parents": ["0a4f40250df5aad9605c9f3fcc44e5fd9892c417"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083306 - WasmFrameIter::WasmFrameIter: use the caller's call site as the resume PC when a wasm trap has unwound the trapping frame.  r=yury.\n\nWhen an IndirectCallBadSig trap has a wasm caller, wasm::StartUnwinding\ndiscards the callee's frame and WasmFrameIter starts at the caller's frame.\nIts resume PC was still the trap's resume PC in the callee, so a GC during the\ntrap looked up the callee's stackmap for the caller's frame. That finds\nnothing, leaving the caller's frame untraced; once the next patch adds a map\nfor this trap, it would apply the wrong map and assert.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335990\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/wasm-indirect-bad-sig-gc.js", "js/src/wasm/WasmFrameIter.cpp"], "git_node": "f70112a06d428542eedf9c1dd42166766b86e241", "git_parents": ["f6176fe3d657e397279524027a7717317e5be7df"], "node": "019a6c53474ed5f34d7828b9c69cb23ce7fcf2fb", "parents": ["5311c7f39f9a2a7d08e3e7e7c1613153c94611fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083306 - Give the IndirectCallBadSig trap in the wasm baseline function prologue a stackmap.  r=yury.\n\nGenerateFunctionPrologue creates a signature-check trap.  This patch now causes\nit to return the trap's location, so that beginFunction can register a stackmap\nfor it.\n\nDeciding what stackmap to make is difficult.  The trap fires only when the\ncaller's and callee's signatures differ, so the callee's signature can't be\ntrusted to say which argument registers and stack slots hold refs.  The trap\ndoesn't resume, and we take advantage of that to build a map that marks nothing\nas a ref; the only important feature is that the map has to match the size of\nthe callee's frame.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335991\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmBaselineCompile.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmFrameIter.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmFrameIter.h"], "git_node": "78aa3c457a1d264dde4d89cfae5477766ee61ce4", "git_parents": ["f70112a06d428542eedf9c1dd42166766b86e241"], "node": "068b5a1d7d894715edfa349fa4a527deafc1bdc6", "parents": ["019a6c53474ed5f34d7828b9c69cb23ce7fcf2fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ndokutovich \u003cndokutovich@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080608 - Restore tabs that reference an unknown tab group. r=sessionstore-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,sthompson\n\ncreateTabsForSessionRestore() creates tabs with insertTab: false, so a tab is\ninserted only when it is appended to a DOM fragment. A tab whose groupId is not\npresent in the window's groups list skipped that append - the \"skip any group\nprocessing\" comment also skipped insertion - leaving the tab uninserted and\nwithout a position.\n\nSessionStore's #restoreTab() then threw \"Shouldn't be trying to restore a tab\nthat has no position\" on that tab, which aborted the restore of the entire\nwindow and silently dropped every remaining tab in it. Measured against 157.0.1\nwith a 40-tab state, one tab carrying an unresolvable groupId at index 35\nrestored 35 tabs; with the group defined, all 40 restored.\n\nAppend such a tab to the top-level fragment so it is restored ungrouped, and\nkeep a single bad tab from discarding the rest of the window.\n\n#restoreTab() marks the window busy before it touches the tab and clears that\nstate on its last line, so the check for a missing position now runs before the\nwindow is marked busy. Without that, a caller that swallows the error leaves the\nwindow busy forever and SSWindowStateReady is never dispatched for it. The\nselected tab, restored ahead of the loop, is guarded like the rest.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D332744\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_tab_groups_restore_unknown_group_id.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "eeab674cf8ee30cbb6fabf9678177736d8f3d219", "git_parents": ["78aa3c457a1d264dde4d89cfae5477766ee61ce4"], "node": "e1fcf8e4bfeecae9a7c790bef552ccc22b855fca", "parents": ["068b5a1d7d894715edfa349fa4a527deafc1bdc6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fabio Kaminski \u003cfabio.kaminski@codethink.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080821 Support for color conversion in GetImageData/PutImageData. r=emilio,gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334581\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/color-type/2d.color.type.u8p3.to.f16srgb.to.u8p3.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/color-type/2d.color.type.u8p3.to.u8srgb.to.u8p3.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/color-type/2d.color.type.u8srgb.to.f16p3.to.u8srgb.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/color-type/2d.color.type.u8srgb.to.u8p3.to.u8srgb.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/context-attributes/getContextAttributes.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-color-space-settings.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-display-p3-drawImage-ImageBitmap-Blob.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-display-p3-drawImage-ImageBitmap-cloned.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-display-p3-drawImage-ImageBitmap-image.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-display-p3-drawImage-ImageBitmap-video.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-display-p3-drawImage-video.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-display-p3-drawImage.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/wide-gamut-canvas/canvas-display-p3-pattern-image.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/pixel-manipulation/2d.imageData.createImageBitmap.p3.rgba.unorm8.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/color-type/2d.color.type.u8p3.to.f16srgb.to.u8p3.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/color-type/2d.color.type.u8p3.to.f16srgb.to.u8p3.worker.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/color-type/2d.color.type.u8p3.to.u8srgb.to.u8p3.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/color-type/2d.color.type.u8p3.to.u8srgb.to.u8p3.worker.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/color-type/2d.color.type.u8srgb.to.f16p3.to.u8srgb.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/color-type/2d.color.type.u8srgb.to.f16p3.to.u8srgb.worker.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/color-type/2d.color.type.u8srgb.to.u8p3.to.u8srgb.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/color-type/2d.color.type.u8srgb.to.u8p3.to.u8srgb.worker.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/pixel-manipulation/2d.imageData.createImageBitmap.p3.rgba.unorm8.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/pixel-manipulation/2d.imageData.createImageBitmap.p3.rgba.unorm8.worker.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/pixel-manipulation/2d.imageData.createImageBitmap.srgb.rgba.unorm8.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/offscreen/pixel-manipulation/2d.imageData.createImageBitmap.srgb.rgba.unorm8.worker.js.ini"], "git_node": "da1273f7594f86927a4e74f8768e0a70fc2ca090", "git_parents": ["eeab674cf8ee30cbb6fabf9678177736d8f3d219"], "node": "731e4e10f270fecfdda16106427eba9c1c6eb79c", "parents": ["e1fcf8e4bfeecae9a7c790bef552ccc22b855fca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072714 - Update inline padding for edge elements in the toolbar/tabstrip and update sidebar tool buttons to be 28x28 in compact mode r=desktop-theme-reviewers,sidebar-reviewers,nsharpley,sfoster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333826\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_editcontrols_update.js", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_hidden_widget_overflow.js", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-main.css", "browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar.css", "browser/themes/shared/toolbarbuttons.css"], "git_node": "1219580d439b0c5efb5d182237a6d68966fbc34d", "git_parents": ["da1273f7594f86927a4e74f8768e0a70fc2ca090"], "node": "d8b103f10bca6102d139c03156cc2e644017a119", "parents": ["731e4e10f270fecfdda16106427eba9c1c6eb79c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071191 - Write wptrunner.local.ini atomically. r=jgraham\n\nConcurrent manifestupdate.run callers, such as the parallel graph\ngeneration in test_generate_params.py, could read the config while\nanother process had truncated it, failing with \"No 