pdateRootFrame when the root scroll container is gone. r=layout-reviewers,tnikkel\n\nThe root element can lose its frames, e.g. by display:none, while the\nPresShell and the root content APZC stay alive, so a repaint request with\nan async zoom can arrive without a root scroll container.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337312\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/util/APZCCallbackHelper.cpp", "gfx/tests/crashtests/2086198.html", "gfx/tests/crashtests/crashtests.list"], "git_node": "6e9b55e44cc1843f3c583fffca18c79ac123a8ca", "git_parents": ["bf75471716c53f2d8e94284f3d37ad6f209459d6"], "node": "ffb86723842797519c5b4296144390204822088c", "parents": ["eef421b1b07dcef283eed7104fec4fe49b6bf736"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077043 - Make `HTMLEditor` stop deleting extant unnecessary line break at inserting text r=m_kato\n\nAfter bug 2019689, we try the simplest structure for the following\nedit handling, i.e., we always clean up unnecessary line break after\nthe inserted text. However, some web apps may insert unnecessary\nline breaks for their private markers. Then, removing the unnecessary\nline breaks causes breaking such app, especially when we're handling\ncomposition string because modifying the DOM during a composition may\ncause committing the composition.\n\nThis patch makes `HTMLEditor::HandleInsertText` retrieve unnecessary\nline break first (except the unnecessary line break for empty block).\nThen, if there is, the clean-ups won't run.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336976\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/EditorLineBreak.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorLineBreak.h", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditSubActionHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditUtils.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditUtils.h", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDeleteHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorInsertParagraphHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLStyleEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/WhiteSpaceVisibilityKeeper.cpp", "editor/libeditor/WhiteSpaceVisibilityKeeper.h", "editor/libeditor/gtest/TestHTMLEditUtils.cpp", "editor/libeditor/tests/mochitest.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/test_bug787432.html", "editor/libeditor/tests/test_insert_composition_before_unnecessary_linebreak.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/editing/data/inserttext.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/editing/data/multitest.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/editing/other/inserttext-before-unnecessary-linebreak.html", "widget/tests/window_composition_text_querycontent.xhtml"], "git_node": "b75f9efa5e0d477e208c24c29c374c4878f04905", "git_parents": ["6e9b55e44cc1843f3c583fffca18c79ac123a8ca"], "node": "44005623c405acee44b8feab0cba7b5889013a4a", "parents": ["ffb86723842797519c5b4296144390204822088c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Botond Ballo \u003cbotond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083925 - Use a buffer of recent pan gesture events to determine direction for axis locking. r=hiro,canalun\n\nIf the touchpad hardware is sending frequent events with small deltas\n(or the user is just panning slowly), it's possible that no single\nevent's delta is large enough to overcome\napz.axis_lock.breakout_threshold, causing the user to get stuck with\nscrolling locked to an axis even if they're now trying to scroll\nalong the other axis.\n\nTouchscreens have had similar logic since bug 1894122.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336929\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.h", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestAxisLock.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "3f2fce60f2a443bc0bfca6af029ddd1b868eee50", "git_parents": ["b75f9efa5e0d477e208c24c29c374c4878f04905"], "node": "2f3adcc02dba49bd191056b3dc10c01348b6c724", "parents": ["44005623c405acee44b8feab0cba7b5889013a4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Magnus Melin \u003cmkmelin+mozilla@iki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085914 - Discard buffered input when TCPSocket upgrades to TLS. r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337009\n", "files": ["dom/network/TCPSocket.cpp", "dom/network/TCPSocket.h", "dom/network/moz.build", "dom/network/tests/unit/test_tcpsocket_starttls.js", "dom/network/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "8d88dd1eefe0ee3dd4db74b1e5647babe1fd49c3", "git_parents": ["3f2fce60f2a443bc0bfca6af029ddd1b868eee50"], "node": "36b2209a54ab159f65b3d730a72ed097a97cf221", "parents": ["2f3adcc02dba49bd191056b3dc10c01348b6c724"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Exploding-Joysticks \u003cExplodingJoysticks@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1831048 - Part 13: Fix 136 'misc-unused-parameters' warnings under /toolkit r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,crashreporting-reviewers,application-update-reviewers,spohl,Gijs\n\nhttps://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/misc/unused-parameters.html\n\nEverything found by ./mach static-analysis was manually inspected and changed if needed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335792\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/commandlines/nsCommandLine.cpp", "toolkit/components/ctypes/ctypes.cpp", "toolkit/components/downloads/DownloadPlatform.cpp", "toolkit/components/extensions/NativeMessagingProxy.cpp", "toolkit/components/finalizationwitness/FinalizationWitnessService.cpp", "toolkit/components/parentalcontrols/nsParentalControlsServiceDefault.cpp", "toolkit/components/reflect/reflect.cpp", "toolkit/components/remote/nsDBusRemoteClient.cpp", "toolkit/components/remote/nsDBusRemoteServer.cpp", "toolkit/components/remote/nsRemoteService.cpp", "toolkit/components/satchel/nsFormFillController.cpp", "toolkit/components/statusfilter/nsBrowserStatusFilter.cpp", "toolkit/components/typeaheadfind/nsTypeAheadFind.cpp", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/VariableLengthPrefixSet.cpp",