user": "ctuns@mozilla.com"}, "45675": {"changesets": [{"author": "Mark Kennedy \u003cmkennedy@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077705 - Replace Solo with Firefox Enterprise on More from Mozilla r=fluent-reviewers,settings-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles,bolsson,Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337213\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/logos/firefox-enterprise.svg", "browser/base/jar.mn", "browser/components/preferences/config/moreFromMozilla.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/moreFromMozilla.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/moreFromMozilla/browser_moreFromMozilla.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/moreFromMozilla/head.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/moreFromMozilla.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/jar.inc.mn", "browser/themes/shared/preferences/preferences.css", "browser/themes/shared/preferences/solo-ai-logo.svg", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/branding/brandings.ftl"], "git_node": "673144f7a5d7c0f157915424ee6e9647df0fdcd1", "git_parents": ["86136a5faf970e59063cd07b822717f6fd03a958"], "node": "034286ffe0bfa630cce0d4879c26ead7cfcc68d4", "parents": ["0d3cae2fecc47097a51629b29675099ceed72c5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi Lee \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085544 - Fill cc-csc only in frames same-origin with the triggering frame. r=credential-management-reviewers,NeilDeakin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338015\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_iframe_autofill_cc_csc.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/head.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/fixtures/autocomplete_cc_csc_embeded.html", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "334f7cfa82b31bebb3727135e0faded27e1ae5d5", "git_parents": ["673144f7a5d7c0f157915424ee6e9647df0fdcd1"], "node": "5359471cfcebf97f0a3c275d3c23cfdd86cdc923", "parents": ["034286ffe0bfa630cce0d4879c26ead7cfcc68d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087016 - Document reusing existing tasks with mach try. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337922\n", "files": ["tools/tryselect/docs/existing-tasks.md", "tools/tryselect/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "971830b72b3f666f53c9d9d67443b4ebc8fa0da4", "git_parents": ["334f7cfa82b31bebb3727135e0faded27e1ae5d5"], "node": "6a024a3922eff984a0df9dd82e7f021f95465c25", "parents": ["5359471cfcebf97f0a3c275d3c23cfdd86cdc923"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087019 - Add options to filter the tasks reused by mach try --use-existing-tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nThis allows e.g. reusing docker images and toolchains from a previous push\nwhile still running builds and tests, when a change would otherwise rebuild\nevery image and toolchain.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337923\n", "files": ["tools/tryselect/docs/existing-tasks.md", "tools/tryselect/task_config.py", "tools/tryselect/test/test_task_configs.py"], "git_node": "6b6bbcdef9007d0d4166ce08bf6723b0476aa905", "git_parents": ["971830b72b3f666f53c9d9d67443b4ebc8fa0da4"], "node": "71b6ee0d91495d5aa258018c3b366c37b7ff350d", "parents": ["6a024a3922eff984a0df9dd82e7f021f95465c25"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087017 - Show the unparsable value in the mach try --use-existing-tasks error. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337924\n", "files": ["tools/tryselect/task_config.py"], "git_node": "deba32c0ee3e3cd2954e2e13aefbc8e709babf58", "git_parents": ["6b6bbcdef9007d0d4166ce08bf6723b0476aa905"], "node": "95f4ac833b06e323c83b8bddde808219cbe61d4d", "parents": ["71b6ee0d91495d5aa258018c3b366c37b7ff350d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087017 - Allow mach try --use-existing-tasks to use the latest push to a project. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337925\n", "files": ["tools/tryselect/docs/existing-tasks.md", "tools/tryselect/task_config.py", "tools/tryselect/test/test_task_configs.py"], "git_node": "9756c6a371b04abf76afae446536b3aa8e04f111", "git_parents": ["deba32c0ee3e3cd2954e2e13aefbc8e709babf58"], "node": "f2c5287ac9710845e82ccf5dc82e8748991bf2ed", "parents": ["95f4ac833b06e323c83b8bddde808219cbe61d4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086347 - Use green for attention color in LWTs r=desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio\n\nWe updated this to use the OS accent color in bug 2067215 but we're\ngetting reports that there isn't always good contrast. Reverting back to\nthe hard-coded green for LWTs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337999\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/browser-colors.css"], "git_node": "f4d2d4cb760982eed5128566a77c4200250780d3", "git_parents": ["9756c6a371b04abf76afae446536b3aa8e04f111"], "node": "73a16f663de59c7de5e5bde40c90fd117b6a6d0b", "parents": ["f2c5287ac9710845e82ccf5dc82e8748991bf2ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087128 - Wait for the tab opening animation before dragging the tab in browser_tab_detach_fullscreen.js, r=tabbrowser-reviewers,kcochrane.\n\nUntil its opening animation runs, the new tab is 0.1px wide, so the synthesized mousedown could hit the tab strip instead; the drag then never started and the task left its tab open.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338025\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_detach_fullscreen.js"], "git_node": "9d1fae9b60437277ea1419ebe24b0cafda8a437c", "git_parents": ["f4d2d4cb760982eed5128566a77c4200250780d3"], "node": "e2d9b670d392cfe6ad1aea13ef68a1c3287a75cf", "parents": ["73a16f663de59c7de5e5bde40c90fd117b6a6d0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1781668 - Wait for the out-of-process iframes to receive their transforms before moving the mouse into them in test_mouse_enterleave_iframe.html, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug.\n\nA native mouse event sent right after an out-of-process iframe loads is\ndispatched in the embedder's process, so the iframe never sees mouseenter and\nthe test times out.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338032\n", "files": ["dom/events/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/events/test/test_mouse_enterleave_iframe.html"], "git_node": "5f0734705807cc990673aa9253c607012fb99191", "git_parents": ["9d1fae9b60437277ea1419ebe24b0cafda8a437c"], "node": "058687410bdf489f2e9d6d8228f58ab008231a19", "parents": ["e2d9b670d392cfe6ad1aea13ef68a1c3287a75cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1775696 - Wait for the popup's first page to load in newFocusedWindow, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug.\n\nnewFocusedWindow returned once the popup had painted, which can be the\ninitial about:blank. A navigation into a window still showing its initial\ndocument doesn't take focus (NavigationShouldTakeFocus), so the second\nlink click in browser_bug1691214.js sometimes never focused the popup.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338033\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/browser.toml", "dom/base/test/head.js"], "git_node": "bd6a8bbceb23def7a44dfe275f604524d6b2b96a", "git_parents": ["5f0734705807cc990673aa9253c607012fb99191"], "node": "1c5ed7aca09fc7e718455c64bfe0b8fbbdb9bb96", "parents": ["058687410bdf489f2e9d6d8228f58ab008231a19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087110 - Wait for the context menu unload to finish before closing the tab in browser_multiselect_tabs_unload_with_beforeunload.js, r=tabbrowser-reviewers,kcochrane.\n\nWhen the beforeunload prompt was dismissed with \"Stay on page\", the test could remove the tab before permitUnload() returned. The tab was then still pending permitUnload, so it closed without the prompt the test was waiting for, and the test timed out.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338034\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_multiselect_tabs_unload_with_beforeunload.js"], "git_node": "8b6401fe42dcf6e1290d0cecbb1a2c147df114f7", "git_parents": ["bd6a8bbceb23def7a44dfe275f604524d6b2b96a"], "node": "e0d761a0fbc4ffcb371ca6d94faed7f52cbcefc6", "parents": ["1c5ed7aca09fc7e718455c64bfe0b8fbbdb9bb96"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085018 - Update to Glean v71.0.0 r=TravisLong,mach-reviewers,android-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe Cargo.lock update and vendoring will follow in a subsequent commit,\nafter appservices is updated as well to avoid multiple versions of Glean\nbeing pulled in.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337591\n", "files": ["Cargo.toml", "gfx/wr/Cargo.lock", "gfx/wr/Cargo.toml", "gradle/libs.versions.toml", "python/sites/mach.txt"], "git_node": "3ccafb6fd432fcbd1453e6f6a349ed13531facd2", "git_parents": ["8b6401fe42dcf6e1290d0cecbb1a2c147df114f7"], "node": "cb62c451a11fa1928eb2e57f4fd31d7a3d9d7088", "parents": ["e0d761a0fbc4ffcb371ca6d94faed7f52cbcefc6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085018 - Update to glean_parser v22.0.1 r=TravisLong,mach-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337592\n", "files": ["third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-20.1.0.dist-info/METADATA", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-20.1.0.dist-info/RECORD", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-20.1.0.dist-info/WHEEL", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-20.1.0.dist-info/entry_points.txt", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-20.1.0.dist-info/licenses/AUTHORS.md", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-20.1.0.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-22.0.1.dist-info/METADATA", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-22.0.1.dist-info/RECORD", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-22.0.1.dist-info/WHEEL", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-22.0.1.dist-info/entry_points.txt", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-22.0.1.dist-info/licenses/AUTHORS.md", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser-22.0.1.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser/go_server.py", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser/javascript.py", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser/javascript_server.py", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser/lint.py", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser/metrics.py", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser/schemas/metrics.2-0-0.schema.yaml", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser/templates/go_server.jinja2", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser/templates/javascript_server.jinja2", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser/templates/kotlin.jinja2", "third_party/python/glean_parser/glean_parser/templates/swift.jinja2", "third_party/python/pyproject.toml", "third_party/python/requirements.txt", "third_party/python/uv.lock", "third_party/python/uv.lock.hash"], "git_node": "ed82f11f55225390a496288931f326809babf5f0", "git_parents": ["3ccafb6fd432fcbd1453e6f6a349ed13531facd2"], "node": "fbb3b5f6aaf0167be2b650dbf42213e04cdf6e30", "parents": ["cb62c451a11fa1928eb2e57f4fd31d7a3d9d7088"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085018 - Vendor latest appservices r=bdk\n\nDone via:\n\n    ./mach vendor third_party/application-services/moz.yaml\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337904\n", "files": ["third_party/application-services/components/places/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/components/support/error/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/megazords/full/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/megazords/full/src/lib.rs", "third_party/application-services/megazords/ios-rust/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/megazords/ios-rust/Package.resolved", "third_party/application-services/moz.yaml", "third_party/application-services/tools/sdk_generator.sh"], "git_node": "5783fecc3bff2de7dff3a51e76f1d5803a92f277", "git_parents": ["ed82f11f55225390a496288931f326809babf5f0"], "node": "0783ab13fb8dccb819672979b138700894fc21cc", "parents": ["fbb3b5f6aaf0167be2b650dbf42213e04cdf6e30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085018 - Update the Glean Rust dependency & vendor them in r=TravisLong,supply-chain-reviewers\n\nNow with updated and deduplicated Glean.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337905\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/glean-build/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/glean-build/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/glean-build/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/glean-core/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/glean-core/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/glean-core/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/glean-core/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/glean-core/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/glean-core/src/glean.udl", "third_party/rust/glean-core/src/metrics/labeled.rs", "third_party/rust/glean-core/tests/labeled.rs", "third_party/rust/glean-core/tests/metrics_sync.rs", "third_party/rust/glean-sym/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/glean-sym/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/glean-sym/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/glean-sym/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/glean-sym/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/glean-sym/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/glean/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/glean/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/glean/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/glean/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/glean/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/glean/tests/schema.rs"], "git_node": "249ace21720d628838dc02c93d06a3b1f87debdc", "git_parents": ["5783fecc3bff2de7dff3a51e76f1d5803a92f277"], "node": "92988aa56584fa707f9d58b1ea2d261e7486f05e", "parents": ["0783ab13fb8dccb819672979b138700894fc21cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Erik Rediger \u003cjrediger@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085018 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to 723ccb82acf461404d8243a3ad231d7c6fa9d2f3 r=release-managers,android-build-system-reviewers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337975\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "7a0a9f76ef295cbc84464bedc77330f019b99c95", "git_parents": ["249ace21720d628838dc02c93d06a3b1f87debdc"], "node": "7022a0f8219cff6ee02af79530e22ae791aefec7", "parents": ["92988aa56584fa707f9d58b1ea2d261e7486f05e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1920615 - Wait for the controls' icons to be decoded before snapshotting in the videocontrols direction tests, r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,mossop.\n\nThe first test page in a content process that hasn't drawn these icons yet has a cold image cache, which is why this failed consistently in the standalone variant (bug 2026600, and bug 1920614 for the video test) and rarely otherwise. The xorigin failures were the same cold image cache failure.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337698\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/widgets/mochitest.toml", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/videocontrols_direction_test.js"], "git_node": "8cfb486aeaff8fda57baee1e496b05d395ca675a", "git_parents": ["7a0a9f76ef295cbc84464bedc77330f019b99c95"], "node": "d314e6a90ee52853f3a9ccac699bb8977c36c9fa", "parents": ["7022a0f8219cff6ee02af79530e22ae791aefec7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2011552 - Wait for the toggle event in test_find.html instead of a single animation frame, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337700\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/test_find.html"], "git_node": "e042ab3d1e07f4126196c0328dbcc9d82b328758", "git_parents": ["8cfb486aeaff8fda57baee1e496b05d395ca675a"], "node": "508a61dbfbbbe77639ec7a750b50b582aa793106", "parents": ["d314e6a90ee52853f3a9ccac699bb8977c36c9fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086758 - Let window.find() scroll before calling scroll(0, 0) in test_bug1659276.html, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug.\n\nSince bug 2006040, window.find() scrolls to the match from a later task, which\noverrode the test's scroll(0, 0) whenever it ran in a top-level viewport, as\nin the standalone jobs. The test now waits for that scroll after each find,\nso it still checks only that the editor does not scroll after execCommand.\nThis removes the standalone skip-if added in bug 2026600.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337710\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/tests/mochitest.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/test_bug1659276.html"], "git_node": "75c09106949e7ef7a3e9aa17d934f86e345e2390", "git_parents": ["e042ab3d1e07f4126196c0328dbcc9d82b328758"], "node": "c40fe10a740cbdc0e893e5abc9ee124a77a83ae2", "parents": ["508a61dbfbbbe77639ec7a750b50b582aa793106"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086934 - Run the Android lint tasks on 30 core workers r=linter-reviewers,jcristau,marco\n\nThe Android lint tasks are limited by CPU. On try, android-components\nlints takes 279s on 30 cores instead of 549s on 8, and fenix lints 461s\ninstead of 633s.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337862\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint-android.yml"], "git_node": "ec6bd913043e52c05ad065250bcc82173c3edb34", "git_parents": ["75c09106949e7ef7a3e9aa17d934f86e345e2390"], "node": "8ec332717a5eb4f51e52eb8ffac4ead8ee5faf59", "parents": ["c40fe10a740cbdc0e893e5abc9ee124a77a83ae2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087165 - Remove the android-expired-strings linter r=android-reviewers,nalexander\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338052\n", "files": ["docs/code-quality/lint/linters/android-expired-strings.md", "mobile/android/fenix/docs/Working-with-Strings.md", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint.yml", "tools/lint/android-expired-strings.yml", "tools/lint/android-expired-strings/__init__.py", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/example/src/main/java/AcFile.kt", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/example/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/AliasedImport.kt", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/Bad.kt", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/Good.kt", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/Shadow.kt", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/bad_layout.xml", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/good_layout.xml", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/TestFile.kt", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/fenix/lint-baseline.xml", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/FocusFile.kt", "tools/lint/test/files/android-expired-strings/mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "tools/lint/test/python.toml", "tools/lint/test/test_android_expired_strings.py"], "git_node": "f52b67e07a134313dbcf29cfc1ac7b4e274712e1", "git_parents": ["ec6bd913043e52c05ad065250bcc82173c3edb34"], "node": "7bdd9480288296f39781f014a295962bf130adb5", "parents": ["8ec332717a5eb4f51e52eb8ffac4ead8ee5faf59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086842 - Dirty mOptions on HTMLSelectElement's unlink. r=webidl,jjaschke\n\nThe problem here is that we unlink the DOM, unbind all the options, but\nmOptions ends up with a cached element in mElements, and lazy state.\n\nThat's not an issue usually because the content list unlink is about to\nrun, but some callers can still call into mOptions (e.g.\nFieldSetDisabledChanged() etc).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337926\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/forms/the-select-element/option-fieldset-disabled-crash.html"], "git_node": "3bb62c321017415a64584243392736765512bcec", "git_parents": ["f52b67e07a134313dbcf29cfc1ac7b4e274712e1"], "node": "01910d5512bfe6e06f72a4db7ff6be09dbf32d90", "parents": ["7bdd9480288296f39781f014a295962bf130adb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084343 - Add a component to detect app reinstalls. r=Roger,android-reviewers,android-build-system-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336013\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml", "mobile/android/android-components/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/installation-blockstore/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/installation-blockstore/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/installation-blockstore/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/installation-blockstore/src/main/java/mozilla/components/lib/installation/blockstore/InstallBlockStore.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/installation-blockstore/src/test/java/mozilla/components/lib/installation/blockstore/InstallBlockStoreTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/installation-blockstore/src/test/resources/robolectric.properties", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md", "taskcluster/config.yml"], "git_node": "bb080ae3ebb7185e05a4d3777228cd2bd6beb8b1", "git_parents": ["3bb62c321017415a64584243392736765512bcec"], "node": "2d16f0afd28bb726a3eb50e8cdc267d01659107d", "parents": ["01910d5512bfe6e06f72a4db7ff6be09dbf32d90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084344 - Check whether fenix is being reinstalled. r=Roger,android-reviewers,android-build-system-reviewers,sfamisa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336014\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/build.gradle", "mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Analytics.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallationMetricsService.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallationWorker.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallationMetricsServiceTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallationWorkerTest.kt"], "git_node": "cb58cb11d639cf84a5cb75f0d14d9511eb2e25cf", "git_parents": ["bb080ae3ebb7185e05a4d3777228cd2bd6beb8b1"], "node": "94f77666f8106d51d488a4552131985ded30613d", "parents": ["2d16f0afd28bb726a3eb50e8cdc267d01659107d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084346 - Add telemetry for fenix reinstalls. r=Roger,android-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336015\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/pings.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallationWorker.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallationWorkerTest.kt"], "git_node": "2fb24f749be36ac10138101f9ce1a265ff0cae86", "git_parents": ["cb58cb11d639cf84a5cb75f0d14d9511eb2e25cf"], "node": "ad4bea5dda4f211c2630ad0628863f6f74ede6b7", "parents": ["94f77666f8106d51d488a4552131985ded30613d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079858: Improve handling of line-clamp containers with descendants with margins. r=layout-reviewers,AlaskanEmily\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336752\n", "files": ["layout/generic/BlockReflowState.h", "layout/generic/ReflowInput.h", "layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.h", "layout/generic/nsBlockReflowContext.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-063.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-with-ruby-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-064.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-065.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-auto-066.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-auto-064-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-auto-065-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/line-clamp-auto-066-ref.html"], "git_node": "34d554423061a596e22bfcfe940c7b7bd69a1064", "git_parents": ["2fb24f749be36ac10138101f9ce1a265ff0cae86"], "node": "e0d6680c445427e4973cd3d9b37850033b0beb65", "parents": ["ad4bea5dda4f211c2630ad0628863f6f74ede6b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "any1here \u003cany1here@duck.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2013867 - Fix link preview setting UI being hidden entirely instead of only the AI feature UI r=yjamora,mkennedy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D285798\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/config/tabs-browsing.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/tests/aiFeatures/browser_aiFeatures_visibility.js"], "git_node": "c6d8bae2101eeea801941d97ee861a4c85540a8b", "git_parents": ["34d554423061a596e22bfcfe940c7b7bd69a1064"], "node": "7435ae2f354401958596c719da731c5384c53d8a", "parents": ["e0d6680c445427e4973cd3d9b37850033b0beb65"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2085544 - Fill cc-csc only in frames same-origin with the triggering frame. r=credential-management-reviewers,NeilDeakin\" for causing failures at browser_iframe_autofill_cc_csc.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 334f7cfa82b31bebb3727135e0faded27e1ae5d5.\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_iframe_autofill_cc_csc.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/head.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/fixtures/autocomplete_cc_csc_embeded.html", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "731bc025b99cf6b57639b9b4c8bc1181e866fd8c", "git_parents": ["c6d8bae2101eeea801941d97ee861a4c85540a8b"], "node": "cfcddbafe282841f25d9670cd6bd334f855c86c0", "parents": ["7435ae2f354401958596c719da731c5384c53d8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sarah Khan \u003cskhan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1962118 - Part 1: Unsubscribe before invoking the block in waitForSelectedOrDefaultSearchEngine r=android-reviewers,Roger\n\nStore.dispatch notifies its subscribers synchronously, so a block that\ndispatches an action re-enters this observer while it is still\nsubscribed. search.complete is still true at that point, so the block\nruns a second time.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338004\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/search/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/search/ext/BrowserStore.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/search/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/search/ext/BrowserStoreKtTest.kt"], "git_node": "aed04b49c8d61fa3923e84db781abc00904fa321", "git_parents": ["731bc025b99cf6b57639b9b4c8bc1181e866fd8c"], "node": "2a23b5632e6e924c1a25a34fb406924b7957cc4f", "parents": ["cfcddbafe282841f25d9670cd6bd334f855c86c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sarah Khan \u003cskhan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1962118 - Part 2: Wait for the search engines to load before searching on an external search intent r=android-reviewers,Roger\n\nApplicationSearchMiddleware can populate applicationSearchEngines\n(bookmarks/history/tabs, which have an empty URL template) before\nSetSearchEnginesAction has delivered the real region engines, for\nexample right after an external search intent on a cold start. An\nACTION_SEARCH or ACTION_WEB_SEARCH intent arriving in that window made\nselectedOrDefaultSearchEngine fall through to searchEngines[0] and pick\nan application engine, so buildSearchUrl produced an invalid URL that\nwas loaded and reported as \"Invalid Address\" with the raw query in the\naddress bar.\n\nWait for the search state to finish loading before starting the search.\nThis keeps the user's query instead of dropping it, and search.complete\nis only set by SetSearchEnginesAction, so it gates on exactly the window\nabove.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338005\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/intent/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/intent/processing/TabIntentProcessor.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/intent/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/intent/processing/TabIntentProcessorTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/browser/src/main/java/org/mozilla/samples/browser/DefaultComponents.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/IntentProcessors.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/session/IntentProcessor.kt"], "git_node": "d7fddde7b8c279ff01dd8b3c8dc47d3762f88a94", "git_parents": ["aed04b49c8d61fa3923e84db781abc00904fa321"], "node": "083b9c759d368c958d7ae06404498cff5eef67ef", "parents": ["2a23b5632e6e924c1a25a34fb406924b7957cc4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062773 - Part 1: Require [function] XPIDL interfaces to inherit nsISupports, r=xpcom-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336935\n", "files": ["xpcom/idl-parser/xpidl/xpidl.py"], "git_node": "67133412a1a57981dd0b56dfe9d3fa15f689eb83", "git_parents": ["d7fddde7b8c279ff01dd8b3c8dc47d3762f88a94"], "node": "e6a7658f0aa6e528258967ee67c6ed34cadfea1d", "parents": ["083b9c759d368c958d7ae06404498cff5eef67ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062773 - Part 2: Add a FromFunction method to [function] XPIDL interfaces, r=xpcom-reviewers,mccr8,emilio\n\nThis adds a helper to XPIDL interfaces in a similar manner to the\nimplicit conversions supported in JS from JS function objects into\ninterfaces tagged as [function], like `nsIObserver`, `nsIRunnable`,\nand `mozIStorageCompletionCallback`.\n\nCurrently this requires a name string, which will be used to implement\n`nsINamed` and tag the object for refcount logging, similar to how it is\nhandled by `NS_NewRunnableFunction`. This is not intended as a\nreplacement for `NS_NewRunnableFunction`, but could work as an\nalternative.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336953\n", "files": ["xpcom/base/moz.build", "xpcom/base/nsFunctionInterfaceUtils.cpp", "xpcom/base/nsFunctionInterfaceUtils.h", "xpcom/idl-parser/xpidl/header.py", "xpcom/idl-parser/xpidl/xpidl.py"], "git_node": "876bf8c1e2c3577b0a476cfec4d5c2dae8930fc2", "git_parents": ["67133412a1a57981dd0b56dfe9d3fa15f689eb83"], "node": "d0e9ae11ecb0a6fee804e026f07168780c17c63b", "parents": ["e6a7658f0aa6e528258967ee67c6ed34cadfea1d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042829 - Wait for the new tab to load about:newtab in browser_tab_groups_list.js, r=tabbrowser-reviewers,kcochrane.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338029\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_groups_list.js"], "git_node": "3bfdb186f337359e862df841ed3b05e88dcb24f9", "git_parents": ["876bf8c1e2c3577b0a476cfec4d5c2dae8930fc2"], "node": "2b677db7f92456886d9d035968288b99ccfba0ae", "parents": ["d0e9ae11ecb0a6fee804e026f07168780c17c63b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2067122 - Don't select a closing tab after closing multiselected tabs with the keyboard, r=tabbrowser-reviewers,kcochrane.\n\nremoveMultiSelectedTabs selected the first unpinned tab by index, which counts tabs whose close animation hasn't finished, so it could select a tab being closed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338035\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_multiselect_tabs_close.js"], "git_node": "aa75e5ecc8f8692bfe07a2d99f909177a5660b3d", "git_parents": ["3bfdb186f337359e862df841ed3b05e88dcb24f9"], "node": "5ba16634a100665ff1d68c1bc3ebae8639f10e23", "parents": ["2b677db7f92456886d9d035968288b99ccfba0ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086665 - Show the plain Picture of the Day tile while the image loads. r=reemhamz\n\nSince bug 2071112, the sunrise placeholder briefly appeared on every New Tab that skipped preloading. It now appears only when there\u2019s no picture to show. While a picture loads, the widget shows a plain tile without flashing alt text, as requested in bug 2086665 comment 2. This removes the loading placeholder from bug 2071112 but keeps its alt-text fix.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337661\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/PictureOfTheDay/_PictureOfTheDay.scss"], "git_node": "d5ee743ef00888b1ee0eeb9e82f82fb22002805b", "git_parents": ["aa75e5ecc8f8692bfe07a2d99f909177a5660b3d"], "node": "8a26d359a6976139b8b628d401e0305631918140", "parents": ["5ba16634a100665ff1d68c1bc3ebae8639f10e23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sajid Anwar \u003csajidanwar94@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086966 - Use canonical value for sign(). r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338018\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/generics/calc.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/geometry/DOMMatrix-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/signs-abs-computed.html"], "git_node": "96b56997154844df5bfad024f674ba6262f65300", "git_parents": ["d5ee743ef00888b1ee0eeb9e82f82fb22002805b"], "node": "6945e7c611026868a83da7ada9b69ed14b0b3529", "parents": ["8a26d359a6976139b8b628d401e0305631918140"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061474 - Murder JSAutoStructuredCloneBuffer in cold blood r=asuth,spidermonkey-reviewers,dom-storage-reviewers,jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317215\n", "files": ["dom/base/StructuredCloneBlob.cpp", "dom/base/StructuredCloneHolder.cpp", "dom/base/StructuredCloneHolder.h", "dom/indexedDB/IDBObjectStore.cpp", "dom/ipc/ClonedErrorHolder.cpp", "dom/ipc/StructuredCloneData.cpp", "js/public/StructuredClone.h", "js/src/builtin/TestingFunctions.cpp", "js/src/fuzz-tests/testStructuredCloneReader.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testMappedArrayBuffer.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testStructuredClone.cpp", "js/src/vm/StructuredClone.cpp"], "git_node": "33b533c68eb35f18fa5b12ccd4ca235ead216af2", "git_parents": ["96b56997154844df5bfad024f674ba6262f65300"], "node": "e5bc47b185d7ddb035e14c8a3ac30320398ffe4a", "parents": ["6945e7c611026868a83da7ada9b69ed14b0b3529"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061824 - Remove version parameter from JS_ReadStructuredClone r=asuth,spidermonkey-reviewers,dom-storage-reviewers,jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317216\n", "files": ["dom/base/StructuredCloneHolder.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/ActorsParent.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IDBObjectStore.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/SchemaUpgrades.cpp", "js/public/StructuredClone.h", "js/public/friend/ErrorNumbers.msg", "js/src/builtin/TestingFunctions.cpp", "js/src/fuzz-tests/testStructuredCloneReader.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testMappedArrayBuffer.cpp", "js/src/jsapi-tests/testStructuredClone.cpp", "js/src/vm/StructuredClone.cpp"], "git_node": "d4d2e002e92a9bc89fffb7be3e963c458a784f7a", "git_parents": ["33b533c68eb35f18fa5b12ccd4ca235ead216af2"], "node": "69b7ee1d1cfb87ae6ea3a37daec0d26b493053d3", "parents": ["e5bc47b185d7ddb035e14c8a3ac30320398ffe4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061903 - Store structured clone version with the data and error out on unknown version when reading r=asuth\n\nAlso bump the version, for good measure. I don't think this is actually\nnecessary? An older browser reading this new format will see it as an invalid\nscope value and reject it. A newer browser reading a version 8 clone with no\nembedded version number will read it as version 0, which is already treated as\n\"legacy\" and will work. Still, it seems cleaner to bump the version 8 -\u003e 9.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317217\n", "files": ["dom/base/StructuredCloneHolder.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/DBSchema.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/DBSchema.h", "dom/indexedDB/SchemaUpgrades.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/test/unit/test_connection_idle_maintenance_stop.js", "js/public/StructuredClone.h", "js/public/friend/ErrorNumbers.msg", "js/src/vm/StructuredClone.cpp"], "git_node": "71c4e895bca33908c4bae92d4c3e01d3de561289", "git_parents": ["d4d2e002e92a9bc89fffb7be3e963c458a784f7a"], "node": "fbf22c02298b51a456377e5f2305bb3157aaac01", "parents": ["69b7ee1d1cfb87ae6ea3a37daec0d26b493053d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061905 - Remove the single user of mVersion, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317219\n", "files": ["toolkit/modules/sessionstore/SessionHistory.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e1498bec285f396c027a30154455cb5cd8c53d2e", "git_parents": ["71c4e895bca33908c4bae92d4c3e01d3de561289"], "node": "ee0680cc3455425a8300c13d0d1c064186f205df", "parents": ["fbf22c02298b51a456377e5f2305bb3157aaac01"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061905 - Remove structured clone version from the IDL, now that it is checked internally, r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug,saschanaz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317220\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsStructuredCloneContainer.cpp", "dom/interfaces/base/nsIStructuredCloneContainer.idl", "dom/notification/Notification.cpp", "toolkit/modules/sessionstore/SessionHistory.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "3cef7e8c27daa4eb19c94460ccb1cd522c108204", "git_parents": ["e1498bec285f396c027a30154455cb5cd8c53d2e"], "node": "18adad0b5e38fc2ab0818b75bec9872e5e20a516", "parents": ["ee0680cc3455425a8300c13d0d1c064186f205df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Steve Fink \u003csfink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061905 - Stop externally tracking structured clone data version now that it is stored internally, r=asuth,extension-reviewers,robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317221\n", "files": ["dom/base/StructuredCloneBlob.cpp", "dom/base/StructuredCloneHolder.cpp", "dom/base/StructuredCloneHolder.h", "dom/ipc/ClonedErrorHolder.cpp", "dom/ipc/StructuredCloneData.cpp", "dom/ipc/StructuredCloneData.h", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/AddonManagerStartup.cpp"], "git_node": "e5de2119465ded21fd1b026c23835068b5508a2c", "git_parents": ["3cef7e8c27daa4eb19c94460ccb1cd522c108204"], "node": "b7f2d8059506b7a30bf55934561c9c2b9d3e435b", "parents": ["18adad0b5e38fc2ab0818b75bec9872e5e20a516"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084892 - Navigate to the homepage only when the selected tab's URL changes to about:home r=npoon\n\nAboutHomeBinding stops observing the store when the app goes to the background and starts again on resume, when the current URL was handled as if it had just changed.\nWith an about:home tab selected, every resume navigated to the homepage again, dismissing the menu opened over it.\n\nNow we'll also require an URL change for the navigation to happen.\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/407\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/AboutHomeBinding.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/AboutHomeBindingTest.kt"], "git_node": "503229dd4a3d354d44f2d125ed45af8b363a6a35", "git_parents": ["e5de2119465ded21fd1b026c23835068b5508a2c"], "node": "d7d1e3fec4865a0990fa75a6625a4bac0f3bcd54", "parents": ["b7f2d8059506b7a30bf55934561c9c2b9d3e435b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077172 - Remove the network_access_on_socket_process pref and the socketprocess_networking test mode. r=necko-reviewers,webcompat-reviewers,extension-reviewers,application-update-reviewers,credential-management-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,sessionstore-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,profiler-reviewers,dom-storage-reviewers,omc-reviewers,sidebar-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,mconley,sthompson,jsudiaman,jhirsch,chumphreys,emilio,bomsy,cdupuis,canova,twisniewski,rpl,valentin,dimi,jari,aminomancer,ahal\n\nAlso make test_trr_pb_telemetry wait for the TRR response size metric and raise the test_httpssvc_ech_with_alpn.js timeout on Android debug.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331033\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/browser-about/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/browser-contextMenu/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/browser-fullscreen/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/browser-performance/browser.to