ker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nCompiling a wasm module is handled the same regardless of phase,\nso this merges the two functions into one. The difference is whether\nor not we automatically link and evaluate the modules, which is done for\nevaluation phase, but not for source phase.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334957\n", "files": ["dom/script/ModuleLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/workers/loader/WorkerModuleLoader.cpp", "dom/worklet/loader/WorkletModuleLoader.cpp", "js/public/Modules.h", "js/src/shell/ModuleLoader.cpp", "js/src/vm/Modules.cpp"], "git_node": "d3ecb63ebdd28c75a9f9f4438c515bacc8dbd4a8", "git_parents": ["4bd0f7e4471f451ac224ab35d3be5cae0936b121"], "node": "fa6a55bfeafcdda53d2863bbf15f579a5f134fe9", "parents": ["ca863191ba14f8f5d919de92761d2a082a09b464"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Minor \u003cdminor@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030454 - Split out helper functions from GetImports(); r=rhunt\n\nThese will be reused when implementing WasmModuleExecute.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334958\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmJS.cpp"], "git_node": "0f10a616795d3e9131e89bf8e6c06fd56dde4667", "git_parents": ["d3ecb63ebdd28c75a9f9f4438c515bacc8dbd4a8"], "node": "4f918c1fe66cc9165fb3422af9243fb692b4c2b6", "parents": ["fa6a55bfeafcdda53d2863bbf15f579a5f134fe9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Minor \u003cdminor@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030454 - Expose Module APIs for use by WasmModuleExecute; r=arai\n\nMaking these public allows us to call them from WasmJS.cpp, rather\nthan having to define WasmModuleExecute here, which would require\na larger refactoring.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334959\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/ModuleObject.cpp", "js/src/builtin/ModuleObject.h", "js/src/vm/Modules.cpp", "js/src/vm/Modules.h"], "git_node": "1affdc57d8a2f1ba2e248b0dd18474aa2d6604f5", "git_parents": ["0f10a616795d3e9131e89bf8e6c06fd56dde4667"], "node": "7c4043fa345bef0f517061839dddfaf99a9b9a2c", "parents": ["4f918c1fe66cc9165fb3422af9243fb692b4c2b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Minor \u003cdminor@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030454 - Add initWasmExportBindings; r=arai\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334960\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/ModuleObject.cpp", "js/src/builtin/ModuleObject.h"], "git_node": "5b5454215cf2971ea7946c8173ec70a581250bca", "git_parents": ["1affdc57d8a2f1ba2e248b0dd18474aa2d6604f5"], "node": "efea75835987724ae45cb9714e4b42a1fe19e1bc", "parents": ["7c4043fa345bef0f517061839dddfaf99a9b9a2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Minor \u003cdminor@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030454 - Call ensureConstructor in Module::instantiate; r=rhunt\n\nPreviously every path into Module::instantiate went through the\nWebAssembly namespace object, which runs WebAssemblyClassFinish\ndefining all of the prototypes, but WasmModuleExecute will call\ninstantiate from the module loader, meaning the prototypes won't\nbe resolved yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334961\n", "files": ["js/src/wasm/WasmModule.cpp"], "git_node": "43648b2c99e38c4579524f7517b5f7c6f806e973", "git_parents": ["5b5454215cf2971ea7946c8173ec70a581250bca"], "node": "fc1eac7ff3eba651735ae98045352653bbecc24d", "parents": ["efea75835987724ae45cb9714e4b42a1fe19e1bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Minor \u003cdminor@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030454 - Set module private in shell loader; r=arai\n\nThe shell resolves relative specifiers against the referrer's module\nprivate. Wasm modules can now be referrers once their imports are\nloaded, so give them the same script private as JavaScript modules.\nThis wasn't problematic before, because source phase imports don't\nload dependencies.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.se