tative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/wasm/webapi/esm-integration/worker.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/wasm/webapi/esm-integration/worklet-import-source-phase.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "97d9354713dfafe82b4fce9869d6b37cdc1922c8", "git_parents": ["aa2f8236d9fc1fa9f2ce29f8ba3ee9b0fa6b3f05"], "node": "0cf3eb10af4de915300884e82798488d0c2b1a3e", "parents": ["903dbb4f9fdd29683b446c1730b9e05e1ad14b12"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072921 - Keep collecting while the shutdown leak collections are still freeing windows, r=mccr8.\n\nThe parent releases the browsers it keeps alive until shutdown right before broadcasting the collect request and does not wait for the content process, so the runnables that finish tearing their docShells down can still be queued, and can queue more of their own.\n\nA docShell, its outer window and its inner window come apart a level per round, because one CC unlinks the whole group but only a GC drops the reflector's counted reference to the inner window. A fixed number of rounds therefore ends a level short whenever the collections start too early, and the last inner window looks leaked.\n\nRepeat the last round while it still frees windows, which follows the teardown instead of racing it. Inner and outer window destructors notify debug-domwindow-destroyed in debug builds when the DocShellAndDOMWindowLeak log is enabled, which is the case whenever leaks.py checks for leaked windows. DocShells send no such notification, so a round that frees only docShells ends the loop; this relies on a docShell being freed in the same CC as its outer window. The cap, well above the depth of a window group, keeps a process that never settles from holding up the run.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327114\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/ShutdownLeaksCollector.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "90c0d39637f479155437859aed40c405d7be229c", "git_parents": ["97d9354713dfafe82b4fce9869d6b37cdc1922c8"], "node": "1c599bbae29c8a9801c74bca9f98c69323148bcf", "parents": ["0cf3eb10af4de915300884e82798488d0c2b1a3e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086163 - Force a shrinking GC and CC in the privileged about: content process after each newtab browser test, r=ini.\n\nOn slow builds, the privileged about: process spent 4 to 6 s collecting piled-up dead about:newtab windows at the end of a test, overrunning the 5 s check that waits for vsync to be disabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337170\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "dda412b92d74fee6da1e0e563ef90a434659f38e", "git_parents": ["90c0d39637f479155437859aed40c405d7be229c"], "node": "18e207213e7707d76db6d90844771086301b24dd", "parents": ["1c599bbae29c8a9801c74bca9f98c69323148bcf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087630: Show the full menu bar while the Picture-in-Picture player is focused on macOS. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nThe player has no menu bar of its own, so it got a menu bar with only the application menu. It now gets the hidden window's menu bar, which is what Firefox shows when no window is main.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338438\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.h", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm"], "git_node": "7fd9affe20f288206da2a4dba1e9bb57662b77c7", "git_parents": ["dda412b92d74fee6da1e0e563ef90a434659f38e"], "node": "f3bc78744fa60ee782cc5228a1df23ce0d758244", "parents": ["18e207213e7707d76db6d90844771086301b24dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084184: Update custom Dock tiles when the system icon style changes. r=mac-reviewers,mossop,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338222\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsMacDockSupport.mm"], "git_node": "fb1373447da23525661cc88b60ca9749c9a8c079", "git_parents": ["7fd9affe20f288206da2a4dba1e9bb57662b77c7"], "node": "86e2ed4d19cb46f05146b686f9901d98482beddd", "parents": ["f3bc78744fa60ee782cc5228a1df23ce0d758244"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087184: Activate Firefox when the Picture-in-Picture player is clicked on macOS. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nSince bug 1688932 the player is a non-activating window, so clicking it no longer activates Firefox and the menu bar and window management stay with the previously active app. A click into the player now makes it key and activates Firefox, like a click into any other window.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338412\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm"], "git_node": "6371b975daa23a402d758ec4087b875db70b8f67", "git_parents": ["fb1373447da23525661cc88b60ca9749c9a8c079"], "node": "1f3c737972aad82c456f810b6b74e6a7eb2e2865", "parents": ["86e2ed4d19cb46f05146b686f9901d98482beddd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "SVNKVN9 \u003csundaynight.1919@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087495 - Fix inverted IsTextRole() check in ATK editable text callbacks. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,eeejay\n\nBug 1832353 Part 3 inverted the IsTextRole() guard in all six\nAtkEditableText callbacks. Since the EditableText interface is only\nexposed for accessibles where IsTextRole() is true, every call returned\nearly and did nothing. Restore the negation and add an ATK browser test.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338299\n", "files": ["accessible/atk/nsMaiInterfaceEditableText.cpp", "accessible/tests/browser/atk/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/atk/browser_editabletext.js"], "git_node": "ad9e608654767b746c82196bf2de7c867c564498", "git_parents": ["6371b975daa23a402d758ec4087b875db70b8f67"], "node": "0e9ac553b08f9fba4b2c698162c50199d3108483", "parents": ["1f3c737972aad82c456f810b6b74e6a7eb2e2865"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073625 - fix comment and make mContext partially const r=dholbert,firefox-svg-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327606\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "layout/svg/SVGObserverUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "ac4ffb51155729bb3cda97febd9646aeb14a7143", "git_parents": ["ad9e608654767b746c82196bf2de7c867c564498"], "node": "da1bc1de717d9555fe55a56e52f8721d3ece9ace", "parents": ["0e9ac553b08f9fba4b2c698162c50199d3108483"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-bg/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-de/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-en-rGB/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-eu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-fr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-gl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-hsb/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/res/values-hu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/menu/src/main/