ings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-tr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-zh-rTW/strings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-zh-rTW/strings.xml"], "git_node": "0cf45eefa0b5aedf5c76bbf1cbd3cade2ca081c4", "git_parents": ["f5f070711ff95845e3462684d4b76938403e66e3"], "node": "3152e75ec0f6c9acb6e10d8761537d9ee9b35064", "parents": ["50c69d2a476690ab64c44339bc9093c63b4dc422"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Watt \u003cjwatt@jwatt.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021326. Store timeline-scope data on the element instead of in a global array. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nTimelineManager kept one global array entry per element with `timeline-scope`.\nA named timeline lookup did a linear search for every ancestor of the animation\ntarget and for every ancestor of every timeline registered under the name, with\ncost O(depth x timelines x scoping elements).\n\nWe now store the data on a new TimelineScope object owned by the element's\nElementAnimationData, next to its timeline collections, so checks become a\nlookup on the element itself. TimelineManager links the live scopes into a list\nonly so that Disconnect() can destroy them.\n\nA timeline-scope on a pseudo-element is still recorded in the originating\nelement's own slot rather than the pseudo-element's. Bug 2087822 fixes that.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337104\n", "files": ["dom/animation/ElementAnimationData.cpp", "dom/animation/ElementAnimationData.h", "layout/style/GeckoBindings.cpp", "layout/style/TimelineManager.cpp", "layout/style/TimelineManager.h", "layout/style/TimelineScope.cpp", "layout/style/TimelineScope.h", "layout/style/moz.build"], "git_node": "cf3bc05211d6f097e2b6cecd18efc72c2f3bdf36", "git_parents": ["0cf45eefa0b5aedf5c76bbf1cbd3cade2ca081c4"], "node": "15648e0ce20df9ae7c787809fb46ade4b33e665a", "parents": ["3152e75ec0f6c9acb6