e atom marking bitmap is now called the atom reference bitmap r=spidermonkey-reviewers,sfink\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339191\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/TestingFunctions.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-1994871.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-1997896.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2082083.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2084543.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug2010939.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug2045307.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/marked-atoms.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/symbol-description-atom-ref.js"], "git_node": "fbc9d663bb95f6e681f990ff9e79b35b98695e59", "git_parents": ["4e575e90eec19bab0a38e84d55abbe169acf8e93"], "node": "b6aa7802af5899f3f4276fb2b6d243074013c84e", "parents": ["d3fd77535c851b13f9a0c558ba8d9b5328c77d0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083073 - Assert ArrayBufferObject::detach is not called during GC or CC r=spidermonkey-reviewers,sfink\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339211\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/ArrayBufferObject.cpp"], "git_node": "3b90f06c25b362f209bbfc4505847d7a12f06afb", "git_parents": ["fbc9d663bb95f6e681f990ff9e79b35b98695e59"], "node": "d5053c6be1a8eaa937e724cf4345beee8c2dc5f5", "parents": ["b6aa7802af5899f3f4276fb2b6d243074013c84e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085006 - Part 1: Move the node event listener manager list into a reusable NodeOwnedObjectList. r=smaug\n\nNo behavior change. Part 2 puts observers into the same kind of list.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337240\n", "files": ["dom/base/NodeOwnedObjectList.h", "dom/base/moz.build", "dom/base/nsCCUncollectableMarker.cpp", "dom/base/nsCCUncollectableMarker.h", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.h", "dom/base/nsINode.cpp", "dom/events/EventListenerManager.cpp", "dom/events/EventListenerManager.h"], "git_node": "77d0aa82648ac6ee13447d9dfb535cf8b14a1934", "git_parents": ["3b90f06c25b362f209bbfc4505847d7a12f06afb"], "node": "924a629dc9a097f1d8ecc89b5c2d2cc991270c2f", "parents": ["d5053c6be1a8eaa937e724cf4345beee8c2dc5f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085006 - Part 2: Unmark gray the callbacks of observers bound to nodes in live documents. r=smaug\n\nMutation, Resize and Intersection observers are kept alive by the nodes they\nobserve, but unlike event listeners their callbacks were never unmarked gray,\nso the cycle collector traversed everything they keep alive on every run.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337162\n", "files": ["dom/base/DOMIntersectionObserver.cpp", "dom/base/DOMIntersectionObserver.h", "dom/base/ResizeObserver.cpp", "dom/base/ResizeObserver.h", "dom/base/nsCCUncollectableMarker.cpp", "dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.cpp", "dom/base/nsDOMMutationObserver.h"], "git_node": "2c4b30c53e2c08938f9edc5c9a982a2e2fb7d227", "git_parents": ["77d0aa82648ac6ee13447d9dfb535cf8b14a1934"], "node": "d2473f1c4deb5d5b85f6a015c6217e17f6b7c5a0", "parents": ["924a629dc9a097f1d8ecc89b5c2d2cc991270c2f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088440 - Remove mach npm argument '--scripts-prepend-node-path=auto' as it is no longer supported. r=linter-reviewers,perftest-reviewers,sergesanspaille,sparky\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339196\n", "files": ["tools/browsertime/mach_commands.py", "tools/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "3a72f2ad2b45899da9148fb3c036a79bed909d23", "git_parents": ["2c4b30c53e2c08938f9edc5c9a982a2e2fb7d227"], "node": "807fe6a7e7fd186a3eb21b9a3a24ed04e6ef1039", "parents": ["d2473f1c4deb5d5b85f6a015c6217e17f6b7c5a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086759 - Update sidebar motion tokens r=desktop-theme-reviewers,sidebar-reviewers,nsharpley,jules\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337727\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_sidebar_animation.js", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/sidebar.tokens.json"], "git_node": "8890a5d75710e85622088ec96ecb4d4cc9ad5b81", "git_parents": ["3a72f2ad2b45899da9148fb3c036a79bed909d23"], "node": "34ff9a19be27d8e54146867943b7dcfc09b8f1a0", "parents": ["807fe6a7e7fd186a3eb21b9a3a24ed04e6ef1039"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088118 - Bound the provisioning retries in MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nAfter a provisioning attempt, openSession and getKeyRequest are retried\nonce instead of until they succeed, which grew a promise chain without\nbound. The retry also follows a failed provisioning, because another\nactor may have provisioned the device in the meantime.\n\nFailures are no longer remembered, a failed Provision IPC rejects its\nwaiters instead of leaving them pending, and the error code from the\ncontent process is not passed on to the page.\n\nAMEDIA_DRM_RESOURCE_BUSY from openSession is reported as\nQuotaExceededError.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338779\n", "files": ["dom/media/eme/mediadrm/MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent.cpp", "dom/media/eme/mediadrm/MediaDrmRemoteCDMParent.h"], "git_node": "6715376452ed53e7011ea90d77ea1689c847658b", "git_parents": ["8890a5d75710e85622088ec96ecb4d4cc9ad5b81"], "node": "c64796340650aa0b9fca73c4a0166544d713c571", "parents": ["34ff9a19be27d8e54146867943b7dcfc09b8f1a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081780 - Upgrade VRManager assertions to MOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nThese assertions guard critical invariants where violation indicates a programming\nerror that must be caught in all builds, not just debug builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333730\n", "files": ["gfx/vr/VRManager.cpp"], "git_node": "5824e2f509fb835daa9524c2c944ca1938dc600a", "git_parents": ["6715376452ed53e7011ea90d77ea1689c847658b"], "node": "7e19b342d6a82225009a16ce26b7a425db2e7411", "parents": ["c64796340650aa0b9fca73c4a0166544d713c571"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081780 - Upgrade some gfx/vr assertions to MOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nConvert critical assertions in VRServiceHost, VRThread, gfxVRMutex, FxRWindowManager,\nand VRShMem to MOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT to protect:\n- Threading invariants (NS_IsMainThread)\n- Resource validity (GPU process, thread, window, mutex handles)\n- State machine invariants (shared memory state, resource cleanup)\n- Preconditions on public APIs (singleton getters, initialization)\n\nThese assertions guard invariants where violation indicates a programming error that\nmust be caught in all builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333731\n", "files": ["gfx/vr/VRServiceHost.cpp", "gfx/vr/VRShMem.cpp", "gfx/vr/VRThread.cpp", "gfx/vr/gfxVRMutex.h"], "git_node": "d9134491330d23cff94db94c520a92dd47feaef3", "git_parents": ["5824e2f509fb835daa9524c2c944ca1938dc600a"], "node": "fda3475912e51cf0d79648a14336e42184839798", "parents": ["7e19b342d6a82225009a16ce26b7a425db2e7411"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081780 - Upgrade more gfx/vr assertions to MOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nFinal conversions in gfx/vr/ folder:\n- VRShMem.cpp: Mutex and state management assertions (9 conversions)\n- nsFxrCommandLineHandler.cpp: Window/API parameter validation (3 conversions)\n- VRPuppetCommandBuffer.cpp: Singleton init and buffer bounds (3 conversions)\n\nThese protect critical invariants: mutex state, window parameter contracts, array bounds,\nand singleton initialization that must be enforced in all builds.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333732\n", "files": ["gfx/vr/VRPuppetCommandBuffer.cpp", "gfx/vr/VRShMem.cpp"], "git_node": "c790b2a387f52d39fddd52322ae6c5c99eca64c4", "git_parents": ["d9134491330d23cff94db94c520a92dd47feaef3"], "node": "284e4fb8d32cd73f6bb003a225c37967ed70faa1", "parents": ["fda3475912e51cf0d79648a14336e42184839798"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081780 - Upgrade remaining gfx/vr assertions to MOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333733\n", "files": ["gfx/vr/VRManager.cpp", "gfx/vr/VRShMem.cpp", "gfx/vr/VRThread.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRChild.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRGPUChild.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRGPUParent.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRLayerChild.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRManagerChild.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRManagerParent.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRParent.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRProcessChild.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRProcessManager.cpp", "gfx/vr/ipc/VRProcessParent.cpp", "gfx/vr/service/OculusSession.cpp", "gfx/vr/service/OpenVRSession.cpp", "gfx/vr/service/VRService.cpp"], "git_node": "7de9a1e6ff021ab15e7750646cd8dc4e998ec3a7", "git_parents": ["c790b2a387f52d39fddd52322ae6c5c99eca64c4"], "node": "94f9ad4bf3c97108a40ec1c6e9ff87e3613704f1", "parents": ["284e4fb8d32cd73f6bb003a225c37967ed70faa1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elissa Cha \u003cecha@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053495 - Remove the Smart Window mistralRelease pref and legacy model selection paths r=pdahiya,fluent-reviewers,settings-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles,gazhibekova,flod\n\n- Remove browser.smartwindow.mistralRelease, preserving its enabled behavior across Smart Window\n- Remove legacy code, unused strings, and obsolete icons; preserve existing Fluent IDs\n- Update tests and Storybook fixtures for the current models and ordering\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336248\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Utils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_prompt_loader_chat_system_prompt.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/model-choice-1.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/model-choice-2.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/model-choice-3.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/input-model-select/input-model-select.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/input-model-select/input-model-select.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/input-model-select/input-model-select.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/firstrun.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_firstrun.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_smartbar_model_select.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_ChatModelChoice.js", "browser/components/preferences/config/aiFeatures.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/tests/aiFeatures/browser_aiFeatures_smart_window_model_selection.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/aiFeatures/browser_aiFeatures_smart_window_model_selection_custom.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/aiFeatures/browser_aiFeatures_smart_window_model_settings_custom.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/aiFeatures/browser_aiFeatures_smart_window_telemetry.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aiFeatures.ftl", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aiWindow.ftl"], "git_node": "9fe104a7aeaaab9eb521493f41291465d922a257", "git_parents": ["7de9a1e6ff021ab15e7750646cd8dc4e998ec3a7"], "node": "67ae9b1fc86c9b816a3f7f63110a80e10601fcf7", "parents": ["94f9ad4bf3c97108a40ec1c6e9ff87e3613704f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069358 - part 1: Add the source-artifact kind. r=taskgraph-reviewers,ahal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333664\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docs/kinds.md", "taskcluster/kinds/source-artifact/kind.yml"], "git_node": "4f0d6940b55124e128a72c2169aa5384559077de", "git_parents": ["9fe104a7aeaaab9eb521493f41291465d922a257"], "node": "04a4aad740f303ac3245ada2bb59685a9dd4fa99", "parents": ["67ae9b1fc86c9b816a3f7f63110a80e10601fcf7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069360 - part 2: Sign install-firefox.sh with autograph GPG. r=releng-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,ahal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333665\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docs/kinds.md", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/install_script_signing.py", "taskcluster/kinds/install-script-signing/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/source-artifact/kind.yml"], "git_node": "92a73bc31f478edb8ac31c22379a14014c1c1d1d", "git_parents": ["4f0d6940b55124e128a72c2169aa5384559077de"], "node": "633050e0487013453fd5e4ebc7a80efa6457b1bc", "parents": ["04a4aad740f303ac3245ada2bb59685a9dd4fa99"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069358 - part 3: Beetmove install-firefox.sh to linux.firefox.com. r=releng-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,ahal\n\nBeetmover artifact maps now skip empty bucket paths and destinations, so a\nmanifest can publish at the root of a bucket.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333666\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docs/kinds.md", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/manifests/install_script.yml", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/beetmover_install_script.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/util/scriptworker.py", "taskcluster/kinds/beetmover-install-script/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/source-artifact/kind.yml"], "git_node": "e3a774f72655d3b4c162c1f654354e932bff57be", "git_parents": ["92a73bc31f478edb8ac31c22379a14014c1c1d1d"], "node": "99ce5c05ec2e141e71fce1d88288a0083fca9292", "parents": ["633050e0487013453fd5e4ebc7a80efa6457b1bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086521 - Add PDF.js viewer UI performance tests using PDFs with empty pages. r=perftest-reviewers,mozperftest-reviewers,sparky\n\nTalos pdfpaint mixes the viewer startup with the rendering of the first page,\nso most of its subtests measure the startup.\n\nUse empty PDFs to track viewer opening and interaction costs. Record\nopening milestones separately and run interactions in ASAP mode to\nreduce frame pacing delays.\n\nThe opening, scroll, zoom and go-to times alert. The first open and the\nrender delay, too noisy on try, don't.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337603\n", "files": ["python/mozperftest/perfdocs/config.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/linux.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/macosx-aarch64.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/windows11-24h2.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/mozperftest.md", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.build", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/browser_pdfjs_ui_interaction_perf.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/browser_pdfjs_ui_open_perf.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/file_pdfjs_empty_1.pdf", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/file_pdfjs_empty_100.pdf", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/file_pdfjs_empty_1000.pdf", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/head.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/perftest.toml"], "git_node": "09a956508f9784d8bddeaca47861546650102699", "git_parents": ["e3a774f72655d3b4c162c1f654354e932bff57be"], "node": "b3523f5b7ee0917759c5b0c91fc701b4ee634e27", "parents": ["99ce5c05ec2e141e71fce1d88288a0083fca9292"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cristian Tuns \u003cctuns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2086521 - Add PDF.js viewer UI performance tests using PDFs with empty pages. r=perftest-reviewers,mozperftest-reviewers,sparky\" for causing python failures in test_tasks_are_not_scheduled\n\nThis reverts commit 09a956508f9784d8bddeaca47861546650102699.\n", "files": ["python/mozperftest/perfdocs/config.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/linux.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/macosx-aarch64.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/windows11-24h2.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/mozperftest.md", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/moz.build", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/browser_pdfjs_ui_interaction_perf.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/browser_pdfjs_ui_open_perf.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/file_pdfjs_empty_1.pdf", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/file_pdfjs_empty_100.pdf", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/file_pdfjs_empty_1000.pdf", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/head.js", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/perf/perftest.toml"], "git_node": "1f582ab648ccc6fe560329341153a0254c952f3a", "git_parents": ["09a956508f9784d8bddeaca47861546650102699"], "node": "c6f6a1230b04dc24e80ae24491dbb7afe2321975", "parents": ["b3523f5b7ee0917759c5b0c91fc701b4ee634e27"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2025711 - Remove the Smart Window sidebar browser when switching to a classic window, r=Mardak.\"\n\nThis reverts commit f77b6e1096b26fd6544fbb898e5cfe4670f592ab.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "b