rent::mStorageBaseDir with mMutex. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit de3da345cd27e2f22fc9a2014df2c1ced337fc7b.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2081210 - Add gtests for GMP service creation racing the main thread and shutdown. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit b22b147ff424d83aec96cf3df2d89e8b41e83728.\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPService.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPService.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceChild.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceChild.h", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.cpp", "dom/media/gmp/GMPServiceParent.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestGMPServiceCreation.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "ef9c63e8655f23bae7194d0e00f6f45ce019f73e", "git_parents": ["6fb008f079bf4141ae7d3fb641c0fc91ffa51683"], "node": "758d11974b933e89f19805996f400c6f42fbbf42", "parents": ["958756b0d3cd0948db4111a913ee33ef4e5eb162"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Atila Butkovits \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2088559 - Update New Tab Recent Activity for Nova. r=thecount\" for causing failures at browser_parsable_css.js.\n\nThis reverts commit e2dbad7b3b0dc7c0cae4b5737c4a85d91a6e390e.\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Card/Card.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Card/_Card.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/Highlights/_Highlights.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Sections/Sections.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/lib/utils.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/HighlightsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PrefsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_highlights_section.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Card.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Sections.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/lib/utils.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/PrefsFeed.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_HighlightsFeed.js"], "git_node": "08532a0e0eae8334ca32446607fb7ae691760f60", "git_parents": ["ef9c63e8655f23bae7194d0e00f6f45ce019f73e"], "node": "f637024cacc4a1a7a3e6f088e2699feebc6513f5", "parents": ["758d11974b933e89f19805996f400c6f42fbbf42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072661 - Observe the browsing mode in BaseBrowserFragment.onViewCreated r=android-reviewers,jonalmeida\n\nMoving the only private tab to a normal tab selects the new normal tab, then removes the private tab. The browsing mode used to be updated inside observeTabSelection's collector, alongside dismissing dialogs and the rest of the tab-selection handling. HomepageTabBinding could see the new state while the mode was still private, find no private tabs, and open a private homepage tab over the migrated tab.\n\nThe browsing mode is now updated by its own BrowsingModeObserver binding, so it follows the selected tab without waiting on the rest of the tab-selection handling, which stays in observeTabSelection.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337268\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BaseBrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/browsingmode/BrowsingModeObserver.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BrowserFragmentTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/browsingmode/BrowsingModeObserverTest.kt"], "git_node": "255dc0f0ed32571dfea6534d4ac1764103f14005", "git_parents": ["08532a0e0eae8334ca32446607fb7ae691760f60"], "node": "18d58779e1dbb5e5962f82be1b02dc9112d26d29", "parents": ["f637024cacc4a1a7a3e6f088e2699feebc6513f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088431 - Use moz-src for security/ r=geckoview-reviewers,settings-reviewers,sandbox-reviewers,remote-settings-reviewers,akulyk,bobowen,leplatrem,tcampbell\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339088\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-siteIdentity.js", "browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/base/content/pageinfo/security.js", "browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/components/preferences/tests/credentials/browser_cert_export.js", "dom/webauthn/tests/u2futil.js", "mobile/shared/chrome/geckoview/geckoview.js", "mobile/shared/modules/geckoview/GeckoViewProgress.sys.mjs", "security/manager/pki/moz.build", "security/manager/pki/resources/content/certManager.js", "security/manager/pki/resources/content/downloadcert.js", "security/manager/pki/resources/content/exceptionDialog.js", "security/manager/pki/resources/content/load_device.js", "security/manager/ssl/RemoteSecuritySettings.sys.mjs", "security/manager/ssl/X509.sys.mjs", "security/manager/ssl/components.conf", "security/manager/ssl/moz.build", "security/manager/ssl/tests/mochitest/browser/browser_certViewer.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/head_psm.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_blocklist_onecrl.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_cert_storage.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_crlite_filters.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_der.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_intermediate_preloads.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_onecrl_loads_bundle.js", "security/manager/ssl/tests/unit/test_qwacs.js", "services/settings/docs/index.md", "taskcluster/docker/periodic-updates/scripts/getHSTSPreloadList.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json", "tools/lint/extra-js-modules/allowlist.txt"], "git_node": "28bb388fd4f9fed5b40d06a24d3286d68cb33fb8", "git_parents": ["255dc0f0ed32571dfea6534d4ac1764103f14005"], "node": "115d409366b70fc2ae056f148ac5131ca2f0d609", "parents": ["18d58779e1dbb5e5962f82be1b02dc9112d26d29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gela \u003cgmalekpour@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085145 - Add CVV field to CreditCardsAddresses objct in the Kotlin layer r=android-reviewers,sfamisa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336290\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/storage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/storage/CreditCardsAddressesStorage.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/sync-autofill/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/sync/autofill/AutofillCreditCardsAddressesStorage.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/sync-autofill/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/sync/autofill/Types.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/sync-autofill/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/sync/autofill/AutofillCreditCardsAddressesStorageTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/docs/changelog.md"], "git_node": "c2c95c9d9244a6cacbc6aea1d529230ea7bf1814", "git_parents": ["28bb388fd4f9fed5b40d06a24d3286d68cb33fb8"], "node": "284bc790ef9fb128b486024dc70cf81169c79ce8", "parents": ["115d409366b70fc2ae056f148ac5131ca2f0d609"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072806: Abort AITab generation when the chat stop button is clicked r=omarg,mzhang,ai-platform-reviewers,thasan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333286\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/AITab.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/openAIEngine.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab_generation.js", "toolkit/components/ml/actors/MLEngineChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/actors/MLEngineParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/content/backends/OpenAIPipeline.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/MLTestUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_engine_lifetime.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_openai.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "f8b5c29bfebf37840b274b48fe3690cc039bc0b2", "git_parents": ["c2c95c9d9244a6cacbc6aea1d529230ea7bf1814"], "node": "7a8c47e5e6f24a1e0e5e0bca5bc4287fe75532dc", "parents": ["284bc790ef9fb128b486024dc70cf81169c79ce8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2078808 - Make AboutHomeBinding take selected tab url and destination fragment id into account r=android-reviewers,gl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336891\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/AboutHomeBinding.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/AboutHomeBindingTest.kt"], "git_node": "cc1cc02d8ac5631c15d751891306c754f6eeef0d", "git_parents": ["f8b5c29bfebf37840b274b48fe3690cc039bc0b2"], "node": "fc422837027bb65efb3f00e7a2533c045102e2f9", "parents": ["7a8c47e5e6f24a1e0e5e0bca5bc4287fe75532dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088675 - Draw sequence diagrams at their layout size. r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339292\n", "files": ["docs/_static/mermaid_fixups.js", "docs/conf.py"], "git_node": "1214e35d8fc18003d2557cd57bb1db0403102656", "git_parents": ["cc1cc02d8ac5631c15d751891306c754f6eeef0d"], "node": "efc548467ba6ba5c49394948dc86ec1d15f056d0", "parents": ["fc422837027bb65efb3f00e7a2533c045102e2f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061888 - Add Resource Monitor to Firefox Labs r=nimbus-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,beth\n\nAdds a resourceMonitor Nimbus feature whose enabled variable setPrefs\nbrowser.resourceMonitor.enabled, plus the Labs title/description strings,\nso the pref can be flipped from about:preferences#experimental ahead of\na broader rollout.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D329295\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/firefoxlabs/features.ftl"], "git_node": "f28e0cde67ad2fc08719d113376beca549694e57", "git_parents": ["1214e35d8fc18003d2557cd57bb1db0403102656"], "node": "1a279faeb6cb09e9cb21e9603141bf17a750b89e", "parents": ["efc548467ba6ba5c49394948dc86ec1d15f056d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086859 - Refactor the updating of existing CSSAnimation with new properties. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nThis makes `BuildAnimation()` slightly simpler, and decouples the update\nof the existing animation and the timeline name map.\n\nBesides, in order to fix this bug, we may have to cache the old\nanimation-play-state in CSSAnimation, so moving the update of properties\ninto CSSAnimation class makes more sense.\n\nNo behavior change in this patch.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338475\n", "files": ["dom/animation/CSSAnimation.cpp", "dom/animation/CSSAnimation.h", "layout/style/nsAnimationManager.cpp"], "git_node": "5b1cc0111348e85252239af6ec9cd607d2bb0574", "git_parents": ["f28e0cde67ad2fc08719d113376beca549694e57"], "node": "8182608a5f02fdc9afb309bd96334ae8f62a063c", "parents": ["1a279faeb6cb09e9cb21e9603141bf17a750b89e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086859 - Cache animation-play-state for checking if we have to play or pause when mutating the CSSAnimation. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nIt's unfortunate we have to cache this value because we cannot use\n`Animation::PlayState()` to check if we mutate animation-play-state.\n\nAfter we introduce null or non-monotonically increasing timelines,\nit is not guaranteed that `animation-play-state:paused` aligns with\n`AnimationPlayState::Paused`. Also, any further changes in SetTimeline()\nmay have side effects on it, so we should cache the style instead, to\nmake sure that we don't play or pause the animation by accident.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338476\n", "files": ["dom/animation/CSSAnimation.cpp", "dom/animation/CSSAnimation.h", "dom/animation/ComputedTiming.h", "layout/style/nsAnimationManager.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/css/animation-timeline-ignored.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "e3c372dfe9cdc5bf3f205963b5340955e08208af", "git_parents": ["5b1cc0111348e85252239af6ec9cd607d2bb0574"], "node": "5c2ff5881144f7cbea5f9dd4e213f1987a02ee85", "parents": ["8182608a5f02fdc9afb309bd96334ae8f62a063c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrej Glavic \u003caglavic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088059 - Remove stale temporary workarounds from the perf test harnesses. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nThese workarounds were marked as temporary, but the bugs they waited on are\nresolved or will not be fixed:\n\n- Stop disabling the Base Profiler in talos profiling runs (bug 1648324).\n- Drop the WebExtension-only `-cold` test name suffix in raptor (bug 1644344).\n- Drop the temporary python version check in the mozharness talos script.\n- Drop the stale removal TODOs in the AWSY tests.\n- Explain why the window recorder stays disabled on Android instead of calling\n  it temporary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338744\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/mobile.yml", "testing/awsy/awsy/test_base_memory_usage.py", "testing/awsy/awsy/test_memory_usage.py", "testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/testing/talos.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/manifest.py", "testing/talos/talos/gecko_profile.py"], "git_node": "3ad0d1f9850314ac76966011c625fecfbea59da1", "git_parents": ["e3c372dfe9cdc5bf3f205963b5340955e08208af"], "node": "86d65a1c8b6acb33df9f773f45c15b3089d55c87", "parents": ["5c2ff5881144f7cbea5f9dd4e213f1987a02ee85"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrej Glavic \u003caglavic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1943978 - Move the nonmain_startup_fileio notes into the xperf section of the talos docs. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338478\n", "files": ["testing/perfdocs/generated/talos.md", "testing/talos/perfdocs/index.md"], "git_node": "b9fe2ff59fbdfd8664a9a875eb13fd6beddf1a25", "git_parents": ["3ad0d1f9850314ac76966011c625fecfbea59da1"], "node": "25800d67cb9af661b1e5d197b11959941e2b2bbb", "parents": ["86d65a1c8b6acb33df9f773f45c15b3089d55c87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrej Glavic \u003caglavic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2036344 - Add a perfdocs description for the tscrollx_paint_skip talos test. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338477\n", "files": ["testing/perfdocs/generated/talos.md", "testing/talos/perfdocs/config.yml"], "git_node": "4beb6eb65368990d801e60cb6405d8a41a5072c3", "git_parents": ["b9fe2ff59fbdfd8664a9a875eb13fd6beddf1a25"], "node": "77fc16c0563cdc9001eed3f601855f3b93fdbaa1", "parents": ["25800d67cb9af661b1e5d197b11959941e2b2bbb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2080768 - Disable remote recommended preferences for raptor test suites r=perftest-reviewers,sparky\n\nThe goal of this patch is to stop depending on the default test-automation preferences for raptor test suites, initially discussed in Bug 2070193.\nA subset of the recommended preferences is instead set directly in user.js, which avoids setting the preference during the browser startup (which might have some performance impacts).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334239\n", "files": ["testing/profiles/raptor/user.js"], "git_node": "f87c63d628c60e73df874f499ab1ad07b0fb38e4", "git_parents": ["4beb6eb65368990d801e60cb6405d8a41a5072c3"], "node": "753bcb794421392aca425546d4400f593dac1a6b", "parents": ["77fc16c0563cdc9001eed3f601855f3b93fdbaa1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070808 - Stop the Organize Tabs and monitor panels from adding observers after their window unloads, r=Mardak.\n\nThe leak was seen with the Organize Tabs panel; the monitor panel has the same pattern.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337541\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/MonitorPanel.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "2af290f7c33fd2387bfbe0c9814e4c1befcfad51", "git_parents": ["f87c63d628c60e73df874f499ab1ad07b0fb38e4"], "node": "1ac52f1b456d6f22b45a600c58b2179132960962", "parents": ["753bcb794421392aca425546d4400f593dac1a6b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076627 - Fire the headless load deadline once the redirect has gone off-site in browser_smartwindow_get_page_content_timeout.js, r=Mardak.\n\nWith a 500ms load timeout, a slow build could time out before the redirect was seen, so the read was reported as a timeout instead of a block. Wait for the off-site location and expire the load then, as bug 2080002 did for the page extractor tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337543\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_get_page_content_timeout.js"], "git_node": "41fdab201ad0a25378131c8d558b39a7bf0f8b64", "git_parents": ["2af290f7c33fd2387bfbe0c9814e4c1befcfad51"], "node": "32ada0225b32e2defe59f0e96ce0dc4e67903c29", "parents": ["1ac52f1b456d6f22b45a600c58b2179132960962"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071563 - Wait for the smartbar editor to apply typed text before awaiting its query in typeInSmartbar, r=Mardak.\n\nThe multiline editor applies typed text from a mutation observer after\nEventUtils.sendString returns, so typeInSmartbar read a stale\nlastQueryContextPromise and returned while the query was still running.\nbrowser_aiwindow_smartbar_suggestions.js then counted group labels before\nthe query had finished updating the view.\n\ntypeInSmartbar is shared by every test in this directory that types in the\nsmartbar; they all now wait for the editor's input event.\n\nWith the query finished, assertSmartbarSuggestionsVisible measures the full\nlist instead of the heuristic row alone, and the float32 rounding in\ngetBoundingClientRect puts the bottom of the list 0.00003px below the top of\nthe input it touches, so the edge comparisons now allow a rounding tolerance.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337910\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "acfb508d0b642b4b6afcdf4bc890fecf82cfbe2f", "git_parents": ["41fdab201ad0a25378131c8d558b39a7bf0f8b64"], "node": "7fe588abeee5d08ed54f34b7ceec54a3619c0646", "parents": ["32ada0225b32e2defe59f0e96ce0dc4e67903c29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086555 - Don't run LLM telemetry or write its last-run pref during shutdown, r=Mardak.\n\nA scheduler tick or a run in progress at shutdown fails because ChatStore has\nclosed its connection, then writes browser.smartwindow.lastLLMTelemetryRunTime\nafter XPCOMShutdownThreads, which asserts in debug builds. The finally guard\ncovers a run already in progress; the early return avoids starting a run whose\nDB queries can only fail.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337546\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/TelemetryManager.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "7f7ee19c85079a87ab470b5124c2f0ef4652d487", "git_parents": ["acfb508d0b642b4b6afcdf4bc890fecf82cfbe2f"], "node": "969b1b67258e85e07b10362b88da8d398f5ecc10", "parents": ["7fe588abeee5d08ed54f34b7ceec54a3619c0646"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025711 - Remove the Smart Window sidebar browser when switching to a classic window, r=Mardak.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337547\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "7a2e305a2b63c2ea9f1a8d79f5573a246944f17e", "git_parents": ["7f7ee19c85079a87ab470b5124c2f0ef4652d487"], "node": "b35db15b3acbe1a1e09d94ee593075f1204e80c3", "parents": ["969b1b67258e85e07b10362b88da8d398f5ecc10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081861 - Collect the source window's closed tab groups when not including all windows. r=sessionstore-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333759\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/sessionstore/test/browser_tab_groups_closed_groups_source_window.js"], "git_node": "68432a9459333d2899bbd0843c41752388a97a2f", "git_parents": ["7a2e305a2b63c2ea9f1a8d79f5573a246944f17e"], "node": "4c3b23d9ffdb777c43d1671b16972e84c35ed32a", "parents": ["b35db15b3acbe1a1e09d94ee593075f1204e80c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085339 - Don't require -webkit-cross-fade() to pass this test. r=jwatt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339171\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/light-dark-image.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/light-dark-image.html"], "git_node": "07a3c3682601599420ec06f76ca85a467f54e8e6", "git_parents": ["68432a9459333d2899bbd0843c41752388a97a2f"], "node": "80fcc6e99298878b54dca5924a97acb9c9b43239", "parents": ["4c3b23d9ffdb777c43d1671b16972e84c35ed32a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087571 - Remove assert that doesn't hold in case we overflow. r=jwatt\n\nThe test-case creates a very recursive slotted tree which overflows the\ncounter, but seems fine.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339168\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/rule_tree/level.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/many-slots-crash.html"], "git_node": "7d8cdf5a592a483dfc7dacdbf7eded11e4bf9c50", "git_parents": ["07a3c3682601599420ec06f76ca85a467f54e8e6"], "node": "fe6b0697330775b68d2a28f57c6037e78e83575d", "parents": ["80fcc6e99298878b54dca5924a97acb9c9b43239"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086901 Part 1 - Remove the unused visual viewport rect in ComputeVisibleRectForFrame(). r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\n`DisplayPortUtils::IsFixedPosFrameInDisplayPort()` guarantees that the root\nscroll container frame exists and has a displayport.\n\nThis patch removes the dead code, and does not change behavior.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338628\n", "files": ["layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp"], "git_node": "a26c525b83923b26c0d2836fa4abc610611b2fcc", "git_parents": ["7d8cdf5a592a483dfc7dacdbf7eded11e4bf9c50"], "node": "bba819cf0fe1ffe6c1f8d713c9c84a24bbfa881a", "parents": ["fe6b0697330775b68d2a28f57c6037e78e83575d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ting-Yu Lin \u003ctlin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086901 Part 2 - Compute the fixed-pos visible rect in viewport frame coodinates. r=layout-reviewers,hiro\n\nWhen the scrollbar-gutter or a scrollbar is on the left side, the root scroll\nport's origin is not at (0,0). The displayport is relative to the root scroll\nport by default, but the visible rect must be relative to the viewport frame.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338119\n", "files": ["layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fixedpos-005.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fixedpos-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scrollbar-gutter-fixedpos-005.html"], "git_node": "8fe69a72f64b2042ada4ee97bc0f644fd955c025", "git_parents": ["a26c525b83923b26c0d2836fa4abc610611b2fcc"], "node": "1f708e2567f62ba67f1a904764124fe1ebcf7d61", "parents": ["bba819cf0fe1ffe6c1f8d713c9c84a24bbfa881a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ted Campbell \u003ctcampbell@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088318 - Move the build metadata asset generation into ProjectPlugin. r=android-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339027\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/build.gradle", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/build.gradle", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/org/mozilla/conventions/ProjectPlugin.kt"], "git_node": "8a18aacba2f01eb6ebc643d60c85a5344a819772", "git_parents": ["8fe69a72f64b2042ada4ee97bc0f644fd955c025"], "node": "ac722edfa533c8e507f2b585ff6259869853d624", "parents": ["1f708e2567f62ba67f1a904764124fe1ebcf7d61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2071504 - Add multi-select to about:processes?groupby=tab. r=florian,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,emilio\n\nAdds checkbox multi-selection and a bulk-action bar with Unload, Reload,\nand Close. Closing many tabs asks for confirmation, like the tab strip. A\ntab is opened by clicking its name; double-clicking the row no longer\nnavigates.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328418\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.css", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.html", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab_selection.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/head.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/aboutProcesses.ftl"], "git_node": "9866a18fd3a5aa28da97d20a709864946ee5aa17", "git_parents": ["8a18aacba2f01eb6ebc643d60c85a5344a819772"], "node": "9105a125fd2f02b481d3573035bea39240342795", "parents": ["ac722edfa533c8e507f2b585ff6259869853d624"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073286 - Show tab-view CPU as measuring until it has two samples. r=florian\n\nCPU is a rate, so it's unknown on a process's first sample. Until then,\ntab-view CPU cells and totals show \"\u2026\", so an unmeasured tab doesn't\nread as idle.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335200\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab_selection.js"], "git_node": "26ee7fc5f2f8a86efe29e8801305abac5505e202", "git_parents": ["9866a18fd3a5aa28da97d20a709864946ee5aa17"], "node": "c11cbdba6d4cc5acc91d024db4fc5df5b37d2926", "parents": ["9105a125fd2f02b481d3573035bea39240342795"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2073286 - Add tab_action_taken and panel_opened telemetry to about:processes?groupby=tab. r=florian,chutten,sidebar-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nAdds tab-action and panel-open telemetry for the tab view.\npanel_opened records how the panel was opened: sidebar launch, restore\nwith a window or session, or direct navigation. The shared sidebar launch\npath passes the open type as a URL parameter to panels registered with\nappendOpenType, which only the Resource Monitor sets.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D328416\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/SidebarState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/browser-sidebar.js", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_resource_monitor_telemetry.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab_selection.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/head.js", "toolkit/components/glean/metrics_index.py"], "git_node": "6fda284ee12540d330ba01e5439e27d38e37bc80", "git_parents": ["26ee7fc5f2f8a86efe29e8801305abac5505e202"], "node": "331c0af9cb8ebf124a1bcaee354961bb612af6ab", "parents": ["c11cbdba6d4cc5acc91d024db4fc5df5b37d2926"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076293 - Add grouped rendering to about:processes?groupby=tab. r=florian,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,sfoster\n\nGroups tabs by site under a header row showing the site, its tab count\nand RAM/CPU totals, with the site's tabs indented below it. Sites are\nlabeled the way the address bar shows them, and extension pages by the\nextension's name. Groups expand and collapse individually or all at\nonce. A solo tab's site auto-expands when it gains a second tab, so the\ntab being looked at doesn't disappear.\n\nDuring the mouse freeze, rows already shown keep their place. A tab\njoining an existing group appears under it; a new group forms at the\nnext reorder.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330659\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.css", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.html", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab_sites.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/head.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/aboutProcesses.ftl"], "git_node": "4355c1488e9b5bc45007d8e7b3ae5e373d728028", "git_parents": ["6fda284ee12540d330ba01e5439e27d38e37bc80"], "node": "338a1dba1cd0af6c271389b316c442858341f3b0", "parents": ["331c0af9cb8ebf124a1bcaee354961bb612af6ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2076293 - Add group-level selection and unload/reload to about:processes?groupby=tab. r=florian,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nAdds a site header checkbox that selects every tab in the group\n(tri-state when partly selected), and an unload/reload button that acts\non the whole group, active tab included, like per-row and bulk-bar\nunload. The button ignores further clicks until its action finishes and\nhalf a second has passed, so a double-click acts once. These actions\nrecord a new site_header action_source.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333112\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.css", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab_sites.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/aboutProcesses.ftl"], "git_node": "a8069b6db913dd1341c68fa4d91e5cc90131953d", "git_parents": ["4355c1488e9b5bc45007d8e7b3ae5e373d728028"], "node": "70c4ac4eb0fb943ebfa8554d96531c6e96dd9280", "parents": ["338a1dba1cd0af6c271389b316c442858341f3b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077981 - Add search to the about:processes tab view. r=florian,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nAdds search to the grouped tab view, matching what each row shows: a\ntab's title (or URL when it has none), or its site's name. Tabs that\ndon't match are hidden, and every group shows expanded while searching.\nA partly matching site keeps its header, whose count and totals cover\nthe tabs shown. Selected tabs stay listed even when they don't match,\nso bulk actions only act on tabs shown.\n\nDuring the mouse freeze, which tabs are shown changes only on the next\nreorder, like row order.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330660\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.css", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.html", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_tab_search.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/head.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/aboutProcesses.ftl"], "git_node": "00960b32acb0449962496cd7e704cd457868f04d", "git_parents": ["a8069b6db913dd1341c68fa4d91e5cc90131953d"], "node": "889e2eaed8f8240d2e74ccd7b309bcfe276d8c13", "parents": ["70c4ac4eb0fb943ebfa8554d96531c6e96dd9280"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077982 - Update the affected row immediately after unload, reload, or close. r=florian\n\nRows update right after unload, reload, or close, re-reading tab state\nagainst the last sample. During the mouse freeze, rows of closed tabs stay\nin place, dimmed and inert, until the next reorder.\n\nA reloading tab keeps its site while it loads. A row's unload/reload\nbutton ignores repeat clicks like its site header does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D331667\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.css", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab_selection.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab_sites.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "1258ac2749d3dc1827d6d69d2071fe78121946e7", "git_parents": ["00960b32acb0449962496cd7e704cd457868f04d"], "node": "162fe6ee050a86c24880cbc171898ac45fbf0d7a", "parents": ["889e2eaed8f8240d2e74ccd7b309bcfe276d8c13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077982 - Show consistent decimal precision and missing-data handling in tab-view CPU/memory cells. r=florian,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nCPU shows two decimal places, and memory of a gigabyte or more shows one.\nGroup, selection and footer totals show \"\u2014\" when none of their tabs has\nusage data, like single rows.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333113\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab_selection.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab_sites.js", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_tab_totals.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/aboutProcesses.ftl"], "git_node": "a539892441bd1e80cd1c1b60a43db125cfe86f01", "git_parents": ["1258ac2749d3dc1827d6d69d2071fe78121946e7"], "node": "f56730d01a09b84e514c1829a78096148db7d19c", "parents": ["162fe6ee050a86c24880cbc171898ac45fbf0d7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tyler-thorne \u003ctthorne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2077982 - Polish the about:processes tab-view header and cell layout. r=florian,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,emilio\n\nThe tab view's headers have no column dividers, figures use tabular\nnumerals, and the table uses the sidebar panels' font with a larger\naction-column glyph.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330661\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/content/aboutProcesses.css", "toolkit/components/aboutprocesses/tests/browser/browser_aboutprocesses_groupby_tab.js"], "git_node": "4f8786b01759317976dfaacc6a63c3ab8e9f90f8", "git_parents": ["a539892441bd1e80cd1c1b60a43db125cfe86f01"], "node": "8163540ec42cade83bceb9d92c108fd9a5b03468", "parents": ["f56730d01a09b84e514c1829a78096148db7d19c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088638: Add webcompat intervention for www.weather.gov r=webcompat-reviewers,twisniewski\n\nwww.weather.gov sends Referrer-Policy: no-referrer, so OpenStreetMap tile\nrequests carry no Referer.  OSM enforces its Referer requirement for\nFirefox UAs, so the /srh/ hazards map shows \"Access blocked\" tiles.\nOverride the document policy to strict-origin-when-cross-origin there.\n\nThe header is site-wide, but the other pages using OSM tiles (/crh/)\nalready set referrerPolicy on each tile image, so only /srh/ is covered.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339308\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/webcompat/data/interventions/2088638-www.weather.gov.json", "browser/extensions/webcompat/manifest.json", "testing/webcompat/interventions/tests/test_2088638_www_weather_gov.py"], "git_node": "38c480b946b84353a63bd36898247bf26af25911", "git_parents": ["4f8786b01759317976dfaacc6a63c3ab8e9f90f8"], "node": "63feff10288dc0239b112f63efedc505a282ed2a", "parents": ["8163540ec42cade83bceb9d92c108fd9a5b03468"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086579 - Part 6 - Run the Android lint tasks only when the Android linters change r=adhingra\n\nAny change under `tools/lint` started fenix-lints, focus-lints,\nac-lints and android-lints, though only `tools/lint/android` and the\n`android-*.yml` definitions affect them. Over two days, 72 of 147\nreview bot fenix-lints runs came only from other linters' files.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338958\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint-android.yml"], "git_node": "cecd0f3a1ef0e0f40da968e6ba3e235d16c28980", "git_parents": ["38c480b946b84353a63bd36898247bf26af25911"], "node": "5b5f040688c68203e4dfa74b6fe6552b2c908212", "parents": ["63feff10288dc0239b112f63efedc505a282ed2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085853 - Keep `--fix` jobs on a directory and a file inside it apart r=linter-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nThe `--fix` grouping compared the job paths as strings, so a job on a\ndirectory and a job on a file inside it could run at the same time and\nwrite the same file.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336632\n", "files": ["python/mozlint/mozlint/roller.py", "python/mozlint/test/test_roller.py"], "git_node": "8c359314fb2060e6c09230144da9f7aec03c352e", "git_parents": ["cecd0f3a1ef0e0f40da968e6ba3e235d16c28980"], "node": "1c2543bfdef2cc773484c87dc67d460219a103f6", "parents": ["5b5f040688c68203e4dfa74b6fe6552b2c908212"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2085860 - Check the literals in `test_lint_api_yml` r=linter-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nThe test read a `literal` category, which `mfbt/api.yml` does not have,\nso it never checked `_KiB`, `_MiB` or `_percent`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338564\n", "files": ["tools/lint/test/test_includes.py"], "git_node": "c56c0fe802d3340586f055f06c23e214d380cda6", "git_parents": ["8c359314fb2060e6c09230144da9f7aec03c352e"], "node": "97da5f9057ccda555896ec949733ce8b89bbf459", "parents": ["1c2543bfdef2cc773484c87dc67d460219a103f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088345 - Stop building the clang plugin for the clang-tidy tasks r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThe clang-tidy tasks set `--enable-clang-plugin`, so every run built the\nplugin, but nothing used it. clang-tidy ignores the plugin and has its own\nbuild of the same Mozilla checks, and `mach static-analysis` already passes\n`-DMOZ_CLANG_PLUGIN`, the define the option was there for. Without the plugin\nthe export tiers take about 25 seconds instead of 53 in clang-tidy and\nclang-external, and 46 instead of 127 in the static-analysis unittest, with\nthe same findings.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339041\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/source-test-clang-setup.sh"], "git_node": "af5511b7acbbd3dca93f92351d2e17dbe1667b27", "git_parents": ["c56c0fe802d3340586f055f06c23e214d380cda6"], "node": "7d7f80c3a8f2fc82ddd9eb6dded24bc1c71577a0", "parents": ["97da5f9057ccda555896ec949733ce8b89bbf459"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Tighe \u003cmatthewdtighe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087701 - add debug drawer method to cause page extraction to fail for a tab r=android-reviewers,moyin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338982\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/content/ContentExtractor.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/content/ContentProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/ListenMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/content/ContentExtractorTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/listentopage/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/listentopage/content/ContentProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/listentopage/FenixListenPageExtractor.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/listentopage/ListenDebugController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/listentopage/ListenToPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/listentopage/ListenToPageTools.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/navigation/DebugDrawerRoute.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/ui/FenixOverlay.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/listentopage/FenixListenContentExtractorProviderTest.kt"], "git_node": "2ed8252d30f35dc2686f82945cd95c802fccdc6d", "git_parents": ["af5511b7acbbd3dca93f92351d2e17dbe1667b27"], "node": "8b5a818d36afb0111008d6e5027aaa950aa55eee", "parents": ["7d7f80c3a8f2fc82ddd9eb6dded24bc1c71577a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Tighe \u003cmatthewdtighe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087701 - show listen player when extraction fails r=android-reviewers,moyin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338983\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/listentopage/ListenSheetIntegration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/listentopage/ListenSheetIntegrationTest.kt"], "git_node": "4d631a6c79f1e187fe6c2b94bcd41aa797421b4e", "git_parents": ["2ed8252d30f35dc2686f82945cd95c802fccdc6d"], "node": "7bf08bd4edec0c18bc9d18288f19c8d924da5316", "parents": ["8b5a818d36afb0111008d6e5027aaa950aa55eee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088306 - Define NativePanHandler on the test scope instead of the browser window. r=hiro\n\nSummary\n- Since a second case for touchscreen swipes was added to\n  browser_disableSwipeGestures.js, the file has been run in TV (test-verify)\n  mode. In that mode, the first case in the file fails with\n  \"ReferenceError: ok is not defined\" (on macOS, the same error shows up as\n  a test timeout). This patch fixes that.\n\nCause\n- In short, apz_test_native_event_utils.js defines a `NativePanHandler`\n  getter on `window`, and the getter relies on helpers that are cleaned up\n  when the test ends. TV mode reuses the same window for repeated runs of\n  the test, so the second run fails.\n\nDetailed Cause\n\n  [1st run]\n    test scope #1 = { ok, info, ..., getPanHandler#1, panLeftToRightBegin#1, ... }\n    window        = { NativePanHandler: getter -\u003e calls getPanHandler#1 }\n                    ^ defined on window, not on the test scope\n\n    Test ends -\u003e testScope.destroy() deletes ok, info, ... from scope #1\n    (window survives, so the getter stays)\n\n  [2nd run]\n    test scope #2 = { ok, info, ..., getPanHandler#2, panLeftToRightBegin#2, ... }\n    NativePanHandler already exists on window -\u003e not redefined\n\n    panLeftToRightBegin#2 looks up NativePanHandler\n      -\u003e not in scope #2 -\u003e found on window (the getter from the 1st run)\n      -\u003e getPanHandler#1 -\u003e 1st run's functions -\u003e look up ok()\n      -\u003e ok() is gone from scope #1 -\u003e \"ReferenceError: ok is not defined\"\n\n- The failure happens as follows:\n  - A browser-chrome mochitest involves at least two objects: the window and\n    the test scope. The window is the browser window, which is the global of\n    the JS context the test runs in. The test scope is created by the\n    harness inside that window, once for each run of a test file.\n  - When the test starts, it loads apz_test_native_event_utils.js into the\n    test scope with Services.scriptloader.loadSubScript. The file then\n    defines `NativePanHandler` on `window`, unless it is already defined\n    there.\n    (https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/2b71df5bf2e07525d1129be46e0ee02ec70d34d8/gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/apz_test_native_event_utils.js#1819-1827)\n  - This getter returns a handler such as NativePanHandlerForLinux from the\n    test scope that the file was loaded into. The key point is that the\n    functions these handlers call use helpers such as ok() and info(),\n    which the harness defines as properties of the test scope.\n    (https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/2b71df5bf2e07525d1129be46e0ee02ec70d34d8/testing/mochitest/browser-test.js#2286,2292-2299)\n    - They only call these helpers when the target is in another window, such\n      as the PiP window here. That is why other tests that use these handlers\n      don't fail.\n      (https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/2b71df5bf2e07525d1129be46e0ee02ec70d34d8/gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/apz_test_native_event_utils.js#233)\n  - testScope.destroy() deletes these helpers once all the tests in the\n    test file have finished.\n    (https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/2b71df5bf2e07525d1129be46e0ee02ec70d34d8/testing/mochitest/browser-test.js#1675)\n    (https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/2b71df5bf2e07525d1129be46e0ee02ec70d34d8/testing/mochitest/browser-test.js#2623-2627)\n  - So in TV mode, `NativePanHandler` is not redefined in the second run,\n    and the getter left on `window` by the first run is used instead. It\n    ends up calling a helper that has already been deleted, and the test\n    fails with \"ReferenceError: ok is not defined\".\n    - getPanHandler#1 remains, because it's not cleaned up by testScope.destroy()\n      or GCed (`window` refers to it).\n\nWhat this patch does\n- This patch changes apz_test_native_event_utils.js to define\n  `NativePanHandler` on `this`, which is the test scope in browser-chrome\n  tests.\n- In tests that load the file with a \u003cscript\u003e tag in an HTML page\n  (e.g. mochitest-plain), `this` is still `window`, so they behave as\n  before.\n- This patch actually fixed local failure of TV mode on Mac.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339323\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/apz_test_native_event_utils.js"], "git_node": "7d3f423b812f1dc494eff307b31c3f4ccf5e65b8", "git_parents": ["4d631a6c79f1e187fe6c2b94bcd41aa797421b4e"], "node": "a211eaa9ee7cc69de4318b821e46baaf3b7f8bb0", "parents": ["7bf08bd4edec0c18bc9d18288f19c8d924da5316"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Oberhauser \u003cj.git@obez.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081834 - Add a shared profile authentication check for sensitive data on Android Automotive OS r=twhite\n\nAdds `AutomotiveSensitiveDataAuthenticator`, a shared check that sensitive data flows call before continuing on Android Automotive OS when the `automotive-sensitive-data` Nimbus feature is enabled. If no device lock is set up, it shows the setup prompt from bug 2081830; otherwise it asks the user to authenticate. The action only continues on success.\n\nTry: https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=114034\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/426\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/biometric/AutomotiveAuthenticationSetupPrompt.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/biometric/AutomotiveSensitiveDataAuthenticator.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/biometric/ext/DeviceLock.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/logins/ui/BiometricAuthenticationUtils.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/biometric/AutomotiveSensitiveDataAuthenticatorTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/biometric/ext/DeviceLockTest.kt"], "git_node": "59dbaa27107454ac9f01b9cfaddf84e9b51b909f", "git_parents": ["7d3f423b812f1dc494eff307b31c3f4ccf5e65b8"], "node": "010fedb3a969df44fe5a6a6f123baed1df1be9fd", "parents": ["a211eaa9ee7cc69de4318b821e46baaf3b7f8bb0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Punam Dahiya \u003cpdahiya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083978 - Add Smart Window Nimbus variables for the auth provider and guest sign-in mode. r=yjamora,baku,tliu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D335468\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/auth/AuthImplSelector.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_AuthImplSelector.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_nimbus.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "3ab7da31691b1f2d7c8060d53cf2ca7b5724de82", "git_parents": ["59dbaa27107454ac9f01b9cfaddf84e9b51b909f"], "node": "4ad1faac31a95156624722abfd44f3ebecd85947", "parents": ["010fedb3a969df44fe5a6a6f123baed1df1be9fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Punam Dahiya \u003cpdahiya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084445 - Add telemetry for the Smart Window guest sign-in flow r=yjamora,baku,cdipersio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338147\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/AuthProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/auth/AuthImplSelector.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/auth/AuthProviderImpl.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/auth/FxaAuthProviderImpl.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/auth/FxaSignedInWatcher.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/auth/GuestAuthProviderImpl.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_auth_guest.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_FxaSignedInWatcher.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/SmartWindowTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_account_auth.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_nimbus.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_request_response_telemetry.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_switcher_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "c1cb80aa44b5f3f236cc47d50d86bcfd4a7e0ade", "git_parents": ["3ab7da31691b1f2d7c8060d53cf2ca7b5724de82"], "node": "cb271a38c01b4075789e6fbaef8fd3df42d3f0e0", "parents": ["4ad1faac31a95156624722abfd44f3ebecd85947"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nickgrato \u003cngrato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086741 - [Research Agent][FE] Add a reusable clarifying question card for Smart Window AI flows r=yjamora,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,reusable-components-reviewers,bolsson,mstriemer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337687\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-clarifying-question/ai-clarifying-question.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-clarifying-question/ai-clarifying-question.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-clarifying-question/ai-clarifying-question.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-base.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/aitab-page/aitab-highlights/aitab-highlights.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/ai-window-shared.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/aitab.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_moz_input_text.html", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_moz_textarea.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-text/moz-input-text.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-textarea/moz-textarea.mjs"], "git_node": "8b9d48769ac979395dad084a95ce377ecc3fc259", "git_parents": ["c1cb80aa44b5f3f236cc47d50d86bcfd4a7e0ade"], "node": "b82f8956e7454c037792ff9a2ba5a70061555081", "parents": ["cb271a38c01b4075789e6fbaef8fd3df42d3f0e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Almeida \u003cjonalmeida942@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088672 - Move ipprotection reducers to the appropriate package r=Roger,android-reviewers\n\nMove all reducers to { =\u003e reducer} package.\nLocationRepository to {store =\u003e storage} package.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339285\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/storage/IPProtectionLocationRepository.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/AccountReducer.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/ActivationReducer.kt", "mobile/a