elements with accesskeys in the chrome r=masayuki,mkennedy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321562\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/test/chrome.toml", "dom/events/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/events/test/test_accesskey_visibility.html", "dom/events/test/test_accesskey_visibility_content.html", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/lit-test-helpers.js", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_moz_box_button.html"], "git_node": "548adc3a0f44efec4c388756943b0e88c5a467d0", "git_parents": ["98bddef2a90f3746379bea72892214ac35b825bd"], "node": "ef89e12b1444300756963eaa7e0b8385561500a7", "parents": ["ebeddb8734cd9a6052b50d3e9634d51b79efe57c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hannajones \u003chjones@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1942186 - Add automatic Fluent support for moz-button accesskeys r=mkennedy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321563\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_moz_button.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-button/moz-button.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-button/moz-button.stories.mjs"], "git_node": "f1852f296fb297065460b2ab0208b3982b9d4f2f", "git_parents": ["548adc3a0f44efec4c388756943b0e88c5a467d0"], "node": "ec91552b3ad607f0d566277ed8b2d46f82da01f6", "parents": ["ef89e12b1444300756963eaa7e0b8385561500a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hannajones \u003chjones@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1942186 - Part 2: clean up existing usage of data-l10n-attrs='accesskey' on moz-button r=mkennedy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D321564\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/preferences/widgets/sync-device-name/sync-device-name.mjs", "toolkit/content/net-error-card.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-folder/moz-input-folder.mjs"], "git_node": "26387196692b03a8d265ed06d52edf7335d90a17", "git_parents": ["f1852f296fb297065460b2ab0208b3982b9d4f2f"], "node": "c060f5b5df158cd508b49d4e9b28dac8c4d83e54", "parents": ["ec91552b3ad607f0d566277ed8b2d46f82da01f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "csalinezh \u003ccsalinezh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084416 - Resolve presses in text-control padding like single clicks. r=masayuki\n\nCurrently, A double click in a text control's padding or empty area\nselected no word, and a long press there left the caret where it was\nwhile showing its Paste menu. MoveCaretToEventPoint resolves single\nclicks with only SKIP_HIDDEN, whereas SelectByTypeAtPoint and\nAccessibleCaretManager::SelectWordOrShortcut also set\nIGNORE_NATIVE_ANONYMOUS_SUBTREE, with which a point on the text\ncontrol's own frame resolves outside the control.\n\nIGNORE_NATIVE_ANONYMOUS_SUBTREE was added for bug 1872302 so that moving\nthe document's caret up or down a line can't enter text controls.\nFrames within a text control use that control's independent selection,\nwhere the editor's content belongs. Add\nnsIFrame::GetContentOffsetsFromPointForSelection, which resolves the\npoint for such frames as a single click does, but never outside the\nroot of the independent selection, e.g. to an ancestor with\n`user-select: all`, and use it in both places. Caret dragging, which\nalso sets the flag, first constrains its frame to the selection's\nanchor subtree, and is unaffected.\n\nA double click there now selects the word where the click before it\nputs the caret. A long press there places the caret at that position\nwith its Paste menu, as in contenteditable and other content\n(bug 1448730); whether it should select the word is left to a\nfollow-up.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336882\n", "files": ["layout/base/AccessibleCaretManager.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/resources/text-control-selection-around-text.html", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/text-control-longpress-around-text.html", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/text-control-multiclick-around-text.html"], "git_node": "ad208230c5dbf6e80987c5cc02e3910633a6c21c", "git_parents": ["26387196692b03a8d265ed06d52edf7335d90a17"], "node": "0d2195f1744834689f81a9f5b959dd1fcf6f41cf", "parents": ["c060f5b5df158cd508b49d4e9b28dac8c4d83e54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088559 - Update New Tab Recent Activity for Nova. r=thecount\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339203\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/_Grid.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Card/Card.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Card/_Card.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/Highlights/_Highlights.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Sections/Sections.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/lib/utils.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/HighlightsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PrefsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_highlights_section.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Card.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Sections.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/lib/utils.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/PrefsFeed.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_HighlightsFeed.js"], "git_node": "269c87a92f4d1ea2b6a050e084ce064fffe05b17", "git_parents": ["ad208230c5dbf6e80987c5cc02e3910633a6c21c"], "node": "5fa1d7bb6fee67a6a53e30c27dd24bbb8288d566", "parents": ["0d2195f1744834689f81a9f5b959dd1fcf6f41cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Frederik Braun \u003cfbraun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070804 - Add per-document Trusted Types readiness telemetry r=tschuster,smaug\n\nThis adds a Glean labeled_counter whose label encodes the full combination of readiness signals for that document:\n\n  htmlsink-{none,trusted,string}_writesink-{none,trusted,string}_ttcsp-{none,report,enforce}_strictcsp-{none,report,enforce}_created-{0,1}_used-{0,1}_lib-{0,1}_js-{0,1}\n\nRecording depends on the pref\n`dom.security.trusted_types.readiness_telemetry.enabled`\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330553\n", "files": ["dom/base/DOMParser.cpp", "dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/Range.cpp", "dom/base/ShadowRoot.cpp", "dom/base/nsContentUtils.cpp", "dom/events/EventListenerManager.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLIFrameElement.cpp", "dom/jsurl/nsJSProtocolHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/security/metrics.yaml", "dom/security/nsCSPContext.cpp", "dom/security/nsCSPContext.h", "dom/security/nsCSPUtils.cpp", "dom/security/nsCSPUtils.h", "dom/security/test/general/browser.toml", "dom/security/test/general/browser_trusted_types_readiness.js", "dom/security/test/general/file_trusted_types_readiness.sjs", "dom/security/trusted-types/TrustedTypePolicy.cpp", "dom/security/trusted-types/TrustedTypePolicyFactory.cpp", "dom/security/trusted-types/TrustedTypeUtils.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "9265a34c6bdfe0746f8b2fe17e3a325ccfe196db", "git_parents": ["269c87a92f4d1ea2b6a050e084ce064fffe05b17"], "node": "c67c533126909f5d98db6d8d63a2a1cd3edb52e0", "parents": ["5fa1d7bb6fee67a6a53e30c27dd24bbb8288d566"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Frederik Braun \u003cfbraun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070804 - Add a Nimbus feature gating Trusted Types readiness telemetry r=tschuster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330554\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "05896e2c0ad21af9472f6825a2df051b604ca2ae", "git_parents": ["9265a34c6bdfe0746f8b2fe17e3a325ccfe196db"], "node": "60e334e0615ca54005b9f19291256c178f4b7a79", "parents": ["c67c533126909f5d98db6d8d63a2a1cd3edb52e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Frederik Braun \u003cfbraun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2070804 - Detect libraries that ease Trusted Types adoption for the readiness telemetry r=smaug\n\nSet the HasTrustedTypesLibrary signal, reported as the lib dimension of\nsecurity.trusted_types_readiness, when a page uses one of React, Angular, Lit\nor htmx.\n\nDetections:\n - Lit: TrustedTypePolicyFactory::CreatePolicy matches the \"lit-html\" policy\n   name, which Lit always creates when it loads. It is checked before the CSP\n   check, so a blocked attempt still counts.\n - React: React DOM looks up __REACT_DEVTOOLS_GLOBAL_HOOK__ when it loads.\n   nsGlobalWindowInner::MayResolve and DoResolve recognize that id, from a\n   new XPCJSContext string id, and record the lookup without resolving it,\n   ignoring Xray lookups. Defining the global goes through the resolve hook\n   too, so after load the lookup only counts if the hook still does not\n   exist. A hook the page defined as a data property, typically to disable\n   DevTools, counts as well. The React DevTools extension defines it behind a\n   getter on every page, and that does not count.\n - htmx: an htmx global property.\n - Angular: an ng-version attribute, which Angular sets on the root\n   component's host element.\n\nEverything but Lit is checked once per document, from OnPageShow right after\nthe load event, so nothing runs when a document enters or leaves the bfcache.\nAngular is only looked for on body and its first element children, where its\napps mount: no document walk, and no element wrapper is touched. Documents\nthat merely embed a widget deeper in the tree, or append one to the end of\nbody, are not the target of this measurement.\n\nbrowser_trusted_types_libraries.js checks each detection against a page that\nonly reproduces its symptom, that a DevTools hook behind a getter is not\ndetected, and that a document leaving the bfcache is reported exactly once.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D333577\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/security/metrics.yaml", "dom/security/test/general/browser.toml", "dom/security/test/general/browser_trusted_types_libraries.js", "dom/security/test/general/file_trusted_types_library.sjs", "dom/security/trusted-types/TrustedTypePolicyFactory.cpp", "js/xpconnect/src/XPCJSRuntime.cpp", "js/xpconnect/src/xpcprivate.h"], "git_node": "cb72114e9ce3e94453d1c0a74c1a92ec35f5d147", "git_parents": ["05896e2c0ad21af9472f6825a2df051b604ca2ae"], "node": "cddba487ff0e4266f4e0bdfafbacbe9cb250a657", "parents": ["60e334e0615ca54005b9f19291256c178f4b7a79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087974 - [devtools] Add CSS explainers for attr() using type(). r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339047\n", "files": ["devtools/client/shared/output-parser.js", "devtools/client/shared/test/browser_outputparser.js"], "git_node": "d0a271892f17ce6af4b4c54cc9c276aa305856a3", "git_parents": ["cb72114e9ce3e94453d1c0a74c1a92ec35f5d147"], "node": "ec4303459f242ebe0ac7785adfe27baad6cf1cc6", "parents": ["cddba487ff0e4266f4e0bdfafbacbe9cb250a657"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088360 - [devtools] Add test cases for arbitrary function argument grammar. r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339050\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/rules/test/browser_rules_css_explainers.js"], "git_node": "42321edfed997f1b202c1bd71f2c21535200025c", "git_parents": ["d0a271892f17ce6af4b4c54cc9c276aa305856a3"], "node": "60c999ff576c720159fe53122eaebdb18f48906b", "parent