er support for arm64e recently landed for LLD\n(https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/234002).\nWe keep the existing partch around, though, because backporting the\nwhole stack is more effort than necessary at the moment provided the\nlack of support in Rust.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339381\n", "files": ["build/build-clang/clang-trunk.json"], "git_node": "a9e937a28972a809a43c50c60ee4a6ea4047833f", "git_parents": ["f92a9e17fc2c20be25d187bf0311876d2cf838f6"], "node": "eee7b4cb58a8d17d3980c6dede150b41aea058e4", "parents": ["98a57ffe8adfe4ba494def306d63f3a6c44447fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088750 - Upgrade clang 23 toolchain to 23.1.5. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339391\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml"], "git_node": "2739c9fa5a8f3ad2c486c8206844ee0ae165ec63", "git_parents": ["a9e937a28972a809a43c50c60ee4a6ea4047833f"], "node": "6634c31e22c82f3e48aa7ed9f9adaa2cd4fff4c8", "parents": ["eee7b4cb58a8d17d3980c6dede150b41aea058e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2079251 - Preload PDF.js renderer workers. r=pdfjs-reviewers,marco\n\nOverlap renderer startup with viewer initialization.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336024\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/pdfjs/content/PdfStreamConverter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/test/browser_pdfjs_preloaded_worker.js"], "git_node": "924e93a2685c3c24de64b38a526af6a1eaba42fa", "git_parents": ["2739c9fa5a8f3ad2c486c8206844ee0ae165ec63"], "node": "1e24e52a402009ab9454ddc4e5ce6e8753e538cb", "parents": ["6634c31e22c82f3e48aa7ed9f9adaa2cd4fff4c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cornelius Emase \u003ccorneliuslochipi@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2075356 - Don't rewrite let/const to assignments for console eval in frames r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nThe console rewrote `let x = 1` into `x = 1` before the engine saw it,\nwhich mutated the outer binding instead of shadowing it.\n\nThe same rewrite handled `var`, which must persist across evals even while paused.\nI've narrowed the rewrite to `var` only.\n\nI've also added a test that pauses in a frame and checks `let`/`const` shadow\ncorrectly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D330110\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/dist/parser-worker.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/workers/parser/mapBindings.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/workers/parser/tests/mapBindings.spec.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/workers/parser/tests/mapExpression.spec.js", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/_jsterm.toml", "devtools/client/webconsole/test/browser/browser_jsterm_redeclare_let_const_in_frame.js"], "git_node": "16d68d4b34157ef037fb8ab2cf9ed2c245094580", "git_parents": ["924e93a2685c3c24de64b38a526af6a1eaba42fa"], "node": "d3bd9bab547804df5efcb447541ade9a698b9d46", "parents": ["1e24e52a402009ab9454ddc4e5ce6e8753e538cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088752 - Upgrade diffoscope docker images to Debian trixie. r=taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339394\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/docker-image/kind.yml"], "git_node": "499b5252e8e15ffe90721d6fa9a13c38a8f2158f", "git_parents": ["16d68d4b34157ef037fb8ab2cf9ed2c245094580"], "node": "80bf74700cd8ebe4d68fec6b341747db1d14bea3", "parents": ["d3bd9bab547804df5efcb447541ade9a698b9d46"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083057 - Keep the New Tab address bar's input from running under the go button. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers,kcochrane,daisuke\n\nThis also gives #searchbar-new the address bar's spacing between the text and the go button, where it had none.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339095\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-newtab/browser_narrowWindow.js", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar.css"], "git_node": "68fbba60ed84199c67d08804d68278ee9aadcda6", "git_parents": ["499b5252e8e15ffe90721d6fa9a13c38a8f2158f"], "node": "2edecc85fc6e815e8335bdbaeb35470c5d1b8e23", "parents": ["80bf74700cd8ebe4d68fec6b341747db1d14bea3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088498 - Draw gantt charts 800px wide. r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339313\n", "files": ["docs/conf.py"], "git_node": "b7bfbc12df366f0a305d975c7a3e2d719c43a7dd", "git_parents": ["68fbba60ed84199c67d08804d68278ee9aadcda6"], "node": "b6ea0a501083be223199653829393da2f29c9a9e", "parents": ["2edecc85fc6e815e8335bdbaeb35470c5d1b8e23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henrik Skupin \u003cmail@hskupin.info\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088640 - [remote] Handle navigations with a suppressed start state in ProgressListener. r=jdescottes,webdriver-reviewers\n\nWhile a document is still loading the web progress suppresses the\nSTATE_START notification of a new load. A ProgressListener waiting for\nan explicit start then ignored the stop state of that new load, and the\nnavigation either hung or failed with a wrong error name.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337271\n", "files": ["remote/shared/Navigate.sys.mjs", "remote/shared/test/xpcshell/test_Navigate.js"], "git_node": "6c9348c89ee6d0baa883b79c6d35e41d2da69a57", "git_parents": ["b7bfbc12df366f0a305d975c7a3e2d719c43a7dd"], "node": "bba2cac2536c281e80cc98c7fd35a0ecf5d6e861", "parents": ["b6ea0a501083be223199653829393da2f29c9a9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1945032, Bug 1942186 - Part 2: clean up existing usage of data-l10n-attrs='accesskey' on moz-button r=mkennedy\" for causing a11y failures on browser_test_panel.\n\nThis reverts commit 26387196692b03a8d265ed06d52edf7335d90a17.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1942186 - Add automatic Fluent support for moz-button accesskeys r=mkennedy\"\n\nThis reverts commit f1852f296fb297065460b2ab0208b3982b9d4f2f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1945032 - Perform visibility checks on HTML elements with accesskeys in the chrome r=masayuki,mkennedy\"\n\nThis reverts commit 548adc3a0f44efec4c388756943b0e88c5a467d0.\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/preferences/widgets/sync-device-name/sync-device-name.mjs", "dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/test/chrome.toml", "dom/events/test/mochitest.toml", "dom/events/test/test_accesskey_visibility.html", "dom/events/test/test_accesskey_visibility_content.html", "toolkit/content/net-error-card.mjs", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/lit-test-helpers.js", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_moz_box_button.html", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_moz_button.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-button/moz-button.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-button/moz-button.stories.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-input-folder/moz-input-folder.mjs"], "git_node": "8fe9d0db7d1daf553a702af9454daa83a4fb2675", "git_parents": ["6c9348c89ee6d0baa883b79c6d35e41d2da69a57"], "node": "b9c86b6d2c433b50e040bb28aea0754bd38313d7", "parents": ["bba2cac2536c281e80cc98c7fd35a0ecf5d6e861"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2084416 - Resolve presses in text-control padding like single clicks. r=masayuki\" for causing wpt failures @text-control-multiclick-around-text.html.\n\nThis reverts commit ad208230c5dbf6e80987c5cc02e3910633a6c21c.\n", "files": ["layout/base/AccessibleCaretManager.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/resources/text-control-selection-around-text.html", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/text-control-longpress-around-text.html", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/selection/text-control-multiclick-around-text.html"], "git_node": "94ec952205f0d9e39c738746058977fbe42a3a62", "git_parents": ["8fe9d0db7d1daf553a702af9454daa83a4fb2675"], "node": "928d1bc5bec5a274ea41191fa9ee966689e8dd8d", "parents": ["b9c86b6d2c433b50e040bb28aea0754bd38313d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088758 - Add DRM Source Status to DCSurfaceVideo Profiler Marker in DCSurfaceVideo::CalculateSwapChainSize() r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339399\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/DCLayerTree.cpp"], "git_node": "5fdab06b4b663d7043a6fb18bcb5b29331b28b8b", "git_parents": ["94ec952205f0d9e39c738746058977fbe42a3a62"], "node": "73dfd883c8303400da720d5b65bd3245329d4a52", "parents": ["928d1bc5bec5a274ea41191fa9ee966689e8dd8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059683 - Use highp for the image UV bounds in the quad shaders. r=gw\n\nWith mediump, Mali GPUs evaluate the normalized atlas UV bounds in fp16, which\nis off by up to half a texel in the far half of a 2048px atlas. The sample\nbounds then fail to keep filtering inside the image, producing seams at each\nrepetition of repeated images and between the tiles of large images.\nbrush_image used highp for these varyings for the same reason.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339243\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_quad_repeat.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/res/sample_color0.glsl"], "git_node": "9ae0b0c42feda0075a3260b72a439a7dd7d444a4", "git_parents": ["5fdab06b4b663d7043a6fb18bcb5b29331b28b8b"], "node": "e1f99eb32714c2a57951ebb49615d00cc20ec161", "parents": ["73dfd883c8303400da720d5b65bd3245329d4a52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Botond Ballo \u003cbotond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086786 - Guard against a zero-delta pan-start event causing APZ to let a scroll through when content is preventDefault-ing wheel events. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth,hiro\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337809\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_zero_delta_pan_with_prevent_default.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/test_group_wheelevents.html", "widget/InputData.cpp", "widget/InputData.h", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm", "widget/gtk/nsWindow.cpp", "widget/nsIWidget.cpp", "widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "b0e87da00a5f2a0196a9039611c2872a55b5d9ec", "git_parents": ["9ae0b0c42feda0075a3260b72a439a7dd7d444a4"], "node": "c91352f7593cda3e3503acf3268144552c7107c8", "parents": ["e1f99eb32714c2a57951ebb49615d00cc20ec161"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Botond Ballo \u003cbotond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086786 - Guard against a zero-delta pan-end event causing APZ to let a (momentum) scroll through when content is preventDefault-ing wheel events. r=hiro\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339005\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/InputQueue.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestPanning.cpp"], "git_node": "84da89381479f364481410e2b8d41022840e945a", "git_parents": ["b0e87da00a5f2a0196a9039611c2872a55b5d9ec"], "node": "bca537b93a1308c7ca2f71d9a338a3d6866d27f1", "parents": ["c91352f7593cda3e3503acf3268144552c7107c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058057 - Switch networking prefs from EARLY_BETA_OR_EARLIER to IS_NIGHTLY_BUILD r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nMost of these have been in EARLY_BETA for a while.\nWe probably want to either let them ride the trains or remove them, but the safest path forward is to mark them NIGHTLY for now\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339209\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "87eb9f4ef9fc14eaa73bc69825902c7e7fad8ffd", "git_parents": ["84da89381479f364481410e2b8d41022840e945a"], "node": "3ed827af6abe8bb4aa017d97ec87b68e45a22660", "parents": ["bca537b93a1308c7ca2f71d9a338a3d6866d27f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086762 - Don't let the selection scroll queued by focusing a text control scroll the page after it loses focus, r=dom-core-reviewers,masayuki,smaug.\n\nFocusing an input or textarea queues an async selection scroll that also scrolls its ancestors, so calling focus() then blur() then scrollTo(0, 0) brings the page back to the input on the next refresh tick. On blur, the pending scroll is now limited to the text control's own scroller.\n\nThis is a regression: the fix for bug 562447 revoked the pending focus scroll on blur; bug 1634153 dropped that revoke when it limited the scroll to the control, and bug 1644366 made the scroll reach ancestors again.\n\ntest_bug562447.html now waits for a refresh tick, so it fails without the fix in standalone runs, where the test frame can scroll; remove the skip-if from bug 2026600.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337713\n", "files": ["dom/base/Selection.cpp", "dom/base/Selection.h", "layout/forms/nsTextControlFrame.cpp", "layout/forms/test/mochitest.toml", "layout/forms/test/test_bug562447.html", "layout/forms/test/test_pending_selection_scroll_after_blur.html"], "git_node": "66add401cdbb6aad6c99167ff23ce14e6036504a", "git_parents": ["87eb9f4ef9fc14eaa73bc69825902c7e7fad8ffd"], "node": "98d478361be04b1797022549a56664e477ba706c", "parents": ["3ed827af6abe8bb4aa017d97ec87b68e45a22660"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan-Niklas Jaeschke \u003cjjaschke@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084702 - Construct ECMASet/ECMAMap entries in place. r=edgar\n\nGCC 11 crashes when instantiating the braced Entry temporary inside the\nWithEntryHandle lambda for raw pointer keys.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339246\n", "files": ["dom/bindings/ECMACollections.h", "dom/bindings/gtest/TestECMACollections.cpp"], "git_node": "53130afaac3cbecf9dab2bddafd355f8208354a1", "git_parents": ["66add401cdbb6aad6c99167ff23ce14e6036504a"], "node": "61598aae6b51fea0fc8cd7920d109c7cb108990f", "parents": ["98d478361be04b1797022549a56664e477ba706c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lars Eggert \u003clars@eggert.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1939152 - Use 64 KiB upload copy segments on all channels. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339409\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "0a3fd3baad9f2631c6a194c8e6335f58bbe86af1", "git_parents": ["53130afaac3cbecf9dab2bddafd355f8208354a1"], "node": "4fecfbf16e25c31c32df9e3361b1ef95440d4374", "parents": ["61598aae6b51fea0fc8cd7920d109c7cb108990f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088598 - [devtools] Stop redefining wait in netmonitor tests r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339231\n", "files": ["devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_basic-search.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_block-connection-allowlist.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_block-context.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_block-csp.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_block-pattern.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_brotli.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_cached-status.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/test/browser_net_cause_redirect.js", "devtools/cl