rty/application-services/tools/generate-rust-dashboards/src/team_config.rs", "third_party/application-services/tools/start-bindings/templates/build.gradle", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/ads-client/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/adsclient/ads_client.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/remotesettings/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/remotesettings/remote_settings.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustAdsClient.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustRemoteSettings.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "e68853ccf82c0b412b805c27f5d94e0de242ffb7", "git_parents": ["2c8abb14b0ed222a64071ec4bb6db1d6dcb1494c"], "node": "f528980adbd1758908f7e5d949bdc688b17625d1", "parents": ["f9d2204397fd6d383a64d021d3e812aaf6c39a99"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063424 - Set original pref values for migrateFirefoxLabs directly r=ralkhulaidi,nimbus-reviewers,emcminn\n\nmigrateFirefoxLabs()` is a migration that transitions clients into live\nFirefox Labs delivieries if they interacted with the non-Nimbus powered\nversion of Firefox Labs and opted in to various features. At this point,\nthere is only a single feature / rollout pair still in tree.\n\nBecause the user has already opted into this feature and set the\nrequired pref, the enrollment machinery will compute a value of `true`\nfor the original value of the pref. However, if the user opts out of the\nnew lab rollout, they should have their pref reset to the disabled\nvalue. We therefore need to overwrite the original value of a pref in\nthis one specific case.\n\nPreviously we were updating the enrollment directly and re-triggering a\nsave. However, this had a subtle race condition where it was technically\npossible that `NimbusEnrollments` had already flushed by the time we\nmodified the migration and called `updateEnrollment`. In that case, the\nsecond flush would actually result in an unenrollment being recorded in\nthe database because the update was registered without a recipe.\n\nNow we thread a Map of pref values from the migration through the\nenrollent pipeline all the way to\n`ExperimentManager._getPrefsForBranch`. This is an unfortunate change as\nit has to be threaded through so many layers, but alas it is not\npermanent: it will be removed in bug 2086737 when we retire the\n`migrateFirefoxLabs()` migration.\n\nThe second patch in this series updates the API of NimbusEnrollments to\nmake it clear what database changes will occur with each call, which\nwould have made this issue obvious.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338115\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/FirefoxLabs.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/ExperimentManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/Migrations.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_FirefoxLabs.js"], "git_node": "397886b23fc0dcf4cb0d9daf340029d40451df2c", "git_parents": ["e68853ccf82c0b412b805c27f5d94e0de242ffb7"], "node": "3a06b11b074d7b3c219b8e449a75809e0c948d0d", "parents": ["f528980adbd1758908f7e5d949bdc688b17625d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063424 - Rewrite the public NimbusEnrollments API in terms of distinct operations r=ralkhulaidi,nimbus-reviewers,emcminn\n\nPreviously the the NimbusEnrollments API had a single method for\nupdating enrollments: the aptly-named `updateEnrollment`. Calling it\ncould result in either an upsert, update, or delete to be triggered\ndepending on its arguments and the store state at the time of writing.\nThis was confusing because calling `updateEnrollment(e)` when trying to\nmodify metadata on an enrollment could actually result in an\nunenrollment (see the previous patch in this series).\n\nNow, the API has been split into three new methods:\n\n- `recordEnrollment()` for enrollments;\n- `recordUnenrollment()` for unenrollments; and\n- `deleteEnrollments()` for deletions (garabge collecting old\n  enrollments or calling `ExperimentStore._deleteForTests`).\n\nWe also now clone the enrollments into the pending write objects when\ncalling the above methods to eliminate races that occur when flushing\nthe `NimbusEnrollments` database and modifying enrollment state in the\n`ExperimentStore`. This change also revealed a test that was not\ncorrectly awaiting the result of `NimbusTestUtils.cleanupManager` and\nwas only passing because the `NimbusEnrollments` looked up enrollments\nin the store.\n\nThe `NimbusEnrollments` object now no longer requires a circular reference\nto its parent `ExperimentStore`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338116\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/Enrollments.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/ExperimentStore.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/SharedDataMap.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_Enrollments.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_ExperimentManager_enroll.js"], "git_node": "cc732b206a7d732ebe38866b84b34eb9527a053b", "git_parents": ["397886b23fc0dcf4cb0d9daf340029d40451df2c"], "node": "98f874f247bc6e38dff78e2581086b7298913c73", "parents": ["3a06b11b074d7b3c219b8e449a75809e0c948d0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063424 - Record enrollment statuses in the shared profiles database r=ralkhulaidi,nimbus-reviewers,jhirsch,emcminn\n\nWe now keep track of the history of all enrollment statuses for each\nrecipe.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338117\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/Enrollments.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/ExperimentManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/Telemetry.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/NimbusTestUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_Enrollments.js", "toolkit/profile/ProfilesDatastoreService.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d1973ebbab812c5f16b65b02a7615e13a9e7bde3", "git_parents": ["cc732b206a7d732ebe38866b84b34eb9527a053b"], "node": "9bcf9c2187525ea3064b08405fbc77260c9320a5", "parents": ["98f874f247bc6e38dff78e2581086b7298913c73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2063424 - Support submitting enrollment status change telemetry only r=ralkhulaidi,nimbus-reviewers,emcminn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338118\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml", "toolkit/components/nimbus/lib/Enrollments.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/nimbus/schemas/NimbusTelemetryFeature.schema.json", "toolkit/components/nimbus/test/unit/test_Enrollments.js"], "git_node": "3a5358f52405c4c77cee2e5a3e0cd758c6490e4a", "git_parents": ["d1973ebbab812c5f16b65b02a7615e13a9e7bde3"], "node": "6670040cf84a90b9e3961a0c578a45e39638d21e", "parents": ["9bcf9c2187525ea3064b08405fbc77260c9320a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emily McDonough \u003cemcdonough@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2068132 - Add Skrifa glyph variant function to fontations_glue and use it for FreeType fonts. r=jfkthame,layout-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338842\n", "files": ["gfx/fontations_glue/lib.rs", "gfx/thebes/gfxFT2FontBase.cpp"], "git_node": "156b8e2f46d40d9277a3cf8548325f9755794d5c", "git_parents": ["3a5358f52405c4c77cee2e5a3e0cd758c6490e4a"], "node": "4bb5ac684434ef003bbc8ce7f5bd146b981a94ba", "parents": ["6670040cf84a90b9e3961a0c578a45e39638d21e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmed Ashraf ElGendy \u003cahmedashrafelgendy25@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1377755 - Allow scrolling while eyedropper is open and update screenshot on scroll. r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nInstead of blocking scroll/wheel events (which could still be triggered via trackpads or scrollbars), allow natural scrolling and use a debounced update on scroll events to refresh the screenshot and keep sampled colors accurate.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336921\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser.toml", "devtools/client/inspector/test/highlighter/browser_inspector_highlighter-eyedropper-scroll.js", "devtools/server/actors/highlighters/css/highlighters.css", "devtools/server/actors/highlighters/eye-dropper.js"], "git_node": "092d490beea26cc5d33eadb9cf88316f57f338dd", "git_parents": ["156b8e2f46d40d9277a3cf8548325f9755794d5c"], "node": "2146211240be791fc6924c52ffbd84196108d9c2", "parents": ["4bb5ac684434ef003bbc8ce7f5bd146b981a94ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johan Lorenzo \u003cjlorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2069358 - part 4: Fetch install-firefox.sh from GitHub or hg by revision. r=releng-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,hneiva DONTBUILD\n\nThis change fixes the [failure seen on m-c](https://firefox-ci-tc.services.mozilla.com/tasks/UXvBhL-xRSKntags4R7Gvw/runs/1/logs/public/logs/live_backing.log#L57):\n\n```\n[task] + curl --fail --location --retry 5 --output /builds/worker/artifacts/install-firefox.sh https://hg.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/raw/ebeddb8734cd9a6052b50d3e9634d51b79efe57c/browser/installer/linux/script/install-firefox.sh\n[task] curl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 400\n```\n\nI'm going with an approach that supports both git and hg, which makes the task work on `try`\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339539\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-artifact/kind.yml"], "git_node": "378345a864a0264b0fd336a7a5b9cdc572eb8be8", "git_parents": ["092d490beea26cc5d33eadb9cf88316f57f338dd"], "node": "e5d024f3c4335aff6db92e7566eec830ea34796a", "parents": ["2146211240be791fc6924c52ffbd84196108d9c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sky Ning \u003csning@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2072656 - Measure the network data cost of Speculation Rules prefetch r=acreskey,sunil\n\nPrefetching trades data for latency and we have no field measure of the data\nside. speculation_rules.prefetch_transfer_size sums a prefetch record's\nnsIHttpChannel.transferSize, labelled used, unused or incomplete, recorded\nwhen the record is discarded since that is the first point that knows whether\na navigation ever came for it.\n\nZero-byte samples are recorded, so each label's sample count is also the\nnumber of records that ended with that outcome.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D327492\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/browser.toml", "dom/base/test/browser_prefetch_data_usage.js", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h", "dom/metrics.yaml", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp"], "git_node": "8c94629380d9394c3b4a15129741a8b4b0f08c17", "git_parents": ["378345a864a0264b0fd336a7a5b9cdc572eb8be8"], "node": "a46a1bae129f9a5fe0349d5835901f721782c3be", "parents": ["e5d024f3c4335aff6db92e7566eec830ea34796a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eitan Isaacson \u003ceitan@monotonous.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050939 - Remove invisible select subtree. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,Jamie,devtools-reviewers,morgan,ochameau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309162\n", "files": ["accessible/base/HTMLMarkupMap.inc", "accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/base/nsCoreUtils.cpp", "accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp", "accessible/generic/LocalAccessible.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLSelectAccessible.cpp", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_caching_value.js", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_obj_group.js", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_treeupdate_optgroup.js", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/doc_language.html", "accessible/tests/browser/name_and_description/browser_name_markup.js", "accessible/tests/browser/selectable/browser_test_select.js", "accessible/tests/browser/states/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/states/browser_test_select_visibility.js", "accessible/tests/browser/tree/browser_select.js", "accessible/tests/mochitest/attributes/test_obj_group.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/elm/test_HTMLSpec.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/events/test_coalescence.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/events/test_focus_selects.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/events/test_selection.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/name/markuprules.xml", "accessible/tests/mochitest/relations/test_general.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/states/test_selects.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/tree/test_select.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/treeupdate/test_optgroup.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/treeupdate/test_select.html", "devtools/server/tests/browser/browser_accessibility_keyboard_audit.js", "devtools/server/tests/browser/doc_accessibility_text_label_audit.html", "dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/html-aam/roles.html"], "git_node": "cef75e552196d52f3a413776691a2d6793a22c50", "git_parents": ["8c94629380d9394c3b4a15129741a8b4b0f08c17"], "node": "6a15dadfe9f7a39b2487cfb8a5eba78119ac9762", "parents": ["a46a1bae129f9a5fe0349d5835901f721782c3be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Max Inden \u003cmail@max-inden.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088678 - Add happy_eyeballs_dns_answer_spread_v2 labeled timing distribution r=kershaw,omansfeld,necko-reviewers\n\nRecords the DNS answer spread as a timing distribution with two labels,\nboth recorded once per run: until_first_attempt (same window as the\nexisting happy_eyeballs_dns_answer_spread) and until_end (all positive\nanswers of the run).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339303\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/happy_eyeballs_glue/src/metrics.rs", "netwerk/protocol/http/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "623d9bf00dbb67bf447690794f07bba806306b2c", "git_parents": ["cef75e552196d52f3a413776691a2d6793a22c50"], "node": "60db7be38cd9e054508b3ae5ad1e677c7670c029", "parents": ["6a15dadfe9f7a39b2487cfb8a5eba78119ac9762"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086864 - Pick image raster sizes with the reference frame origins WebRender snaps with. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nWebRender snaps an item with every enclosing reference frame's origin\ncomposed in, rounding the accumulated offset of snapping frames, but the\ninherited transform Gecko rounds an image's rect with to pick its raster size\nonly carried the frames' transforms. Under a fractional origin the size could\nbe a device pixel off the snapped rect, and when a transform moved from script\nit alternated between sizes, re-decoding the image and changing its shape.\n\nThe tests are Mozilla reftests because they rely on layout.css.devPixelsPerPx\nand layout.disable-pixel-alignment.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338620\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/StackingContextHelper.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/StackingContextHelper.h", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.h", "layout/painting/nsDisplayList.cpp", "layout/reftests/image/image-fractional-raster-1-ref.html", "layout/reftests/image/image-refframe-fractional-raster-1.html", "layout/reftests/image/image-refframe-nested-fractional-raster-1.html", "layout/reftests/image/image-svg-snapped-origin-raster-1.html", "layout/reftests/image/reftest.list"], "git_node": "f5d2ec1ecdeed17690889b9d73fcaebdb8e94bac", "git_parents": ["623d9bf00dbb67bf447690794f07bba806306b2c"], "node": "58f6f7d69f451717556fbbd130a6bc9143a91a73", "parents": ["60db7be38cd9e054508b3ae5ad1e677c7670c029"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089070 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to af81da7208a53c47e3ada8b17a4a172a25bd9d87 r=dmeehan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339641\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "a249b88d2231333634e709372ae1d8530fe75f4d", "git_parents": ["f5d2ec1ecdeed17690889b9d73fcaebdb8e94bac"], "node": "554a29f16471a35126b77f1a1827e828caea99c5", "parents": ["58f6f7d69f451717556fbbd130a6bc9143a91a73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084407 - Intern text runs in the display list builder r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe glyphs no longer travel with every paint. The key holds the unresolved\nFontInstanceKey and the run is resolved when the delta is applied; a run whose\nfont is unusable resolves to None and is skipped at prepare, where the scene\nbuilder used to drop the item. Every kind that casts a shadow now has a\ncaptured key, so shadow_copy_of_item goes. Because interning slots restart with\na new display list builder, a list from a fresh builder (e.g. a replaced\ncontent process) now re-interns its text runs under new uids and invalidates\nits tiles, as rectangles already did.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339299\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/dl_interner.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/intern.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/interned.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_debug.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interned_prims.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interning.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/invalidation.list", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/wrench.rs"], "git_node": "fb0840150efbebdd40f2f2fdcca57f7e3d4ed9f7", "git_parents": ["a249b88d2231333634e709372ae1d8530fe75f4d"], "node": "4c9389abae4d10565ae458025aa3f2940c3c48d9", "parents": ["554a29f16471a35126b77f1a1827e828caea99c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2081459 - Wait for onOrientationLock before changing the orientation in OrientationDelegateTest. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nlockPortrait and lockLandscape called orientationChanged right after calling lock(). The change event resolves\nthe pending lock promise, and when it ran before the lock task, the task treated its promise as superseded and\nnever locked the device or registered the fullscreen exit listener, so the next exitFullscreenAndWaitForUnlock\ntimed out waiting for onOrientationUnlock.\n\nlockPortrait and lockLandscape now share one helper, which registers the delegate before calling lock(), since\nevaluatePromiseJS can process the onOrientationLock call before a delegate registered after it is in place.\norientationLockUnlock had its own copy of lockLandscape and now uses it. orientationLock and\norientationUnlockByExitFullscreen compared the configuration orientation against ActivityInfo constants, which\nonly matched in portrait.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338980\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/OrientationDelegateTest.kt"], "git_node": "07209b8e07f42bbb4f2d2be61bcd6cd60fc6489a", "git_parents": ["fb0840150efbebdd40f2f2fdcca57f7e3d4ed9f7"], "node": "68b479cb0b9eaead586c2a560477298c93883d43", "parents": ["4c9389abae4d10565ae458025aa3f2940c3c48d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2050939 - Remove invisible select subtree. r=accessibility-platform-reviewers,Jamie,devtools-reviewers,morgan,ochameau\" for causing mochitests failures in browser_popupbutton.js.\n\nThis reverts commit cef75e552196d52f3a413776691a2d6793a22c50.\n", "files": ["accessible/base/HTMLMarkupMap.inc", "accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.cpp", "accessible/base/nsCoreUtils.cpp", "accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp", "accessible/generic/LocalAccessible.cpp", "accessible/html/HTMLSelectAccessible.cpp", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_caching_value.js", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_obj_group.js", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/browser_treeupdate_optgroup.js", "accessible/tests/browser/e10s/doc_language.html", "accessible/tests/browser/name_and_description/browser_name_markup.js", "accessible/tests/browser/selectable/browser_test_select.js", "accessible/tests/browser/states/browser.toml", "accessible/tests/browser/states/browser_test_select_visibility.js", "accessible/tests/browser/tree/browser_select.js", "accessible/tests/mochitest/attributes/test_obj_group.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/elm/test_HTMLSpec.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/events/test_coalescence.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/events/test_focus_selects.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/events/test_selection.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/name/markuprules.xml", "accessible/tests/mochitest/relations/test_general.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/states/test_selects.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/tree/test_select.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/treeupdate/test_optgroup.html", "accessible/tests/mochitest/treeupdate/test_select.html", "devtools/server/tests/browser/browser_accessibility_keyboard_audit.js", "devtools/server/tests/browser/doc_accessibility_text_label_audit.html", "dom/html/HTMLSelectElement.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/html-aam/roles.html"], "git_node": "2a78fc918dddfcdb766e44bc09b5f1565de1bf11", "git_parents": ["07209b8e07f42bbb4f2d2be61bcd6cd60fc6489a"], "node": "7b915cc2a405aae1ff81501b522dced528827fce", "parents": ["68b479cb0b9eaead586c2a560477298c93883d43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1753174 - Trickle 200 bytes in WebExecutorTest#readTimeout. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nGeckoInputStream.read only checks the timeout while no data is buffered, so a test thread delayed past the\nwhole 2.25 second trickle of 10 bytes read the complete body without timing out.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338633\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/WebExecutorTest.kt"], "git_node": "fb509cae3f4deee10a8f0dff373c65ba2c24c6df", "git_parents": ["2a78fc918dddfcdb766e44bc09b5f1565de1bf11"], "node": "ff373912ff3ae4560ae70b400ddb5fdfe4eb6b18", "parents": ["7b915cc2a405aae1ff81501b522dced528827fce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086666 - Remove version 159 train-hop tile_id strips from newtab and newtab-content ping sanitizers. r=Dre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337684\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/NewTabContentPing.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_NewTabContentPing.js"], "git_node": "4e8b3009c3de2b93765a3c793bf638ed48276699", "git_parents": ["fb509cae3f4deee10a8f0dff373c65ba2c24c6df"], "node": "004d0be0f353079b149731f39cb3d189f36b9cf2", "parents": ["ff373912ff3ae4560ae70b400ddb5fdfe4eb6b18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086669 - Remove the section_position backward-compat guard from NewTabContentPing.sanitizeEventData. r=ini\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337680\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/NewTabContentPing.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "a3aa25f5eb41834d48ffdf7191a883671483a17f", "git_parents": ["4e8b3009c3de2b93765a3c793bf638ed48276699"], "node": "e16b1ac1423716a034b55b67ff781926b16084db", "parents": ["004d0be0f353079b149731f39cb3d189f36b9cf2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086521 - Only run pdfpaint on PDFs marked for Talos. r=perftest-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau,sparky\n\nRun all of them in a single task, 15 times each, instead of in 10 chunks\nof 100.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337625\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/other.py", "taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/fetch-talos-pdfs.py", "testing/perfdocs/generated/talos.md", "testing/talos/perfdocs/config.yml", "testing/talos/talos/config.py", "testing/talos/talos/test.py", "testing/talos/talos/unittests/conftest.py", "testing/talos/talos/unittests/test_config.py"], "git_node": "c7a90862386c40fe65f762abea0cbd7710061129", "git_parents": ["a3aa25f5eb41834d48ffdf7191a883671483a17f"], "node": "39fe05ddab7552ec04c224bb7460a2b8dbd55b94", "parents": ["e16b1ac1423716a034b55b67ff781926b16084db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2086521 - Time PDF.js first-page rendering in worker and main-thread pdfpaint tests. r=perftest-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,sparky,jcristau\n\nMeasure PDFPageProxy.render after document loading and renderer worker\ninitialization, excluding viewer startup. Add main-thread suites with canvas\nacceleration enabled or disabled, and drop the webrender-sw variant, which\nonly disabled canvas acceleration.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D337731\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/test/talos.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/test-sets.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/talos.md", "testing/talos/mach_commands.py", "testing/talos/perfdocs/config.yml", "testing/talos/talos.json", "testing/talos/talos/config.py", "testing/talos/talos/pageloader/chrome/lh_pdfpaint.js", "testing/talos/talos/pageloader/chrome/pageloader.js", "testing/talos/talos/test.py", "testing/talos/talos/tests/pdfpaint/empty.pdf"], "git_node": "866b4fe83b543186a064b89d19135978643fbd5c", "git_parents": ["c7a90862386c40fe65f762abea0cbd7710061129"], "node": "bf1b8c47c71bc95807bb741f01f6523f59e905db", "parents": ["39fe05ddab7552ec04c224bb7460a2b8dbd55b94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087899 - Install the gtest libxul import library to dist/lib/gtest instead of dist/lib r=RyanVM\n\ntoolkit/library/gtest builds a second DLL named \"xul\" (xul-gtest). On Windows, the recursive make backend installs every installed shared library's import library to `$(DIST)/lib$(DIST_SUBDIR:%=/%)`. Because the gtest directory set `FINAL_TARGET` directly and not `DIST_SUBDIR`, both toolkit/library/build and toolkit/library/gtest installed `xul.lib` to `dist/lib/xul.lib`. With `--enable-gtest-in-build`, both run in the same tier, so their nsinstall calls race (\"cannot make symbolic link .../dist/lib/xul.lib: File exists\"). Even without the race, the gtest import library could overwrite the real libxul one.\n\nSetting `DIST_SUBDIR = \"gtest\"` keeps FINAL_TARGET at `dist/bin/gtest` (its default value then) and moves the gtest import library to `dist/lib/gtest/xul.lib`. Nothing uses the gtest xul.lib from dist/lib.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339639\n", "files": ["toolkit/library/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "dec51785338974372c28c9cd3245d67b55d24e0f", "git_parents": ["866b4fe83b543186a064b89d19135978643fbd5c"], "node": "3cacc429769e074f73f8c5057ffae659e5dec196", "parents": ["bf1b8c47c71bc95807bb741f01f6523f59e905db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Rishel \u003cnrishel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088734 - Remove remaining references to Canvas worker threads. r=lsalzman,perftest-reviewers,android-reviewers,nalexander,aglavic\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339370\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/performance-new/prefs-presets.sys.mjs", "gfx/ipc/CanvasRenderThread.cpp", "gfx/ipc/CanvasRenderThread.h", "gfx/layers/d3d11/TextureD3D11.cpp", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/perf/ProfilerUtils.kt", "testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.md", "testing/perfdocs/generated/talos.md", "testing/raptor/raptor/tests/benchmarks/motionmark-1-3-desktop.toml", "testing/raptor/raptor/tests/benchmarks/motionmark-1-3-mobile.toml", "testing/talos/talos/test.py", "xpcom/threads/nsThreadUtils.h"], "git_node": "6be9060d005fc8ff1e8c6d97f7c187d398cdf0cf", "git_parents": ["dec51785338974372c28c9cd3245d67b55d24e0f"], "node": "42c7fc071da85ee8fe413d5270ec4b184bdc4f8e", "parents": ["3cacc429769e074f73f8c5057ffae659e5dec196"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Corentin Bect \u003ccbect@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2087435 - Remove lazyMonitored wrapper function r=android-reviewers,tcampbell\n\n`lazyMonitored` was only a thin wrapper around `lazy`. Its performance monitoring logic was removed a long time ago (2021) and it was only kept because putting it back on every component would not be trivial, but this is no longer true.\n\nThis replaces every use with `lazy`, deletes the wrapper and removes the `MozillaUseLazyMonitored` detekt rule, its tests and the config entry in `detekt.yml`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339194\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Ads.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Analytics.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/BackgroundServices.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Core.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/FxSuggest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/IntentProcessors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/NimbusComponents.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/PerformanceComponent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Push.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Services.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/UseCases.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/llm/Llm.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/perf/LazyMonitored.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/config/detekt.yml", "mobile/android/fenix/mozilla-detekt-rules/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/detektrules/CustomRulesetProvider.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/mozilla-detekt-rules/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/detektrules/perf/MozillaUseLazyMonitored.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/mozilla-detekt-rules/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/detektrules/perf/MozillaUseLazyMonitoredTest.kt"], "git_node": "4ea9beba1aaad07a59f99d7da36d049fb07bcc02", "git_parents": ["6be9060d005fc8ff1e8c6d97f7c187d398cdf0cf"], "node": "c54e373cdd778f61e81b53b18e17fbc81980be51", "parents": ["42c7fc071da85ee8fe413d5270ec4b184bdc4f8e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089056 - Update the private homepage and homepage search bar layout to match the latest designs r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nDesigns:\n- https://www.figma.com/design/hBfKusHhCaTfERowKh1yYP/HNT-Handoff?node-id=3001-27708&m=dev\n\nChanges:\n- Private mode icon is 40dp and sits where the logo is in normal mode\n- Private browsing description text is left-aligned, uses the Headline 7 and Body 2 type styles, and the learn more link uses onSurfaceVariant\n- Spacing between the private mode icon, the search bar and the description matches the designs\n- The homepage search bar and the private browsing description are capped at containerMaxWidth and centered on wider screens, such as landscape and tablets\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339634\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/ui/Homepage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/ui/HomepageHeader.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/ui/MiddleSearchHomepage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/ui/PrivateBrowsingDescription.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/ui/SearchBar.kt"], "git_node": "cd98901f47d7659f0ce2e201f4a378b75fe12c0d", "git_parents": ["4ea9beba1aaad07a59f99d7da36d049fb07bcc02"], "node": "2cd04e41de3e04f0d39c985116e3e149a6d14d9e", "parents": ["c54e373cdd778f61e81b53b18e17fbc81980be51"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Markus Stange \u003cmstange.moz@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089083 - Look through the interpreter entry trampoline frame in branchIfNotActivationEntryFrame. r=jandem\n\nWhen running with emitInterpreterEntryTrampoline,\nMacroAssembler::branchIfNotActivationEntryFrame now adds some extra\ncode which also handles the \"I am called by my interpreter trampoline\"\ncase. This makes the CanSkipAwait optimization work in the presence\nof interpreter trampolines. Before this patch, a generator that resumes\ninto the Baseline Interpreter through its per-script entry trampoline\nwas never able to skip its awaits because the code generated by\nbranchIfNotActivationEntryFrame would always see the interpreter frame\nand immediately say no.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339666\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/onEnterFrame-async-tryskipawait-interpreter-entry.js", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler-inl.h"], "git_node": "3178b9120f34e0c76b94fade10472bf1bf3e27ef", "git_parents": ["cd98901f47d7659f0ce2e201f4a378b75fe12c0d"], "node": "4f5d090ff97086a9902065b213a58e70bf982e09", "parents": ["2cd04e41de3e04f0d39c985116e3e149a6d14d9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089044 - Return nsISupports* from MediaError::GetParentObject r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339631\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediaelement/MediaError.cpp", "dom/media/mediaelement/MediaError.h"], "git_node": "c04ae7404d988a236bbebfbfdcf7f4da665c219b", "git_parents": ["3178b9120f34e0c76b94fade10472bf1bf3e27ef"], "node": "bb56d21a474725c60656646568a63678ab5e6cae", "parents": ["4f5d090ff97086a9902065b213a58e70bf982e09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rebecca King \u003crking@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088515 - VPN panel fails to update content when switching tabs via keyboard shortcut - r=ip-protection-reviewers,mcleinman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339311\n", "files": ["browser/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionPanel.sys.mjs", "browser/components/ipprotection/tests/browser/browser_ipprotection_content_site_rules.js"], "git_node": "e9e17ff9a7230c0c46a5ad7a4c76bb8408c81df5", "git_parents": ["c04ae7404d988a236bbebfbfdcf7f4da665c219b"], "node": "4245db78b73c0870172041d6a654d10f75876f6c", "parents": ["bb56d21a474725c60656646568a63678ab5e6cae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089092 - Comment on why some Tabbrowser members are static, per window or `this`-free. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339676\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/Tabbrowser.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "5a54d5e0fe9040782e1f0c35cc8de3d18068befc", "git_parents": ["e9e17ff9a7230c0c46a5ad7a4c76bb8408c81df5"], "node": "d8c6ef2852bedece2ac1c0f85647757bf56c046e", "parents": ["4245db78b73c0870172041d6a654d10f75876f6c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "KS \u003ckshampur@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2084762 - Lower the nav-bench alert threshold to 2% on desktop. r=perftest-reviewers,aglavic\n\nRecently nav-bench desktop was bumped to tier 2 with alerting enabled as\nwell. This patch drops the alert_threshold from 5% -\u003e 2% to better catch\nsmaller regressions/improvements.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339640\n", "files": ["testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.md", "testing/raptor/raptor/tests/nav-bench/browsertime-nav-bench.toml"], "git_node": "21effcba9d759812d99c325aba35452aaeb05db8", "git_parents": ["5a54d5e0fe9040782e1f0c35cc8de3d18068befc"], "node": "0df4cb24a7b88ee72ad05c67bd683566b3d0e342", "parents": ["d8c6ef2852bedece2ac1c0f85647757bf56c046e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089074 - Update freetype2 to c4a3c188e82bc5b457390a87630ac782316421a1 r=jfkthame\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339647\n", "files": ["modules/freetype2/include/freetype/internal/ftobjs.h", "modules/freetype2/moz.yaml", "modules/freetype2/src/autofit/ft-hb.c", "modules/freetype2/src/base/ftobjs.c", "modules/freetype2/src/cache/ftccache.h", "modules/freetype2/src/cache/ftcmanag.c", "modules/freetype2/src/truetype/ttvarc.c"], "git_node": "31fb582ea4deb9f9ced2fd7baec9e547b5a85652", "git_parents": ["21effcba9d759812d99c325aba35452aaeb05db8"], "node": "6189dbff2dc02b11fcd445ccada5df1e6f04e193", "parents": ["0df4cb24a7b88ee72ad05c67bd683566b3d0e342"], "tags": []}, {"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083628 - Part 1: Make EMEDecryptor's decoder const. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D338301\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/agnostic/eme/EMEDecoderModule.cpp"], 