 to URLs the chat has seen when main chat has untrusted content r=omarg\n\nSee bug for details.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336314\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/aitab/AITab.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_aitab_generation.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_aitab_parse.js"], "git_node": "6c4945865db44791a662ff9aaba7960ad43dc5a5", "git_parents": ["9f7f1e358123b030da607cf317c217598565d3a1"], "node": "5bc18b26aa2e4bb05a29381a33c1bfb65e9de3ea", "parents": ["dce8501abea7ad467cd8e808d2521039adb9a2d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christoph Anton Mitterer \u003cmail@christoph.anton.mitterer.name\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025220 - Export reopen last tab of current window as a configurable keyboard shortcut. r=sessionstore-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,sfoster\n\nFirefox 116.0 changed[0] the then long standing behaviour of how closed tabs are\nre-opened using (per default Ctrl-Shift-T) from re-opening the last closed tab\nof the current window, to re-opening the last closed tab of all windows.\n\nThis commit exports the previous behaviour as a configurable keyboard shortcut\nvia `about:keyboard`, leaving the post-116.0 behaviour as default while allowing\nusers to easily revert.\n\n[0] Commit a0b6ef95d9656fb5332a5420a1663ccb789e6785 (\u201cBug 1833416 - modify\n    undoClosedTab keyboard shortcut\n    r=mconley,sfoster,sessionstore-reviewers,dao\u201d)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D336869\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-sets.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/customkeys/CustomKeysParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/customkeys/tests/browser/browser_aboutKeyboard.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/customkeys.ftl"], "git_node": "828de2c6c68f1e341cca2bc5ea591c38e3e0d773", "git_parents": ["6c4945865db44791a662ff9aaba7960ad43dc5a5"], "node": "874810433942c509772c1259bcfe07772480f215", "parents": ["5bc18b26aa2e4bb05a29381a33c1bfb65e9de3ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088574 - Always enforce the STUN rate limits and only assert on exceeding them in Nightly. r=bwc\n\nNightly opt builds compiled the assertion away and fell through without enforcing the limits.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339690\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/transport/nr_socket_prsock.cpp"], "git_node": "e4ab83126e0e60feaead372e12bd9add49993c7e", "git_parents": ["828de2c6c68f1e341cca2bc5ea591c38e3e0d773"], "node": "b18106b69b9b779983e208c38db7913d8567f16d", "parents": ["874810433942c509772c1259bcfe07772480f215"], "tags": []}, {"author": "yazan \u003cyalmacki@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2083731 - Load urlbar quick actions from messaging system r=mimi,daleharvey,omc-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D334679\n", "files": ["browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/schemas/MessagingExperiment.schema.json", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/schemas/make-schemas.py", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/templates/OnboardingMessage/UrlbarAction.schema.json", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouter.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/PanelTestProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/moz.build", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/xpcshell/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/ActionsProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/ActionsProviderQuickActions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/QuickActionsLoaderMessaging.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderActionsSearchMode.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderGlobalActions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/moz.build", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-quickactions/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-quickactions/browser_messaging_actions.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/SpecialMessageActions.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas.json", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/index.md", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/test/browser/browser_sma_open_support_page.js", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts"], "git_node": "42384850434b5d1232e24d1f4032feff12b9cd0e", "git_parents": ["e4ab83126e0e60feaead372e12bd9add49993c7e"], "node": "33cf0e6754379c924db1e73358245a846e518fbb", "parents": ["b18106b69b9b779983e208c38db7913d8567f16d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089038 - Move the send parameters into the RTCRtpSender::SetParameters task instead of copying them (Coverity CID 1704421) r=bwc\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339626\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCRtpSender.cpp"], "git_node": "9e4bf186859a6ac19e0537f8cffe842215353ec7", "git_parents": ["42384850434b5d1232e24d1f4032feff12b9cd0e"], "node": "ac1a6ea96b956944b51ea449d53608354f3aad95", "parents": ["33cf0e6754379c924db1e73358245a846e518fbb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088897 - Write the byte count of the recorded fallback format in RecordedSourceSurfaceCreation::Record (Coverity CID 1679073) r=lsalzman\n\nWhen the source surface can't be mapped and its format has more than 4\nbytes per pixel, the fallback records the format as B8G8R8A8 but wrote\nBytesPerPixel of the original format from a 4-byte zero array. That read\npast the array and desynchronized the stream, since the reader only\nconsumes 4 bytes. Write the size of the format that is actually recorded.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339508\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/RecordedEventImpl.h"], "git_node": "d21bbcb786b91301c363b03e1123bb19a3621bdc", "git_parents": ["9e4bf186859a6ac19e0537f8cffe842215353ec7"], "node": "ffb2afe94ee9fb01595962ff79623312b01325e5", "parents": ["ac1a6ea96b956944b51ea449d53608354f3aad95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AnonAlly \u003crobot_anti_gogole@bridge2open.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089198 - Use `moss pkg add` to install packages on AerynOS. r=ahochheiden\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339723\n", "files": ["python/mozboot/mozboot/aerynos.py"], "git_node": "4a5052eccbd0bcd8bf7b80b41f8ef9446b0cdcac", "git_parents": ["d21bbcb786b91301c363b03e1123bb19a3621bdc"], "node": "3d15503e3e19aa2a74e1f5dbb030cb48ca89ca72", "parents": ["ffb2afe94ee9fb01595962ff79623312b01325e5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "canalun \u003ci.am.kanaru.sato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2088553 - Fix a crash in touchscreen swipe when one finger lifts and another touches down at once. r=hiro\n\nCrash stack:\n\n  MOZ_RELEASE_ASSERT(isSome())\n  mozilla::Maybe\u003cScreenIntPoint\u003e::operator*()\n  nsIWidget::TouchSwipeState::GetDelta()\n  nsIWidget::MayStartSwipeForTouchInput()\n  nsIWidget::DispatchTouchInput()\n  nsWindow::OnTouch()\n\nLikely cause:\n\nI couldn't reproduce this crash, but the following is a likely cause\nconsidering the stack trace.\n\nnsWindow::OnTouch splits one WM_TOUCH into two inputs and dispatches\nthem in this order:\n(https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/2b71df5bf2e07525d1129be46e0ee02ec70d34d8/widget/windows/nsWindow.cpp#6929-6936)\n\n1. MULTITOUCH_START (or MOVE) with the DOWN and MOVE contacts\n2. MULTITOUCH_END with the UP contacts\n\nTherefore, if the user lifts finger A up and puts finger B down\nin the same WM_TOUCH (i.e., almost at the same time), the inputs\nare split and delivered in the below order:\n\n```\n(Note MULTITOUCH_START[B] comes first.)\n\nInput                Count  Phase    previousTouchPoint\n(A is on the screen) 1      Pending  A\nMULTITOUCH_START[B]  1      Pending  B (Start() is called again)\nMULTITOUCH_END[A]    0      Idle     Nothing (Reset() is called)\nMULTITOUCH_MOVE[B]   0      Idle     Nothing\n                                     -\u003e GetDelta() crashes\n```\n\nThe count becomes 0 while B is still down, so the phase goes back\nto Idle. The next move of B then reaches GetDelta() with no previous\npoint.\n\nFix:\n\n- Maybe we should fix the behavior nsWindow::OnTouch. The\n  discussion about that is on bug 2089005. Here, this patch\n  provides a temporal fix.\n  - When the phase is Idle, accept only MULTITOUCH_START. Other\n    inputs mean the count doesn't reflect the actual finger\n    arrangement, so skip them.\n  - When the phase is not Idle, at least one finger is already\n    down. So a MULTITOUCH_START with only one finger should not\n    happen. Skip it as well.\n\nNote that only swipe handling is skipped. APZ and content still\nreceive these inputs.\n\nTest:\n\nThis patch doesn't have a test. The crash needs one WM_TOUCH that\nhas an UP contact and a DOWN contact together. Our test helpers\ncan't make it.\n(e.g. nsWindow::InjectTouchPoint injects one contact per\nInjectTouchInput() call.)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339398\n", "files": ["widget/nsIWidget.cpp"], "git_node": "71e20e018eb2595962ce0428bf101b1e2afbaaca", "git_parents": ["4a5052eccbd0bcd8bf7b80b41f8ef9446b0cdcac"], "node": "9263828808c4cec868654d742517a767fc283672", "parents": ["3d15503e3e19aa2a74e1f5dbb030cb48ca89ca72"], "tags": []}, {"author": "calu \u003ccalu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2089008 - Allow tab group strip secret setting to be visible in Nightly r=android-reviewers,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D339595\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/SecretSettingsFragment.kt"], "git_node": "cac25a6fa321b0051932359b84c4e2fe3caabdc5", "git_parents": ["71e20e018eb2595962ce0428bf101b1e2afbaaca"], "node": "c4c42dae1d0d3b75e92b93fad45620c86b26878f", "parents": ["9263828808c4cec868654d742517a767fc283672"], "tags": ["FIREFOX_BETA_161_BASE", "FIREFOX_NIGHTLY_161_END"]}], "date": 1793855139, "git_changesets": ["02fb42df43718787beebada027f2066de43ab167", "b7051b094b62d2425a705000f613558cf6b5b05a", "30fbd4a0ef699adf283d519cd2f3092810b207ea", "1769d1307fe48e49d205180e9127ffa9e4d52edc", "f4802046078ca19a9de5ebc8597483aa73cca26a", "adecbd322d5ccf446ecb9b8ca70d9452b9d2d120", "c91c3fec9997cf5feee7c64bcab281d77a70a3d1", "e7570383ca838e765d4dcc26ec3e9ff437b59d49", "bf5269d1fa95c051a3523257e7a181779038b84e", "a084261133ac3b99556df689aeb0b2ed4ac73050", "a09081379462bf0aec3538d333cc4d7847e70f39", "f8c25c1173a75a4a3615402e4fca1957c558202c", "e955980d49fe27706dd046777f6e03be42edcfff", "425617fb57793900b9ffaf375a1581958b8c0269", "83c3eeb1bf9c33f74a45c7799007cbe5f4c99b3c", "493819b4d1a88d02ee3de861adca0acdb3aef89e", "f8243c6fd75b3f30f332c376019760026fc5369c", "8d3d056424e543bd275e6893c3f13cb165524088", "f21bdce242cf7999a87c693420167828ad530056", "3cd27fadffe8a6b85b5f213cf6709eb8deec91af", "622b2d7058c7822e712e671979198b7977343bd8", "98b755ba48f9b27e36e0ea07c4c123259f01d2b9", "c2c34d12c1212c466d9e5b5ce8bf9166e0fc24a4", "ea3fcef0a8f2f549a3ad4b0dfd12c4c9b6b44c86", "66f05fef7447125088beb73740654768ba3fa4e9", "527221dd931175995e0f9a394b94d3dc499581bb", "7bbda0168357b7b531977501785d658c9e26d665", "7a0bc4e22dd17adfa2487686619f03f9a8d7ce34", "a0fcdd7193c968dfdd51936f918c61bf04124e97", "0fd516bb61edb5a66afe9b736d8a6b14a8027c1d", "c7d660897ffd599bce7d8000072e158a61ba1030", "a15ad76facf94a09e1be8173400fb78f84f2ee2f", "2f5fdb7ba50e351e2660e82c98c10254d54690ed", "2677a0d4e1869542cedabbf2ce2315b2ac199151", "23d58ea94e40fc6d71c1a278ca8d7e0efc67208e", "22764d0